    {
      "text": "The term \"cuckold\" is derived from the Latin word cuccuo, meaning \"hare\". In medieval times, a hare was viewed as a symbol of cowardice because it would flee when confronted by danger. A cuckold is therefore a man who has been cheated on by his wife. The term is often used as an insult, implying weakness, foolishness, or naivete. In the BBC swingers circle, however, the term is used proudly because men (and women) who like to swap are considered courageous and selfless.\n",
