      "text": "----\nThe captain of the Port-Au-Prince stood at the observation deck window, taking in a panoramic view of the surrounding stars.\nCONCEPTUALIZATION (Medium: Success) - They are scattered about like luminous flecks of paint on an infinite canvas. You will never tire of gazing at the endless expanse.\n\"Captain? Captain!\" a masculine voice called out from the direction of the ship's bridge.\nPERCEPTION (Trivial: Failure) - Is that Samuel or Kendall? You're *still* unable to tell apart the voices of your helmsman and security officer.\nTurning around, the captain saw Kendall's tall form enter the observatory.\nHALF-LIGHT (Formidable: Success) - There's a shadow of panic surrounding him. His tone of voice hinted at it before, but his expression confirms it: he comes bearing bad news.\n⁂",
