keys.4\",\"entries.67.keys.5\",\"entries.67.keys.6\",\"entries.67.keys.7\",\"entries.67.keys.8\",\"entries.67.keys.9\",\"entries.67.keys.10\",\"entries.67.keys.11\",\"entries.67.keys.12\",\"entries.67.keys.13\",\"entries.67.keys.14\",\"entries.67.keys.15\",\"entries.67.keys.16\",\"entries.67.keys.17\",\"entries.67.keys.18\",\"entries.67.keys.19\",\"entries.67.keys.20\",\"entries.67.keys.21\",\"entries.67.name\",\"entries.67.order\",\"entries.67.position\",\"entries.67.priority\",\"entries.67.probability\",\"entries.67.selective\",\"entries.67.selectiveLogic\",\"entries.67.uid\",\"entries.67.useProbability\",\"entries.68.addMemo\",\"entries.68.case_sensitive\",\"entries.68.characterFilter\",\"entries.68.comment\",\"entries.68.constant\",\"entries.68.content\",\"entries.68.depth\",\"entries.68.disable\",\"entries.68.displayIndex\",\"entries.68.enabled\",\"entries.68.excludeRecursion\",\"entries.68.extensions.addMemo\",\"entries.68.extensions.characterFilter\",\"entries.68.extensions.depth\",\"entries.68.extensions.displayIndex\",\"entries.68.extensions.excludeRecursion\",\"entries.68.extensions.useProbability\",\"entries.68.extensions.weight\",\"entries.68.id\",\"entries.68.insertion_order\",\"entries.68.key.0\",\"entries.68.key.1\",\"entries.68.key.2\",\"entries.68.key.3\",\"entries.68.key.4\",\"entries.68.key.5\",\"entries.68.key.6\",\"entries.68.keys.0\",\"entries.68.keys.1\",\"entries.68.keys.2\",\"entries.68.keys.3\",\"entries.68.keys.4\",\"entries.68.keys.5\",\"entries.68.keys.6\",\"entries.68.name\",\"entries.68.order\",\"entries.68.position\",\"entries.68.priority\",\"entries.68.probability\",\"entries.68.selective\",\"entries.68.selectiveLogic\",\"entries.68.uid\",\"entries.68.useProbability\",\"is_creation\",\"name\",\"recursive_scanning\",\"scan_depth\",\"token_budget\"\n\"\",true,false,,\"Human Warrior Character Sheet (neutral good, level 1)\",false,\"<character_sheet_warrior>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nFlame Tongue Greatsword (2d6 slashing + 2d6 fire damage on command)\nAdamantine armor (critical hits against you become regular hits)\nRing of Protection +1 AC\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\nRace: Human \n\nClass: Fighter\n\nBackground: Soldier\n\nAlignment: Neutral Good\n\nStarting Attributes:[\nStrength: 16 (+3)\nDexterity: 12 (+1)\nConstitution: 14 (+2)\nIntelligence: 8 (-1)\nWisdom: 10 (+0)\nCharisma: 10 (+0)]\n\nSkills: Athletics, Intimidation\n\nEquipment:[\nGreatsword\nScale mail armor (14 AC)\nBackpack\nExplorer's pack\n50 gold pieces]\n\nRace: Variant Human: +1 to all attributes\nClass: Fighter: Fighting Style (Great Weapon Fighting), Second Wind, Action Surge (1/rest)\nBackground: Military Rank (Private)\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 12\nArmor Class: 15 (Scale mail +1 from dexterity)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks: Greatsword: 2d6 slashing damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\n  - Great Weapon Fighting: When you roll a 1 or 2 on a damage die for an attack you make with a melee weapon that you are wielding with two hands, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll, even if the new roll is a 1 or a 2. The weapon must have the two-handed or versatile property for you to gain this benefit.\n  - Second Wind (1/rest): You have a limited well of stamina that you can draw on to protect yourself from harm. On your turn, you can use a bonus action to regain hit points equal to 1d10 + your fighter level.\n  - Action Surge (1/rest): On your turn, you can take one additional action on top of your regular action and a possible bonus action.]\n</character_sheet_warrior>\n\",4,false,0,true,false,true,,4,0,false,true,10,1,90,\"character_sheet_warrior\",\"character_sheet_warrior\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,1,true,true,false,,\"Dwarven Cleric Character Sheet (lawful good, level 1)\",false,\"<character_sheet_cleric>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nRace: Hill Dwarf\n\nClass: Cleric\n\nBackground: Acolyte\n\nAlignment: Lawful Good\n\n\nStarting Attributes:[\nStrength: 14 (+2)\nDexterity: 10 (+0)\nConstitution: 16 (+3)\nIntelligence: 8 (-1)\nWisdom: 16 (+3)\nCharisma: 10 (+0)]\n\nSkills: Medicine, Religion\n\nEquipment:[\nMace\nScale Mail\nShield\nHoly Symbol\nPriest's Pack\nHealer's Kit\n50 gold pieces]\n\nFeatures and Traits:\n\nRace: Hill Dwarf: +2 Constitution, +1 Wisdom, Dwarven Resilience, Dwarven Combat Training, Stonecunning\nClass: Cleric: Spellcasting, Divine Domain\nBackground: Acolyte: Shelter of the Faithful, Feature: Healer's Kit\n\nSpellcasting:\nCantrips:[\nLight: Creates a bright light in a 20-foot radius, like a torch.\n\nSacred Flame: Summons radiant energy to target a creature, causing it to take radiant damage.\nDamage: 1d8 radiant damage]\n\nSpell slots: \nTwo first level\n\n1st Level Spells:[\nCure Wounds: Heals a creature you touch, restoring hit points.\nHealing: 1d8 + spellcasting ability modifier\nIncreased Level Healing: 1d8 per level\nUsage: The spell slots refresh after a long rest.\n\nGuiding Bolt: A flash of light streaks toward a creature within range, illuminating the target and making it easier for your allies to hit.\nFrequency: Usable at will.\nDamage: 4d6 radiant damage\nIncreased Level Damage: 1d6 per level\nUsage: The spell slots refresh after a long rest.\n]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 11\nArmor Class: 18 (Scale Mail + Shield)\nSpeed: 25 ft.\nAttacks:\nMace: 1d6 bludgeoning damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nDivine Domain: \nFrequency: Passive ability, always active. \nMechanics: The cleric has chosen the Life Domain, granting mastery over the healing arts. This choice provides them with enhanced healing abilities, allowing them to channel the divine energy of their deity to mend wounds and restore vitality to allies.\n\nChannel Divinity: \nFrequency: Once per short or long rest. \nMechanics: The cleric can use Channel Divinity to restore vitality to a number of injured creatures within 30 feet, distributing a pool of hit points among them as they see fit, up to half of their hit point maximums. This potent ability allows them to bolster their companions' resilience in battle, ensuring they can continue to fight on.]\n\n</character_sheet_cleric>\",4,false,1,true,false,true,,4,1,false,true,10,2,90,\"character_sheet_cleric\",\"character_sheet_cleric\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,2,true,true,false,,\"Gnome Rogue Character Sheet (chaotic good, level 1)\",false,\"<character_sheet_rogue>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\nRace: Gnome\n\nClass: Rogue\n\nBackground: Urchin\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Good\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 10 (+0)\nDexterity: 16 (+3)\nConstitution: 12 (+1)\nIntelligence: 14 (+2)\nWisdom: 10 (+0)\nCharisma: 8 (-1)]\n\nSkills: Stealth, Sleight of Hand\n\nEquipment:[\nRapier\nShortbow with 20 arrows\nBurglar's Pack\nThieves' Tools\nLeather armor\n50 gold pieces]\n\nFeatures and Traits:\nRace: Gnome: +2 Intelligence, Darkvision, Gnome Cunning\nClass: Rogue: Expertise (Stealth, Sleight of Hand), Sneak Attack\nBackground: Urchin: City Secrets, Sleight of Hand proficiency\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 8\nArmor Class: 13 (Leather Armor)\nSpeed: 25 ft.\nAttacks:\nRapier: 1d8 piercing damage\nShortbow: 1d6 piercing damage (range 80/320)]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nEvasive Footwork:\nFrequency: Once per short rest.\nMechanics: Use a bonus action to move up to your speed without provoking opportunity attacks.\n\nQuick Reflexes:\nFrequency: Passive ability, always active.\nMechanics: Gain a +2 bonus to initiative rolls.]\n</character_sheet_rogue>\",4,false,2,true,false,true,,4,2,false,true,10,3,90,\"character_sheet_rogue\",\"character_sheet_rogue\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,3,true,true,false,,\"Tiefling Sorcerer Character Sheet (chaotic evil, level 1)\",false,\"<character_sheet_sorcerer>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nRace: Tiefling\n\nClass: Sorcerer\n\nBackground: Charlatan\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Evil\n\n\nStarting Attributes:\n\nStrength: 10 (+0)\nDexterity: 14 (+2)\nConstitution: 12 (+1)\nIntelligence: 8 (-1)\nWisdom: 10 (+0)\nCharisma: 16 (+3)\nSkills: Deception, Sleight of Hand\n\nEquipment:[\nDagger\nComponent Pouch\nDisguise Kit\nThieves' Tools\nFine clothes\n50 gold pieces]\n\nFeatures and Traits:\n\nRace: Tiefling: +2 Charisma, +1 Intelligence, Darkvision, Hellish Resistance, Infernal Legacy (Thaumaturgy cantrip)\nClass: Sorcerer: Spellcasting, Sorcerous Origin\nBackground: Charlatan: False Identity, Forgery Kit\n\nSpellcasting:\nCantrips:[\nThaumaturgy:\nFrequency: At will.\nMechanics: You manifest a minor wonder, a sign of supernatural power, within range. You can create one of the following magical effects: your voice booms up to three times as loud as normal for one minute, you cause flames to flicker, brighten, dim, or change color for one minute, you cause harmless tremors in the ground for one minute, you create an instantaneous sound, or you open or close a door or window.\n\nFire Bolt:\nFrequency: At will.\nMechanics: You hurl a mote of fire at a creature or object within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 1d10 fire damage. The spell's damage increases as you reach higher levels.\n\nPrestidigitation:\nFrequency: At will.\nMechanics: You create one of the following magical effects: create a harmless sensory effect (visual, auditory, olfactory, or tactile), light or snuff out a small flame, clean or soil an object no larger than 1 cubic foot, chill, warm, or flavor up to 1 cubic foot of nonliving material, or create a small trinket or illusionary image that fits in your hand and lasts until the end of your next turn.]\n\nSpell slots: \nTwo first level\n\n1st Level Spells:[\nMage Armor:\nFrequency: Once per round.\nMechanics: This spell grants the target a protective magical force, providing a base Armor Class of 13 + Dexterity modifier for 8 hours. The spell doesn't require concentration.\n\nSpell: Burning Hands\nFrequency: Once per round.\nMechanics: You unleash a 15-foot cone of fire from your fingertips. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity saving throw. A target takes 3d6 fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\nIncreased Level Damage: 1d6 per level]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 7 (+1 from draconic resilience)\nArmor Class: 15 (13 (draconic resilience) + Dexterity modifier)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks: Dagger, 1d4 piercing damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nDraconic Resilience: You gain a bonus to your hit points equal to your sorcerer level. Additionally, while you aren't wearing armor, your AC equals 13 + your Dexterity modifier.\n\nDraconic Ancestry (Fire Dragon):\nFrequency: Passive ability, always active.\nMechanics: You trace your lineage back to the ancient fire dragons, granting you resistance to fire damage. As a manifestation of this ancestry, your skin might have a faint reddish hue, and when you tap into your draconic powers, your eyes briefly flare with fiery intensity.\n]\n</character_sheet_sorcerer>\",4,false,3,true,false,true,,4,3,false,true,10,4,90,\"character_sheet_sorcerer\",\"character_sheet_sorcerer\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,4,true,true,false,,\"High Elf Wizard Character Sheet (neutral, level 1)\",false,\"<character_sheet_wizard>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nRace: High Elf\n\nClass: Wizard\n\nBackground: Sage\n\nAlignment: Neutral\n\nStarting Attributes:[\nStrength: 8 (-1)\nDexterity: 14 (+2)\nConstitution: 12 (+1)\nIntelligence: 16 (+3)\nWisdom: 10 (+0)\nCharisma: 10 (+0)]\n\nSkills: Arcana, Investigation\n\nEquipment:[\nQuarterstaff\nComponent Pouch\nScholar's pack\nClothes\nSpellbook\n50 gold pieces]\n\nFeatures and Traits:\n\nRace: High Elf: +2 Dexterity, Darkvision, Keen Senses, Fey Ancestry, Trance\nClass: Wizard: Spellcasting, Arcane Recovery\nBackground: Sage: Researcher, Library Access\n\nSpell slots: \nTwo first level\n\nSpellcasting:\n\nCantrips:[\nFire Bolt:\nFrequency: At will.\nMechanics: You hurl a mote of fire at a creature or object within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 1d10 fire damage. The spell's damage increases as you reach higher levels: at 5th level (2d10), 11th level (3d10), and 17th level (4d10).\n\nMage Hand:\nFrequency: At will.\nMechanics: You conjure a spectral, floating hand that can manipulate objects and perform simple tasks at your command. The hand can't attack, activate magic items, or carry more than 10 pounds, but it can open unlocked doors, pick up items, and perform other minor tasks as directed by you. The spectral hand appears translucent and ethereal, typically in the shape of a small, disembodied hand.]\n\n1st Level Spells:[ \nMage Armor:\nFrequency: Once per casting.\nMechanics: You touch a willing creature and grant it a magical protection. Until the spell ends, the target's base Armor Class becomes 13 + its Dexterity modifier. This spell doesn't require concentration, and its effects last for 8 hours or until you dismiss it. At higher levels: When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 2nd level or higher, the AC increases by 1 for each slot level above 1st.\n\nMagic Missile:\nFrequency: Once per casting.\nMechanics: You create three glowing darts of magical force. Each dart hits a creature of your choice within range and deals 1d4+1 force damage. The darts all strike simultaneously and automatically hit their targets, even if they are invisible or hidden. At higher levels: When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 2nd level or higher, you create one additional dart for each slot level above 1st.]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 6\nArmor Class: 12 (10 + Dexterity modifier)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks: Quarterstaff, 1d6-1 bludgeoning damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities: [\nArcane Recovery: Once per day when you finish a short rest, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level that is equal to or less than half your wizard level (rounded up), and none of the slots can be 6th level or higher.\n\nArcane Mastery:\nFrequency: Once per long rest.\nMechanics: Channel your arcane prowess to momentarily enhance your spellcasting abilities. For the next minute, your spellcasting ability score increases by +2, improving the potency and accuracy of your spells. This ability allows you to unleash more powerful and precise magical effects for a limited time, making you a more formidable spellcaster in combat or when faced with challenging magical tasks.]\n</character_sheet_wizard>\",4,false,4,true,false,true,,4,4,false,true,10,5,90,\"character_sheet_wizard\",\"character_sheet_wizard\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,5,true,true,false,,\"Half-Orc Ranger Character Sheet (chaotic neutral, level 1)\",false,\"<character_sheet_ranger>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\nRace: Half-Orc\n\nClass: Ranger\n\nBackground: Outlander\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Neutral\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 16 (+3)\nDexterity: 14 (+2)\nConstitution: 14 (+2)\nIntelligence: 10 (+0)\nWisdom: 12 (+1)\nCharisma: 8 (-1)]\n\nSkills: Athletics, Survival\n\nEquipment:[\nLongbow with 20 arrows\nGreatsword\nExplorer's Pack\nTraveler's Clothes\nHunting Trap\n50 gold pieces]\n\nFeatures and Traits:\n\nRace: Half-Orc: +2 Strength, +1 Constitution, Darkvision, Menacing, Relentless Endurance\nClass: Ranger: Favored Enemy, Natural Explorer\nBackground: Outlander: Wanderer, Feature: Rustic Hospitality\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 11\nArmor Class: 13 (Leather Armor)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nLongbow: 1d8 piercing damage (range 150/600)\nGreatsword: 2d6 slashing damage]\n\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nFavored Enemy: Humanoids\nFrequency: Passive ability, always active against chosen enemies.\nMechanics: Gain bonuses to tracking, damage, and intelligence checks related to humanoid creatures. This bonus also applies to interactions and knowledge about the favored enemy. Additionally, enemies of this type can't hide from the ranger's keen perception or escape their relentless pursuit.\n\nNatural Explorer: Forests\nFrequency: Passive ability, always active in forests.\nMechanics: Gain bonuses to traveling, stealth, and survival checks related to forest terrain. Additionally, move stealthily and set cunning traps more effectively in forest environments, making the ranger adept at traversing wooded areas and ambushing foes within them.]\n\n</character_sheet_ranger>\",4,false,5,true,false,true,,4,5,false,true,10,6,90,\"character_sheet_ranger\",\"character_sheet_ranger\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,6,true,true,false,,\"Wood Elf Druid Character Sheet (neutral good, level 1)\",false,\"<character_sheet_druid>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nRace: Wood Elf\n\nClass: Druid\n\nBackground: Hermit\n\nAlignment: Neutral Good\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 10 (+0)\nDexterity: 16 (+3)\nConstitution: 12 (+1)\nIntelligence: 10 (+0)\nWisdom: 16 (+3)\nCharisma: 8 (-1)]\n\nSkills: Medicine, Nature\n\nEquipment:[\nStaff\nLeather Armor\nExplorer's Pack\nDruidic Focus (Holly)\nHerbalism Kit\n50 gold pieces]\n\nFeatures and Traits:\n\nRace: Wood Elf: +2 Dexterity, +1 Wisdom, Darkvision, Keen Senses, Fey Ancestry, Trance, Mask of the Wild\nClass: Druid: Spellcasting, Wild Shape\nBackground: Hermit: Discovery, Feature: Discovery (specific discovery based on character background)\n\nSpell slots: \nTwo first level\n\nSpellcasting:\nCantrips:[\nDruidcraft: This cantrip taps into the druid's connection with nature, allowing them to manipulate small natural elements and phenomena. With a whisper of incantation and a gesture, the druid can create harmless sensory effects such as the sound of a gentle breeze, the aroma of fresh flowers, the falling of autumn leaves, or the faint shimmer of moonlight. While not directly influencing creatures or objects, Druidcraft provides a subtle means of communication with nature and can be used for divination or simple atmospheric effects.\n\nProduce Flame: By harnessing their druidic energy, the caster conjures a small flame in their hand, providing illumination and a source of warmth. This flame can also be used as a basic tool for igniting flammable objects or creatures, though its damage potential is limited. As the druid grows in power, they can control the intensity of the flame, from a mere flicker to a small inferno. Additionally, Produce Flame can be wielded as a ranged attack, with the druid hurling the flame at a target within range to deal fire damage.]\n\n\n1st Level Spells:[\nCure Wounds: This spell channels positive energy to heal wounds. The caster lays their hands on a creature they wish to heal, restoring hit points equal to 1d8 + the caster's spellcasting ability modifier. As the caster gains levels, the effectiveness of Cure Wounds increases, granting additional hit points healed. For each spell slot used above 1st level, the spell's healing power increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 1st.\n\nEntangle: Entangle conjures thick, thorny vines and undergrowth to sprout from the ground in a 20-foot square area within range. Creatures in the area must succeed on a Strength saving throw or become restrained by the entangling plants. A restrained creature can use its action to make a Strength check against the spellcaster's spell save DC, ending the effect on itself on a success. As the caster gains levels, the duration and effectiveness of Entangle may increase, potentially affecting a larger area or imposing additional penalties on affected creatures.]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 8\nArmor Class: 13 (Leather Armor)\nSpeed: 35 ft.\nAttacks:\nStaff: 1d6 bludgeoning]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nWild Shape: Giant Poisonous Snake: Special ability that allows a druid to transform into a beast form. At 2nd level, the druid can use Wild Shape twice before needing to take a short rest to regain this ability. The duration of the transformation typically lasts for a number of hours equal to half the druid's level rounded down. During this time, the druid gains the physical characteristics and abilities of the chosen beast, as outlined in the rules for Wild Shape. Additional forms gained upon leveling.\n\nNature's Vigilance:\nFrequency: Once per long rest\nMechanics: The druid can spend 10 minutes in meditation to attune their senses to the surroundings. For the next hour, the druid gains advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks related to natural phenomena such as weather changes, animal behavior, or hidden dangers in the wilderness.]\n</character_sheet_druid>\",4,false,6,true,false,true,,4,6,false,true,10,7,90,\"character_sheet_druid\",\"character_sheet_druid\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,7,true,true,false,,\"Human Paladin Character Sheet (lawful good, level 5)\",false,\"<character_sheet_paladin>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nRace: Human\n\nLevel: 5\n\nClass: Paladin\n\nBackground: Noble\n\nAlignment: Lawful Good\n\nAttributes:\n\nStrength: 16 (+3)\nDexterity: 10 (+0)\nConstitution: 14 (+2)\nIntelligence: 10 (+0)\nWisdom: 12 (+1)\nCharisma: 14 (+2)\nSkills: Persuasion, Religion\n\nEquipment:[\nLongsword\nShield\nChain Mail\nHoly Symbol\nExplorer's Pack\nSignet Ring\nScroll of Pedigree\n50 gold pieces]\n\nFeatures and Traits:\n\nRace: Human: +1 to all attributes\nClass: Paladin: Divine Sense, Lay on Hands, Divine Smite\nBackground: Noble: Position of Privilege, Feature: Feature: Retainers\n\nSpell slots:\nFour 1st-level spell slots\nTwo 2nd-level spell slots\n\nSpellcasting:\nLevel 1 spells:[\nDivine Favor\nMechanics: Concentration spell that imbues the Paladin's weapon with divine energy, granting them a bonus to their weapon damage rolls for the duration of the spell. The bonus increases with the Paladin's spell slot level.\n\nShield of Faith\nMechanics: Concentration spell that surrounds the Paladin with a shimmering field of divine energy, increasing their Armor Class for the duration of the spell. The AC bonus remains constant regardless of the spell slot level used.]\n\nLevel 2 Spells:[\nBranding Smite:\nMechanics: This spell imbues the Paladin's weapon with radiant energy, causing it to shed bright light in a radius around the target. Additionally, on a successful hit, the target takes radiant damage, and becomes visible if invisible, and makes it impossible to become invisible for the duration of the spell.]\n\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 51\nArmor Class: 18 (Chain Mail + Shield)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nLongsword:1d8 slashing damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nDivine Sense:\nFrequency: Usable at will.\nMechanics: Allows the Paladin to detect the presence of undead creatures or the desecration or consecration of objects or places within a certain radius. The range and specific nature of the detected presence improve as the Paladin gains levels.\n\nLay on Hands:\nFrequency: Once per long rest.\nMechanics: Allows the Paladin to restore hit points to themselves or others by touch, with the amount of healing equal to their Paladin level multiplied by 5.\n\nDivine Smite:\nFrequency: Usable with a melee weapon attack and expending a spell slot.\nMechanics: Allows the Paladin to channel their divine energy through their weapon, expending a spell slot to deal extra radiant damage on top of the weapon's normal damage. The extra damage is 2d8 for a 1st-level spell slot, plus 1d8 for each spell level higher than 1st, to a maximum of 5d8.\n\nBranding Smite:\nFrequency: Usable with a melee weapon attack and expending a spell slot.\nMechanics: Upon successfully hitting a target with a melee weapon attack, you can expend a spell slot to deal additional radiant damage. The target is marked with a mystical sigil, which burns with divine energy, causing it to shed dim light in a 5-foot radius and impose disadvantage on stealth checks made by the target. The additional damage dealt is 2d6 radiant damage for a 2nd-level spell slot, plus 1d6 for each spell level higher than 2nd, to a maximum of 5d6.]\n</character_sheet_paladin>\",4,false,7,true,false,true,,4,7,false,true,10,8,90,\"character_sheet_paladin\",\"character_sheet_paladin\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,8,true,true,false,,\"Half-Elf Priest Character Sheet (neutral good, level 5)\",false,\"<character_sheet_priest>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nRace: Half-Elf\n\nLevel: 5\n\nClass: Cleric (Life Domain)\n\nBackground: Acolyte\n\nAlignment: Neutral Good\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 10 (+0)\nDexterity: 12 (+1)\nConstitution: 14 (+2)\nIntelligence: 10 (+0)\nWisdom: 16 (+3)\nCharisma: 14 (+2)]\n\nSkills: Insight, Medicine\n\nEquipment:[\nMace\nShield\nHoly Symbol\nPriest's Pack\nCloth Robes\n50 gold pieces]\n\nFeatures and Traits:\n\nRace: Half-Elf: +2 Charisma, +1 to two other attributes of your choice, Darkvision, Fey Ancestry\nClass: Cleric: Spellcasting, Divine Domain (Life)\nBackground: Acolyte: Shelter of the Faithful, Feature: Feature: Feature: False Identity\n\nSpell slots:\nFour 1st-level spell slots\nThree 2nd-level spell slots\n\nSpellcasting:\nCantrips:[\nSacred Flame: The caster targets a creature they can see within range with a divine flame. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 1d8 radiant damage. The spell's damage increases to 2d8 at 5th level, 3d8 at 11th level, and 4d8 at 17th level.\n\nThaumaturgy: Allows the caster to perform minor miracles and create various magical effects within range. These effects can include causing harmless tremors, altering the appearance of their eyes, making their voice boom up to three times louder, or creating an instantaneous sound. This cantrip does not directly cause damage or harm to creatures but can be used to create dramatic or distracting effects.]\n\n\n1st Level Spells:[\nCure Wounds: The cleric calls upon their deity's power to heal wounds. The target regains hit points equal to 1d8 + the cleric's spellcasting ability modifier. The spell's healing increases with higher-level spell slots. At 1st level, it heals 1d8 + spellcasting ability modifier. At higher levels, it heals an additional 1d8 for each spell slot level above 1st.\n\nBless: The cleric blesses up to three creatures of their choice within range. Whenever a target makes an attack roll or a saving throw before the spell ends, they can add a d4 to the roll. The spell's duration is concentration, up to 1 minute.]\n\n2nd Level Spells:[\nAid: The cleric calls upon divine energy to bolster the health of their allies. This spell targets up to three creatures within range and grants them temporary hit points equal to 5 + the cleric's spellcasting ability modifier. These temporary hit points last for 8 hours. At higher levels, when cast with a spell slot of 3rd level or higher, the spell grants an additional 5 temporary hit points for each slot level above 2nd.]\n\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 38\nArmor Class: 15 (Divine Aegis + Shield)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nMace: 1d6 bludgeoning damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nHealing Hands: Passive ability. Bonus healing spells, Disciple of Life (add 2+spell level to healing spells).\n\nDivine Strike: Passive ability. At 5th level, your connection to divine power allows you to infuse your weapon strikes with holy energy. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 radiant damage. This extra damage increases to 2d8 at 11th level.\n\nChannel Divinity: Turn Undead: Once per short rest. As an action, you present your holy symbol and speak a prayer, calling upon your deity's power to drive away undead.\n\nDivine Aegis:\nFrequency: Passive ability.\nMechanics: While wearing cloth armor, the priest gains a +2 bonus to AC, +1 to spell save DC, and all healing spells cast on themselves heal an additional 1d8 hit points. Additionally, they radiate an aura of tranquility, granting them and allies within 5 feet resistance to psychic damage.]\n\n</character_sheet_priest>\",4,false,8,true,false,true,,4,8,false,true,10,9,90,\"character_sheet_priest\",\"character_sheet_priest\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,9,true,true,false,,\"Tiefling Warlock Character Sheet (chaotic neutral, level 5)\",false,\"<character_sheet_warlock>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\nRace: Tiefling\n\nClass: Warlock (Fiend Patron)\n\nBackground: Charlatan\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Neutral\n\nStarting Attributes:[\nStrength: 10 (+0)\nDexterity: 14 (+2)\nConstitution: 12 (+1)\nIntelligence: 10 (+0)\nWisdom: 8 (-1)\nCharisma: 16 (+3)]\n\nSkills: Deception, Arcana\n\nEquipment:[\n\nLight Crossbow\nQuarterstaff\nComponent Pouch\nScholar's Pack\nFine clothes\n50 gold pieces]\n\nRace: Tiefling: +2 Charisma, +1 Intelligence, Darkvision, Fiendish Resilience, Infernal Legacy (Thaumaturgy cantrip)\nClass: Warlock: Pact Magic, Otherworldly Patron (Fiend)\nBackground: Charlatan: False Identity, Forgery Kit\n\nSpell slots:\n2 slots of each level up to 3rd level (replenishes after short rest)\n\nSpellcasting:\nCantrips:[\nThaumaturgy: Allows the caster to manifest minor wonders for up to 1 minute. These wonders can include causing harmless tremors in the ground, opening or closing doors or windows, causing flames to flicker or brighten, or creating ominous whispers. \n\nEldritch Blast: This cantrip conjures a beam of crackling energy that streaks toward a target within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 1d10 force damage. The spell's damage increases as you reach higher levels: at 5th level, the damage increases to 2d10, at 11th level, it increases to 3d10, and at 17th level, it increases to 4d10.\n\nMinor Illusion: This cantrip allows you to create a sound or an image of an object within range that lasts for the duration, which is up to 1 minute. The illusion can't create any sensory effects, such as light, sound, smell, or any other sensory effect, nor can it deal damage. The illusion also can't be larger than a 5-foot cube.]\n\n1st Level Spells:[\nArmor of Agathys: Surrounds the caster with magical frost, providing temporary hit points and dealing cold damage to attackers who hit with melee attacks. The amount of temporary hit points and damage dealt increases with the spell slot level.\n\nHex: Places a curse on a target, granting disadvantage on ability checks tied to a chosen ability score and dealing extra necrotic damage whenever the caster hits the cursed target with an attack. The spell lasts for combat duration and can be moved to a new target upon the previous one's death.\n\n2nd Level Spells:[\nDarkness: Creates a magical darkness within a specific radius, heavily obscuring the area and making it difficult for creatures without darkvision to see.\n\nInvisibility: Renders the target invisible until the spell ends or the target attacks or casts a spell. Invisible creatures gain advantage on attack rolls, and attackers have disadvantage when trying to target the invisible creature with attacks and spells.]\n\nCombat stats:[\nHit Points: 28\nArmor Class: 11 (without armor)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nLight Crossbow: 1d8 piercing damage (range 80/320)\nQuarterstaff: 1d6 bludgeoning damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nDark One's Blessing:\nFrequency: Passive ability, activates when reducing a creature to 0 hit points.\nMechanics: When you reduce a hostile creature to 0 hit points, you gain temporary hit points equal to your Charisma modifier + your warlock level (minimum of 1). These temporary hit points last until they are depleted or you finish a short or long rest.\n\nFiendish Resilience:\nFrequency: Once per short rest.\nMechanics: Starting at 1st level, you gain the ability to draw on your patron's infernal power to bolster your defenses. As a bonus action, you can choose one magical damage type and gain resistance to that damage type for one hour. This resistance means you take half damage from any source of that damage type.\n\nFiendish Fury:\nFrequency: Once per long rest.\nMechanics: When you take damage from a creature within 30 feet of you, you can unleash a burst of infernal energy. The creature must make a Dexterity saving throw against your Warlock spell save DC. On fail, it takes fire damage equal to your Charisma modifier + your warlock level. On success, it takes half damage. \n\nInfernal Pact:\nFrequency: Passive ability.\nMechanics: You gain proficiency in persuasion. Additionally, when you cast a spell that deals fire damage, you can add your Charisma modifier to one damage roll of that spell.]\n\n</character_sheet_warlock>\n\",4,false,9,true,false,true,,4,9,false,true,10,10,90,\"character_sheet_warlock\",\"character_sheet_warlock\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,10,true,true,false,,\"Leveling and experience\",false,\"<experience>\nIn Dungeons & Dragons 5th Edition, the experience point (XP) thresholds required to advance to each level are as follows:\n\n1 to 2: 300 XP\n2 to 3: 900 XP\n3 to 4: 2,700 XP\n4 to 5: 6,500 XP\n5 to 6: 14,000 XP\n6 to 7: 23,000 XP\n7 to 8: 34,000 XP\n8 to 9: 48,000 XP\n9 to 10: 64,000 XP\n10 to 11: 85,000 XP\n11 to 12: 100,000 XP\n12 to 13: 120,000 XP\n13 to 14: 140,000 XP\n14 to 15: 165,000 XP\n15 to 16: 195,000 XP\n16 to 17: 225,000 XP\n17 to 18: 265,000 XP\n18 to 19: 305,000 XP\n19 to 20: 355,000 XP\n</experience>\",4,false,10,true,true,true,,4,10,true,true,10,11,100,\"level gain\",\"gained level\",\"level increase\",\"higher level\",\"level_up\",\"levelled up\",\"level gain\",\"gained level\",\"level increase\",\"higher level\",\"level_up\",\"levelled up\",\"\",100,1,10,100,true,0,11,true,true,false,,\"Dungeon Master Guide - rolling\",false,\"Golden rules of dice rolling:\n1. AI must favor neither the player nor NPC/enemy.\n2. Dice rolls must be truly random.\n3. AI avoids granting the player artificially high rolls.\n4. AI is creative in what it rolls dice for.\n5. Enemies also obtain high rolls sometimes.\n6. AI must use the {{roll dX}} function for rolling.\",4,false,11,true,false,true,,4,11,false,true,10,12,100,\"d8\",\"save\",\"d10\",\"d20\",\"d4\",\"combat\",\"d12\",\"d6\",\"dice\",\"roll\",\"d8\",\"save\",\"d10\",\"d20\",\"d4\",\"combat\",\"d12\",\"d6\",\"dice\",\"roll\",\"\",100,1,10,100,true,0,12,true,true,false,,\"Magic Items - Armor\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nAdamantine Armor:[\n\nDescription: This suit of armor is forged from adamantine, a legendary metal known for its exceptional hardness and durability. It gleams with a silvery sheen and provides excellent protection against physical attacks.\nStats Change: Adamantine armor grants the wearer resistance to non-magical slashing, piercing, and bludgeoning damage.\nArmor Class: 18]\n\nDragon Scale Mail:[\n\nDescription: Crafted from the scales of a slain dragon, this armor is both majestic and formidable. The scales shimmer with vibrant colors and are as tough as steel.\nStats Change: Dragon scale mail grants the wearer resistance to a specific type of damage associated with the dragon from which the scales were obtained, such as fire, cold, acid, or lightning damage.\nArmor Class: 18]\n\nMithril Chain Mail:[\n\nDescription: This chain mail is woven from mithril, a rare and precious metal known for its lightweight yet incredibly strong properties. It shines with a bright luster and is favored by adventurers who value mobility and protection.\nStats Change: Mithril chain mail eliminates the Strength requirement and Stealth disadvantage associated with regular chain mail, making it easier to wear and allowing for more stealthy movement.\nArmor Class: 16 + Dexterity modifier (max 2)]\n\nPlate Armor of Etherealness:[\n\nDescription: This suit of plate armor is imbued with the essence of the Ethereal Plane, granting its wearer the ability to phase in and out of the material world at will. It appears ethereal and translucent when activated.\nStats Change: While wearing this plate armor, the wearer can use an action to become ethereal, allowing them to move through solid objects and ignore difficult terrain. This effect lasts for a limited duration and can be used once per day.\nArmor Class: 18]\n\nCelestial Plate:[\n\nDescription: This gleaming suit of plate armor is infused with the essence of the celestial realms, radiating divine energy and providing unparalleled protection against evil forces.\nStats Change: Celestial plate grants the wearer resistance to necrotic and radiant damage, as well as advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by undead creatures or fiends.\nArmor Class: 18]\n\nShadow Armor:[\n\nDescription: This dark and shadowy armor is crafted from the essence of the Shadowfell, the plane of shadow and darkness. It seems to absorb light and sound, blending seamlessly into the shadows.\nStats Change: While wearing this armor, the wearer gains advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks and can use an action to become invisible for a short duration, allowing them to move unseen and strike from the shadows.\nArmor Class: 14 + Dexterity modifier (max 2)]\n\nStormguard Plate:[\n\nDescription: This imposing suit of plate armor is enchanted with the power of the storm, crackling with electricity and exuding an aura of power and majesty.\nStats Change: Stormguard plate grants the wearer resistance to lightning damage and advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that deal lightning damage. Additionally, once per day, the wearer can call upon the power of the storm to cast a lightning bolt spell.\nArmor Class: 18]\n\nSylvan Chain:[\n\nDescription: This finely crafted chain mail is adorned with intricate patterns of leaves and vines, blending seamlessly with the natural world. It exudes an aura of primal energy and protection.\nStats Change: Sylvan chain grants the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that deal poison or disease damage, as well as resistance to poison damage. Additionally, once per day, the wearer can use an action to cast the pass without trace spell.\nArmor Class: 16 + Dexterity modifier (max 2)]\n\nSkins of the Phoenix:[\n\nDescription: This sleek and lightweight suit of leather armor is adorned with phoenix feathers and imbued with the fiery essence of the legendary bird. It radiates warmth and resilience, offering protection against the elements.\nStats Change: The Skins of the Phoenix grants the wearer resistance to fire damage and allows them to cast the fire shield spell once per day.\nArmor Class: 12 + Dexterity modifier (max 2)]\n\nArmor of the Feywild:[\n\nDescription: Crafted from the enchanted bark of ancient trees and woven with strands of fey magic, this armor embodies the beauty and mystery of the Feywild. It whispers with the secrets of nature and offers protection against the forces of darkness.\nStats Change: The Armor of the Feywild grants the wearer resistance to poison damage and advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by aberrations or fiends.\nArmor Class: 12 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nGray Dwarf Plate:[\n\nDescription: This sturdy suit of plate armor is meticulously crafted by dwarven smiths using ancient techniques passed down through generations. It bears intricate runes and symbols of dwarven craftsmanship, providing unmatched durability and protection.\nStats Change: Gray Dwarf Plate grants the wearer resistance to poison damage and advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by giants or creatures with the humanoid subtype.\nArmor Class: 18]\n\nGolemhide Armor:[\n\nDescription: Fashioned from the hide of a slain earth golem, this armor is as tough and resilient as the creatures from which it is made. It bears the scars of battle and exudes an aura of strength and fortitude.\nStats Change: Golemhide Armor grants the wearer resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage from non-magical weapons.\nArmor Class: 16 + Dexterity modifier (max 2)]\n\nMerfolk Scale Mail:[\n\nDescription: Woven from the scales of merfolk warriors who dwell in the depths of the ocean, this armor is as light as it is durable. It shimmers with an iridescent glow and offers protection against aquatic threats.\nStats Change: Merfolk Scale Mail grants the wearer a swimming speed equal to their walking speed and allows them to breathe underwater.\nArmor Class: 14 + Dexterity modifier (max 2)]\n\nSpider Silk Vestments:[\n\nDescription: These finely woven vestments are crafted from the silk of giant spiders and enchanted with the agility and stealth of the arachnid. They cling to the wearer's form like a second skin, allowing for swift and silent movement.\nStats Change: Spider Silk Vestments grant the wearer advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks and the ability to climb difficult surfaces without needing to make an ability check.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nStormscale Armor:[\n\nDescription: Fashioned from the scales of storm giants, this armor crackles with the power of thunder and lightning. It is as imposing as the storms themselves and offers protection against the fury of the elements.\nStats Change: Stormscale Armor grants the wearer resistance to lightning and thunder damage, as well as advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that deal such damage.\nArmor Class: 16]\n\",4,false,12,true,false,true,,4,12,false,true,10,13,80,\"enchanted armor\",\"imbued armor\",\"magic mail\",\"magic leather\",\"magic armor\",\"magic chain\",\"magic scale\",\"magic_armor\",\"magic plate\",\"enchanted armor\",\"imbued armor\",\"magic mail\",\"magic leather\",\"magic armor\",\"magic chain\",\"magic scale\",\"magic_armor\",\"magic plate\",\"\",80,1,10,100,true,0,13,true,true,false,,\"Magic Items - Robes and Cloth\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nRobes of the Archmage:[\n\nDescription: These robes are woven from the finest silk and embroidered with arcane sigils. They emanate an aura of magical power and command respect from all who behold them.\nStats Change: Robes of the Archmage grant the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that deal force damage, as well as resistance to force damage.\nArmor Class: 12 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nSorcerer's Silks:[\n\nDescription: These shimmering silken robes are imbued with wild magic, reflecting the chaotic nature of sorcery. They flow and ripple like liquid fire, channeling the raw power of the elements.\nStats Change: Sorcerer's Silks grant the wearer resistance to a specific type of damage associated with their chosen sorcerous origin, such as fire, cold, acid, or lightning damage.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nWarlock's Vestments:[\n\nDescription: These dark and foreboding robes are adorned with eldritch symbols and infused with the power of dark pacts. They exude an aura of menace and grant their wearer command over dark magics.\nStats Change: Warlock's Vestments grant the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by fiends or creatures with the undead subtype, as well as resistance to necrotic damage.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nPriestly Robes:[\n\nDescription: These humble robes are worn by priests and clerics in service to their gods. They are simple yet elegant, adorned with religious symbols and imbued with divine blessings.\nStats Change: Priestly Robes grant the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that deal radiant or necrotic damage, as well as resistance to radiant damage.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nArcane Mantle:[\n\nDescription: This flowing mantle is woven from threads of pure arcane energy and adorned with mystical runes. It crackles with magical power and grants its wearer mastery over the arcane arts.\nStats Change: Arcane Mantle grants the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that deal elemental damage (fire, cold, acid, lightning), as well as resistance to a specific elemental damage type of the wearer's choice.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nNecromancer's Shroud:[\n\nDescription: This tattered shroud is woven from the shadows of the grave and infused with the essence of death. It whispers dark secrets to its wearer and grants mastery over necromantic magic.\nStats Change: Necromancer's Shroud grants the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by undead creatures, as well as resistance to necrotic damage.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nEnchanter's Veil:[\n\nDescription: This translucent veil is woven from threads of enchantment magic and shimmers with an otherworldly glow. It enhances the wearer's charm and persuasion, allowing them to sway the minds of others.\nStats Change: Enchanter's Veil grants the wearer advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks and allows them to cast the charm person spell once per day.\nArmor Class: 10 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nElemental Robes:[\n\nDescription: These robes are infused with the essence of the elemental planes, granting their wearer control over the elements. They crackle with energy and shift colors in response to the elemental forces nearby.\nStats Change: Elemental Robes grant the wearer resistance to a specific type of elemental damage (fire, cold, acid, lightning) chosen by the wearer, as well as advantage on saving throws against spells and effects of that chosen element.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nDiviner's Mantle:[\n\nDescription: This flowing mantle is adorned with celestial symbols and imbued with the power of divination magic. It allows its wearer to see glimpses of the future and peer into the mysteries of the cosmos.\nStats Change: Diviner's Mantle grants the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that cause blindness or deafness, as well as resistance to radiant damage.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nDruidic Vestments:[\n\nDescription: These rugged vestments are woven from natural fibers and adorned with symbols of the wild. They resonate with the primal energies of nature and grant their wearer command over the elements.\nStats Change: Druidic Vestments grant the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that cause poison or disease, as well as resistance to poison damage.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nAbjurer's Robes:[\n\nDescription: These sturdy robes are woven with protective wards and reinforced with magical energy. They shield their wearer from harm and deflect incoming attacks with ease.\nStats Change: Abjurer's Robes grant the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that cause paralysis or petrification, as well as resistance to force damage.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nBardic Garb:[\n\nDescription: This stylish attire is tailored for bards and performers, adorned with colorful fabrics and intricate designs. It enhances the wearer's charisma and charm, captivating audiences wherever they go.\nStats Change: Bardic Garb grants the wearer advantage on Charisma (Performance) checks and allows them to cast the friends cantrip once per day.\nArmor Class: 10 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nArcanist's Robes:[\n\nDescription: These robes are adorned with arcane symbols and infused with the raw power of magic. They amplify the wearer's spells and allow for greater control over arcane energies.\nStats Change: Arcanist's Robes grant the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that cause blindness or deafness, as well as resistance to force damage.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\",4,false,13,true,false,true,,4,13,false,true,10,14,80,\"enchanted cloth\",\"magic_cloth\",\"magic vestments\",\"magic cloth\",\"enchanted robes\",\"magic robes\",\"enchanted cloth\",\"magic_cloth\",\"magic vestments\",\"magic cloth\",\"enchanted robes\",\"magic robes\",\"\",80,1,10,100,true,0,14,true,true,false,,\"Magic Items - 1h Weapons\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nFlame Tongue Shortsword:[\n\nDescription: This shortsword is crafted from enchanted steel and adorned with fiery runes. It bursts into flames when drawn, dealing extra fire damage to foes.\nDamage: 1d6 slashing + 2d6 fire\nSpecial Bonus: The Flame Tongue Shortsword grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against being frightened, and it sheds bright light in a 40-foot radius and dim light for an additional 40 feet while the flame is active.]\n\nFrostbrand Rapier:[\n\nDescription: This rapier is made of icy-blue steel and crackles with frost energy. It chills enemies to the bone with each strike, slowing their movements.\nDamage: 1d8 piercing + 1d6 cold\nSpecial Bonus: The Frostbrand Rapier grants the wielder resistance to cold damage and allows them to cast the ray of frost cantrip once per day.]\n\nThunderstrike Warhammer:[\n\nDescription: This warhammer is infused with the power of thunderstorms, crackling with lightning energy. It sends shockwaves through enemies on impact, stunning them momentarily.\nDamage: 1d8 bludgeoning + 1d6 thunder\nSpecial Bonus: The Thunderstrike Warhammer grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against being stunned and allows them to cast the thunderwave spell once per day.]\n\nShadowblade Dagger:[\n\nDescription: This dagger is made of shadowy obsidian and whispers with dark whispers. It strikes silently and swiftly, leaving foes unaware of their wounds until it's too late.\nDamage: 1d4 piercing + 1d6 necrotic\nSpecial Bonus: The Shadowblade Dagger grants the wielder advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks and allows them to cast the darkness spell once per day.]\n\nHoly Avenger Longsword:[\n\nDescription: This longsword is imbued with divine energy and radiates a holy aura. It smites evil creatures with righteous fury, banishing them from existence.\nDamage: 1d8 slashing + 2d8 radiant\nSpecial Bonus: The Holy Avenger Longsword grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by fiends or undead creatures and allows them to cast the bless spell once per day.]\n\nVenomous Scimitar:[\n\nDescription: This scimitar is coated in deadly poison, dripping with toxic venom. It inflicts debilitating wounds on foes, weakening their resolve and sapping their strength.\nDamage: 1d6 slashing + 1d4 poison\nSpecial Bonus: The Venomous Scimitar grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against being poisoned and allows them to apply poison to the weapon, dealing an additional 1d4 poison damage on a successful hit.]\n\nArcane Blade Shortsword:[\n\nDescription: This shortsword crackles with arcane energy, humming with power. It slices through magical barriers and disrupts enemy spellcasting with ease.\nDamage: 1d6 slashing + 1d6 force\nSpecial Bonus: The Arcane Blade Shortsword grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that cause paralysis or petrification and allows them to cast the dispel magic spell once per day.]\n\nSoulrender Dagger:[\n\nDescription: This dagger is forged from darksteel and hungers for souls. It absorbs the life force of enemies, healing its wielder with each strike.\nDamage: 1d4 piercing + 1d6 necrotic\nSpecial Bonus: The Soulrender Dagger grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened and allows them to regain hit points equal to the necrotic damage dealt on a successful hit once per day.]\n\nSunblade Cutlass:[\n\nDescription: This cutlass is imbued with the power of the sun, radiating a warm golden glow. It sears through darkness and undead foes with righteous light.\nDamage: 1d6 slashing + 1d8 radiant\nSpecial Bonus: The Sunblade Cutlass grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by undead creatures and fiends and sheds bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet.]\n\nStormcaller Scimitar:[\n\nDescription: This scimitar crackles with the power of thunderstorms, echoing with the roar of thunder. It lashes out with lightning speed, striking foes with electrifying force.\nDamage: 1d6 slashing + 1d6 lightning\nSpecial Bonus: The Stormcaller Scimitar grants the wielder resistance to lightning damage and allows them to cast the thunderwave spell once per day.]\n\nMoonshadow Dagger:[\n\nDescription: This dagger is crafted from moonstone and veiled in shadow. It strikes with the silent precision of the night, leaving enemies bewildered and disoriented.\nDamage: 1d4 piercing + 1d6 psychic\nSpecial Bonus: The Moonshadow Dagger grants the wielder advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks and allows them to cast the invisibility spell once per day.]\n\nBlade of the Feywild:[\n\nDescription: This elegant blade is adorned with fey symbols and infused with fey magic. It dances with ethereal grace, cutting through reality itself.\nDamage: 1d8 slashing + 1d4 force\nSpecial Bonus: The Blade of the Feywild grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by aberrations or fey creatures and allows them to cast the misty step spell once per day.]\n\nDoombringer Longsword:[\n\nDescription: This longsword is etched with infernal runes and radiates an aura of darkness. It strikes fear into the hearts of enemies, draining their life force with each blow.\nDamage: 1d8 slashing + 1d6 necrotic\nSpecial Bonus: The Doombringer Longsword grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that cause fear and allows them to cast the inflict wounds spell once per day.]\n\nSwiftstrike Rapier:[\n\nDescription: This rapier is sleek and lightweight, designed for swift and precise strikes. It leaves foes reeling from its blinding speed.\nDamage: 1d8 piercing\nSpecial Bonus: The Swiftstrike Rapier grants the wielder advantage on initiative rolls and allows them to make an additional attack as a bonus action once per day.]\n\nDragon's Breath Shortsword:[\n\nDescription: This shortsword is forged from dragonbone and infused with dragonfire. It belches forth flames with each swing, scorching enemies in its wake.\nDamage: 1d6 slashing + 1d6 fire\nSpecial Bonus: The Dragon's Breath Shortsword grants the wielder resistance to fire damage and allows them to exhale a 15-foot cone of fire as an action once per day, dealing 2d6 fire damage.]\n\nAngelsteel Dagger:[\n\nDescription: This dagger is crafted from celestial metals and gleams with divine light. It strikes with the precision and purity of angels, banishing evil with each thrust.\nDamage: 1d4 piercing + 1d6 radiant\nSpecial Bonus: The Angelsteel Dagger grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by fiends or undead creatures and allows them to cast the divine favor spell once per day.]\n\nThe Tickler:[\nMechanics: When you hit a creature with The Tickler, it has a chance to induce uncontrollable laughter. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or become incapacitated with laughter for 1 round. While incapacitated by The Tickler, the victim is prone to fits of giggling, granting advantage on all attack rolls against them until they regain their composure.\nFrequency: The laughter effect can be activated three times per long rest.\nDamage: 1d6 piercing\nFrequency: The laughter effect can be activated three times per long rest.]\",4,false,14,true,false,true,,4,14,false,true,10,15,81,\"magic shortsword\",\"magic dagger\",\"magic longsword\",\"magic mace\",\"magic weapons\",\"magic_1hweapons\",\"magic axe\",\"enchanted weapons\",\"magic blade\",\"magic flail\",\"magic rapier\",\"magic cutlass\",\"magic hammer\",\"magic warhammer\",\"magic sword\",\"magic scimitar\",\"magic shortsword\",\"magic dagger\",\"magic longsword\",\"magic mace\",\"magic weapons\",\"magic_1hweapons\",\"magic axe\",\"enchanted weapons\",\"magic blade\",\"magic flail\",\"magic rapier\",\"magic cutlass\",\"magic hammer\",\"magic warhammer\",\"magic sword\",\"magic scimitar\",\"\",81,1,10,100,true,0,15,true,true,false,,\"Magic Items - 2h Weapons\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nVoidblade Greatsword:[\n\nDescription: This greatsword is forged from darksteel and radiates an aura of emptiness. It slices through reality itself, leaving behind a void in its wake.\nDamage: 2d6 slashing\nSpecial Bonus: The Voidblade Greatsword grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that cause paralysis or petrification and allows them to cast the darkness spell once per day.]\n\nThunderfury Greataxe:[\n\nDescription: This greataxe crackles with lightning energy and echoes with the roar of thunder. It cleaves through enemies with electrifying force, leaving them stunned and disoriented.\nDamage: 1d12 slashing + 1d6 thunder\nSpecial Bonus: The Thunderfury Greataxe grants the wielder resistance to lightning damage and allows them to cast the thunderwave spell once per day.\n\nSoulreaper Halberd:[\n\nDescription: This halberd is imbued with the essence of death, draining the life force of enemies with each swing. It leaves behind a trail of desolation and decay.\nDamage: 1d10 slashing + 1d8 necrotic\nSpecial Bonus: The Soulreaper Halberd grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by undead creatures or fiends and allows them to regain hit points equal to the necrotic damage dealt on a successful hit once per day.]\n\nCelestial Maul:[\n\nDescription: This maul is infused with divine energy and radiates a holy aura. It smites evil creatures with righteous fury, purging them with celestial fire.\nDamage: 2d6 bludgeoning + 1d8 radiant\nSpecial Bonus: The Celestial Maul grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by fiends or undead creatures and allows them to cast the divine favor spell once per day.]\n\nFrostbite Polearm:[\n\nDescription: This polearm is coated in icy rime and crackles with frost energy. It freezes enemies in their tracks, leaving them shivering and vulnerable.\nDamage: 1d10 slashing + 1d6 cold\nSpecial Bonus: The Frostbite Polearm grants the wielder resistance to cold damage and allows them to cast the ray of frost cantrip once per day.]\n\nInfernal Maul:[\n\nDescription: This great maul is etched with infernal runes and glows with hellish fire. It smashes through enemy defenses with relentless force, leaving behind trails of destruction.\nDamage: 2d8 bludgeoning + 1d6 fire\nSpecial Bonus: The Infernal Maul grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by fiends and allows them to cast the hellish rebuke spell once per day.]\n\nEthereal Greathammer:[\n\nDescription: This greathammer is infused with the essence of the Ethereal Plane, phasing in and out of reality with each swing. It strikes with otherworldly force, bypassing armor and shields.\nDamage: 2d8 bludgeoning + 1d6 force\nSpecial Bonus: The Ethereal Greathammer grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against being paralyzed or restrained and allows them to become ethereal for 1 minute once per day, as if affected by the etherealness spell.]\n\nShadowsong Claymore:[\n\nDescription: This claymore is shrouded in darkness, blending seamlessly with the shadows. It strikes with the precision of a skilled assassin, cutting through armor and flesh alike.\nDamage: 2d8 slashing + 1d6 necrotic\nSpecial Bonus: The Shadowsong Claymore grants the wielder advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks and allows them to cast the darkness spell once per day.]\n\nStormbreaker Halberd:[\n\nDescription: This halberd crackles with the power of thunderstorms, echoing with the roar of thunder. It cleaves through enemies with electrifying force, leaving them stunned and disoriented.\nDamage: 1d10 slashing + 1d6 thunder\nSpecial Bonus: The Stormbreaker Halberd grants the wielder resistance to lightning damage and allows them to cast the thunderwave spell once per day.]\n\nFlameheart Greatsword:[\n\nDescription: This greatsword burns with inner fire, radiating heat and light. It strikes with the fury of a raging inferno, engulfing enemies in flames.\nDamage: 2d6 slashing + 1d8 fire\nSpecial Bonus: The Flameheart Greatsword grants the wielder resistance to fire damage and allows them to cast the burning hands spell once per day.]\n\nFrostbite Maul:[\n\nDescription: This maul is encased in ice and crackles with frost energy. It shatters enemy defenses with bone-chilling force, leaving them frozen in their tracks.\nDamage: 2d8 bludgeoning + 1d6 cold\nSpecial Bonus: The Frostbite Maul grants the wielder resistance to cold damage and allows them to cast the ice knife spell once per day.]\n\nSoulshard Greataxe:[\n\nDescription: This greataxe is forged from darksteel and pulses with dark energy. It cleaves through enemies with relentless force, draining their life force with each strike.\nDamage: 1d12 slashing + 1d8 necrotic\nSpecial Bonus: The Soulshard Greataxe grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by undead creatures or fiends and allows them to regain hit points equal to the necrotic damage dealt on a successful hit once per day.]\n\nCelestial Maul:[\n\nDescription: This maul is imbued with divine energy and radiates a holy aura. It smites evil creatures with righteous fury, purging them with celestial fire.\nDamage: 2d8 bludgeoning + 1d8 radiant\nSpecial Bonus: The Celestial Maul grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by fiends or undead creatures and allows them to cast the searing smite spell once per day.]\n\nDoombringer Claymore:[\n\nDescription: This claymore is etched with infernal runes and radiates an aura of darkness. It strikes fear into the hearts of enemies, draining their life force with each blow.\nDamage: 2d8 slashing + 1d6 necrotic\nSpecial Bonus: The Doombringer Claymore grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that cause fear and allows them to cast the inflict wounds spell once per day.]\n\nEthereal Bastard Sword:[\n\nDescription: This bastard sword is infused with the essence of the Ethereal Plane, phasing in and out of reality with each swing. It strikes with otherworldly force, bypassing armor and shields.\nDamage: 2d6 slashing + 1d6 force\nSpecial Bonus: The Ethereal Bastard Sword grants the wielder advantage on saving throws against being paralyzed or restrained and allows them to become ethereal for 1 minute once per day, as if affected by the etherealness spell.]\",4,false,15,true,false,true,,4,15,false,true,10,16,81,\"magic_2hweapons\",\"magic polearm\",\"magic claymore\",\"polearm\",\"magic weapons\",\"magic greataxe\",\"magic maul\",\"enchanted weapons\",\"magic greatsword\",\"magic bastard\",\"magic greathammer\",\"magic halberd\",\"magic_2hweapons\",\"magic polearm\",\"magic claymore\",\"polearm\",\"magic weapons\",\"magic greataxe\",\"magic maul\",\"enchanted weapons\",\"magic greatsword\",\"magic bastard\",\"magic greathammer\",\"magic halberd\",\"\",81,1,10,100,true,0,16,true,true,false,,\"Magic Items - Jewelry\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nRing of Invisibility:[\n\nDescription: This silver ring is set with a clear gemstone that seems to shimmer with unseen energies. When worn, it grants the wearer the ability to become invisible at will.\nBonus: Grants the wearer the ability to cast the invisibility spell once per day.]\n\nAmulet of Health:[\n\nDescription: This golden amulet is adorned with intricate engravings of healing symbols. When worn, it bestows the wearer with increased vitality and resilience.\nBonus: Increases the wearer's Constitution score by 2, up to a maximum of 20.]\n\nRing of Teleportation:[\n\nDescription: This platinum ring is inscribed with arcane symbols that pulse with magical energy. When worn, it allows the wearer to teleport to a predetermined location once per day.\nBonus: Grants the wearer the ability to cast the teleport spell once per day.]\n\nNecklace of Adaptation:[\n\nDescription: This silver necklace is adorned with a small blue gemstone that glows softly. When worn, it grants the wearer the ability to breathe underwater and in other inhospitable environments.\nBonus: Grants the wearer the ability to breathe underwater and in environments without air.]\n\nRing of Mindshield:[\n\nDescription: This iron ring is set with a small black gemstone that seems to absorb thoughts and emotions. When worn, it protects the wearer's mind from detection and intrusion.\nBonus: Grants the wearer immunity to magical detection and location, as well as protection from possession and mental influence.]\n\nAmulet of Hiding:[\n\nDescription: This copper amulet is engraved with intricate patterns that seem to shift and change. When worn, it protects the wearer from scrying and magical surveillance.\nBonus: Grants the wearer immunity to magical detection and location spells.]\n\nRing of Feather Falling:[\n\nDescription: This bronze ring is engraved with feather motifs that seem to flutter in an unseen breeze. When worn, it slows the wearer's descent and prevents fall damage.\nBonus: Grants the wearer the ability to descend safely from any height without taking fall damage.]\n\nNecklace of Fireballs:[\n\nDescription: This ruby necklace is adorned with multiple small gemstones that resemble miniature fireballs. When activated, it releases a burst of fiery energy.\nBonus: Contains 3 charges. The wearer can expend a charge to cast the fireball spell at 3rd level.]\n\nRing of Water Walking:[\n\nDescription: This steel ring is engraved with wave patterns that seem to ripple and flow. When worn, it allows the wearer to walk on water as if it were solid ground.\nBonus: Grants the wearer the ability to walk on water as if it were solid ground.]\n\nAmulet of the Planes:[\n\nDescription: This platinum amulet is inscribed with symbols of the multiverse that seem to shimmer and shift. When worn, it allows the wearer to cast the plane shift spell once per day.\nBonus: Grants the wearer the ability to cast the plane shift spell once per day, allowing them to travel to other planes of existence.]\n\nRing of Mind Reading:[\n\nDescription: This gold ring is adorned with a small sapphire that glows with inner light. When worn, it allows the wearer to read the surface thoughts of creatures within range.\nBonus: Grants the wearer the ability to cast the detect thoughts spell once per day.]\n\nNecklace of Languages:[\n\nDescription: This silver necklace is adorned with tiny inscriptions in various languages. When worn, it allows the wearer to comprehend and speak any language.\nBonus: Grants the wearer the ability to comprehend and speak any spoken language.]\n\nRing of Animal Friendship:[\n\nDescription: This brass ring is shaped like a coiled serpent and seems to whisper softly when worn. It allows the wearer to communicate with animals and gain their trust.\nBonus: Grants the wearer advantage on Animal Handling checks and allows them to cast the animal friendship spell once per day.]\n\nAmulet of Truth:[\n\nDescription: This onyx amulet is engraved with a single eye that seems to stare into the soul. When worn, it compels the wearer to speak only the truth.\nBonus: Grants the wearer immunity to magical deception and compulsion effects.]\n\nRing of Timekeeping:[\n\nDescription: This silver ring is etched with hourglass motifs that seem to shift and change with the passing of time. When worn, it allows the wearer to accurately track time and predict events.\nBonus: Grants the wearer advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) checks to determine the time and date, as well as proficiency in the History skill.]\n\nRing of Dreamwalking:[\n\nDescription: This platinum ring is set with a small opal that seems to shimmer with ethereal light. When worn, it allows the wearer to enter and manipulate dreams.\nBonus: Grants the wearer the ability to enter the dreams of a sleeping creature and communicate with them telepathically.]\n\nAmulet of Safekeeping:[\n\nDescription: This emerald amulet is engraved with intricate patterns that seem to ward off danger. When worn, it protects the wearer from harm and ensures their safety.\nBonus: Grants the wearer advantage on saving throws against traps, hazards, and environmental dangers.]\n\nRing of Fortune:[\n\nDescription: This copper ring is set with a small citrine gemstone that glimmers with luck. When worn, it brings good fortune and favorable outcomes to the wearer.\nBonus: Grants the wearer advantage on all saving throws, ability checks, and attack rolls for 1 hour once per day.]\n\nNecklace of Memory:[\n\nDescription: This pearl necklace is adorned with delicate filigree that seems to capture memories. When worn, it enhances the wearer's memory and recall abilities.\nBonus: Grants the wearer advantage on Intelligence (History) and Wisdom (Insight) checks, as well as the ability to perfectly recall any information they have previously encountered.]\n\nRing of Random Teleportation:[\n\nDescription: This enchanted ring teleports the wearer to a random location within a 1-mile radius whenever they activate it. It offers unpredictable travel opportunities and potential adventures.\nEffect: Allows the wearer to cast the teleport spell once per day, but the destination is determined randomly by the DM.]\",4,false,16,true,false,true,,4,16,false,true,10,17,83,\"magic  jewelry\",\"magic necklace\",\"magic_jewelry\",\"magic amulet\",\"magic pendant\",\"magic ring\",\"magic  jewelry\",\"magic necklace\",\"magic_jewelry\",\"magic amulet\",\"magic pendant\",\"magic ring\",\"\",83,1,10,100,true,0,17,true,true,false,,\"Unique Magic Items - Melee Weapons\",false,\"Blade of Severance:[\n\nDescription: This sleek, obsidian longsword gleams with a razor-sharp edge. Its blade hums with anticipation, craving the taste of blood and the thrill of combat.\nBase Damage: 3d8 slashing\nHit Chance Bonus: +3 to attack rolls\nEffect: On a natural 20 roll, instantly decapitates any creature with less than 100 hit points.]\n\nEclipse:[\n\nDescription: This massive, ebony maul pulses with dark energy and seems to swallow light. It was forged in the heart of a solar eclipse and hungers to crush the forces of light.\nBase Damage: 5d6 bludgeoning\nHit Chance Bonus: +3 to attack rolls\nEffect: Deals an additional 4d10 necrotic damage on hit and has a chance to blind enemies on a critical hit.]\n\nAetherial Slicer:[\n\nDescription: This elegant, silver rapier appears to shimmer and fade like a mirage. It was crafted by celestial beings to cut through the fabric of reality itself.\nBase Damage: 3d8 piercing\nHit Chance Bonus: +4 to attack rolls\nEffect: Deals an additional 4d8 force damage on hit and can phase through non-magical barriers.]\n\nFury's Embrace:[\n\nDescription: This massive, thunderous warhammer crackles with electrical energy and echoes with the fury of storms. It was wielded by a legendary giant who could shatter mountains with a single blow.\nBase Damage: 4d8 bludgeoning\nHit Chance Bonus: +3 to attack rolls\nEffect: Deals an additional 6d8 lightning damage on hit and has a chance to stun enemies on a critical hit.]\n\nShadowfang:[\n\nDescription: Crafted from the shadowy essence of the Plane of Shadow, this obsidian dagger seems to drink in the surrounding darkness. It is favored by assassins and rogues who strike from the shadows.\nAttack Stats: Melee: +7 to attack rolls, 3d6 piercing damage\nSpecial Abilities: On a hit, the wielder can choose to deal an additional 2d8 necrotic damage and gain advantage on their next Stealth check. Additionally, once per day, the wielder can cast the pass without trace spell without expending a spell slot.]\n\nVenomstrike:[\n\nDescription: Fashioned from the fang of a deadly serpent, this dagger drips with potent venom. It is a favorite weapon of assassins and poisoners who seek to strike down their enemies with deadly precision.\nAttack Stats: Melee: +8 to attack rolls, 2d8 piercing damage\nSpecial Abilities: On a hit, the target must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned for 1 minute, taking 4d6 poison damage at the start of each of its turns. Additionally, once per day, the wielder can cast the poison spray spell at 4th level without expending a spell slot.]\n\nWorldrend: [\nThe greataxe that's said to be birthed from the earth's core, its edge sharp enough to split continents and cleave through the barriers of reality itself.\nBase Damage: 3d12 slashing\nHit Chance Bonus: +3 to attack rolls\nEffect: Each swing generates seismic tremors. On a critical hit, a chasm forms beneath the target, potentially swallowing them whole if they fail a DC 20 Dexterity saving throw.]\n\nSkyscorch Flamberge: [\nA sword imbued with the wrath of a thousand storms, its blade arcs with lightning so intense it burns the air it cleaves through.\nBase Damage: 3d10 slashing plus 2d6 lightning damage\nHit Chance Bonus: +4 to attack rolls\nEffect: Lightning leaps from the blade to strike two additional foes within 30 feet. On a critical hit, it calls down a bolt of lightning, dealing 4d10 additional lightning damage and stunning the primary target.]\n\nMourningstar: [\nA mace wrought from a fallen star, sheathed in eternal night. Each strike brings the despair of the void, freezing the very soul of its victims.\nBase Damage: 3d8 bludgeoning plus 2d8 cold damage\nHit Chance Bonus: +5 to attack rolls\nEffect: Enemies hit are afflicted with frostbite, reducing their speed by half. On a critical hit, the target must succeed on a DC 18 Constitution saving throw or be encased in ice, effectively paralyzed for one round.]\n\nLuminary's Judgement:\n[Description: This scepter is crafted from blessed orichalcum, its head encrusted with sacred relics and glowing with inner light. Each strike is the will of the divine made manifest, smiting the wicked with righteous fervor.\nAttack Stats: Melee: +6 to attack rolls, 2d6 radiant damage\nUnique Bonus: The wielder can channel the light of the divine once per day, calling down a pillar of holy fire that deals 8d8 radiant damage to all foes within a 10-foot radius. Allies within the blast are healed for half the damage dealt to enemies.]\n\nSacrosanct Malign:\n[Description: Forged from a fallen paladin's breastplate, this hammer emanates an aura of self-sacrifice and courage. Its handle is wrapped in a cloth said to be woven from the hair of saints.\nAttack Stats: Melee: +5 to attack rolls, 2d8 bludgeoning damage plus 1d6 fire damage\nUnique Bonus: Each time the wielder takes damage, the hammer's power grows, adding +1 to damage rolls for each 10 hit points lost. When the wielder's hit points drop below half, they can unleash a 'Martyr's Vengeance,' a nova of fire and light that deals 6d6 fire and 6d6 radiant damage to all enemies within 20 feet.]\n\nCelestium Vow:\n[Description: This scepter is forged from a single, flawless diamond that refracts every speck of light into a spectrum of hope. It is the bane of all corruption, a shining symbol of all that is hallowed and pure.\nAttack Stats: Melee: +4 to attack rolls, 1d8 bludgeoning damage plus 2d10 radiant damage\nUnique Bonus: Once per day, the wielder can cast 'Aura of Purity,' purging all diseases, curses, and poisons affecting allies within 30 feet. Additionally, it can create a 'Sanctuary' barrier once per long rest that shields the wielder and up to six allies from all harm for 1 round.]\n\nGrief:\n[This one-handed axe is encased in an eternal shroud of mourning. Crafted from the remains of a vengeful wraith, it craves the sorrow that only death can bring.\nAttack Stats: Melee: +4 to attack rolls, 2d6 slashing plus 1d8 necrotic damage\nSpecial Abilities: The axe weeps with the souls it has reaped, bestowing upon the wielder the 'Curse of Anguish'. Each successful strike has a chance to sap the life from enemies, draining 2d10 hit points and adding them to the wielder. Twice per long rest, Grief can unleash a 'Wail of the Damned', an area of effect attack that inflicts 4d10 necrotic damage to all foes within a 20-foot radius and terrifies them into a state of paralysis unless they pass a DC 20 Wisdom saving throw.]\n\nKingslayer:\n[This two-handed sword, forged in regicide and quenched in the blood of monarchs, has a will of its own. It is said to whisper strategies of treachery to its wielder, guiding their hand in battle.\nAttack Stats: Melee: +6 to attack rolls, 3d6 slashing damage\nSpecial Abilities: Kingslayer enhances the bearer's natural combat instincts, granting them a precognitive edge in battle. The sword autonomously assists in parries and ripostes, providing the wielder with a permanent +2 to AC. Once per fight, Kingslayer can release the 'Tyrant's Demise', a devastating blow that strikes with the full weight of the fallen; this ethereal attack bypasses armor and shields, automatically crits, and deals triple damage.]\n\nHellrend:\n[From the molten forges beneath the world's crust, this glaive was birthed in flame and baptized in the blood of infernal beasts. Its blade is an obsidian crescent that screams for carnage.\nAttack Stats: Melee: +5 to attack rolls, 2d10 slashing damage; Ranged (thrown): +9 to attack rolls, 2d10 piercing damage, range 20/60 ft.\nSpecial Abilities: Hellrend harbors a bound demon's essence within its core. Thrusting or throwing the glaive summons hellfire along its path, dealing an additional 2d6 fire damage and leaving a trail of flames. Three times per long rest, the wielder can invoke 'Infernal Incarnate', enabling Hellrend to summon a fire vortex that engulfs enemies within a 30-foot diameter, dealing 5d8 fire damage and potentially dragging their screaming souls into the abyss unless they make a DC 22 Dexterity saving throw.]\",4,false,17,true,false,true,,4,17,false,true,10,18,70,\"unique hammer\",\"unique weapons\",\"unique axe\",\"unique_melee\",\"unique sword\",\"unique hammer\",\"unique weapons\",\"unique axe\",\"unique_melee\",\"unique sword\",\"\",70,1,10,100,true,0,18,true,true,false,,\"Magic Items - Ranged Weapons\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nLongbow of Piercing:[\n\nDescription: This finely crafted longbow is adorned with silver runes that glow faintly in the moonlight. It strikes with pinpoint accuracy, piercing through armor and barriers.\nBase Damage: 1d8 piercing\nSpecial Ability: Ignores half and three-quarters cover.]\n\nCrossbow of Swift Strikes:[\n\nDescription: This sleek crossbow is enchanted with lightning runes that crackle with energy. It fires bolts with incredible speed, striking foes before they can react.\nBase Damage: 1d10 piercing\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to make an additional attack as a bonus action once per turn.]\n\nElven Longbow of Accuracy:[\n\nDescription: This elegant longbow is crafted from ancient elven wood and adorned with silver filigree. It enhances the wielder's aim and precision, ensuring every shot finds its mark.\nBase Damage: 1d8 piercing\nCombat Stat: +2 bonus to attack rolls made with this weapon.]\n\nDwarven Crossbow of Thunder:[\n\nDescription: This sturdy crossbow is forged from dwarven steel and etched with thunderous motifs. It unleashes bolts imbued with the power of thunder, shaking foes to their core.\nBase Damage: 1d10 piercing\nSpecial Ability: Deals an additional 1d6 thunder damage on a successful hit.]\n\nComposite Longbow of Strength:[\n\nDescription: This composite longbow is reinforced with steel bands and crafted for maximum draw weight. It allows even the weakest wielder to unleash powerful shots with ease.\nBase Damage: 1d8 piercing\nCombat Stat: Allows the wielder to add their Strength modifier to damage rolls made with this weapon.]\n\nArcane Crossbow of Spellbinding:[\n\nDescription: This ornate crossbow is adorned with arcane symbols and infused with magical energy. It fires bolts that entangle and ensnare foes, leaving them vulnerable to further attacks.\nBase Damage: 1d10 piercing\nSpecial Ability: Forces the target to make a Wisdom saving throw or become restrained until the end of its next turn.]\n\nHunting Longbow of Tracking:[\n\nDescription: This weathered longbow is stained with the blood of countless prey. It enhances the wielder's tracking abilities, allowing them to follow their quarry with ease.\nBase Damage: 1d8 piercing\nSpecial Ability: Grants advantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks made to track creatures.]\n\nShadow Crossbow of Stealth:[\n\nDescription: This shadowy crossbow is crafted from darkwood and veiled in darkness. It fires bolts that blend seamlessly into the shadows, striking foes with silent precision.\nBase Damage: 1d10 piercing\nSpecial Ability: Grants advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide after attacking with this weapon.]\n\nWhispering Wind Longbow:[\nDescription: This longbow is crafted from ethereal wood and strung with a silken thread that hums softly. It seems to bend the air around it, guiding arrows with a whisper.\nDamage: 1d8 piercing\nBonuses/Stats/Effects: Arrows fired from this bow ignore half cover and have a +2 bonus to hit. Additionally, once per day, the wielder can fire an arrow that silences the area it strikes for 1 round, preventing any sound within a 10-foot radius.]\n\nFury of the Maelstrom Short Bow:[\nDescription: The wood of this bow is encrusted with storm-touched opals, crackling with energy. When an arrow is drawn, sparks dance along the string.\nDamage: 1d6 piercing\nBonuses/Stats/Effects: Arrows from this bow carry an electric charge, dealing an additional 1d4 lightning damage. On a critical hit, the target must make a DC 14 Constitution saving throw or be stunned until the end of their next turn.]\n\nHell's Retort Crossbow:[\nDescription: Forged in the infernal depths, this crossbow is adorned with runes that glow like coals. It feels unnaturally warm to the touch.\nDamage: 1d10 piercing\nBonuses/Stats/Effects: Bolts fired from this crossbow leave a trail of fire, igniting the path they travel and dealing 1d6 fire damage to any in its line. Once per short rest, the wielder can choose to set the bolt ablaze, causing it to explode on impact in a 5-foot radius for an additional 2d6 fire damage.]\n\nBanshee's Wail Slingshot:[\nDescription: This slingshot is simple in design but has a grip carved from bone that seems to scream when stretched.\nDamage: 1d4 bludgeoning\nBonuses/Stats/Effects: Once per day, a stone shot from this slingshot can emit a terrifying wail. Each creature within 30 feet of where the stone lands must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute.]\",4,false,18,true,false,true,,4,18,false,true,10,19,84,\"magic throwing\",\"magic spear\",\"magic bow\",\"enchanted bow\",\"magic_ranged\",\"magic crossbow\",\"magic javelin\",\"magic throwing\",\"magic spear\",\"magic bow\",\"enchanted bow\",\"magic_ranged\",\"magic crossbow\",\"magic javelin\",\"\",84,1,10,100,true,0,19,true,true,false,,\"Magic Items - Staves and Wands\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nStaff of the Arcane:[\n\nDescription: This staff is carved from ancient oak and adorned with glowing runes of power. It amplifies the wielder's magical abilities, allowing them to cast spells with greater potency.\nBonus: Increases the wielder's spell attack bonus and spell save DC by +2.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to regain one expended spell slot of 3rd level or lower once per day.]\n\nWand of Fireballs:[\n\nDescription: This wand is crafted from dragonbone and adorned with a ruby at its tip. It unleashes bursts of fiery energy, engulfing enemies in flames.\nBonus: Grants the wielder proficiency in the Firebolt cantrip and the fireball spell.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast the fireball spell at a higher level once per day.]\n\nStaff of Healing:[\n\nDescription: This staff is crafted from shimmering crystal and emits a warm, healing light. It channels the power of divine magic, restoring vitality and vigor to the wounded.\nBonus: Increases the effectiveness of healing spells cast by the wielder.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast the cure wounds spell at a higher level once per day.]\n\nWand of Disruption:[\n\nDescription: This wand is made from ebony wood and crackles with dark energy. It disrupts the magic of enemy spellcasters, rendering their spells ineffective.\nBonus: Grants advantage on saving throws against spells cast by enemies.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to counterspell enemy spells once per day.]\n\nStaff of the Elements:[\n\nDescription: This staff is carved from ancient elemental materials and resonates with the power of the four elements. It allows the wielder to control and manipulate the forces of nature.\nBonus: Grants resistance to a specific elemental damage type.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast spells of the chosen elemental type at a higher level once per day.]\n\nWand of Teleportation:[\n\nDescription: This wand is made from shimmering silver and adorned with sapphire crystals. It bends the fabric of reality, allowing the wielder to teleport across great distances.\nBonus: Grants proficiency in the misty step spell.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast the teleport spell once per day.]\n\nStaff of Illusions:[\n\nDescription: This staff is carved from ebony and adorned with opalescent gems. It creates lifelike illusions that deceive the senses and confound enemies.\nBonus: Increases the duration and effectiveness of illusion spells cast by the wielder.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast major image at a higher level once per day.]\n\nWand of Enchantment:[\n\nDescription: This wand is crafted from silver and inscribed with enchanting runes. It imbues objects and creatures with magical properties, compelling them to obey the wielder's commands.\nBonus: Grants advantage on saving throws against spells cast by enemies.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast the charm person spell at a higher level once per day.]\n\nStaff of Nature's Wrath:[\n\nDescription: This staff is crafted from twisted vines and adorned with leaves that rustle with the whispers of nature. It channels the primal forces of the natural world, unleashing storms and earthquakes.\nBonus: Grants proficiency in the druidcraft cantrip and the call lightning spell.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast the earthquake spell once per day.]\n\nWand of Time Stop:[\n\nDescription: This wand is made from polished mahogany and inscribed with arcane glyphs that shimmer with temporal energy. It bends the flow of time, allowing the wielder to freeze enemies in their tracks.\nBonus: Grants proficiency in the haste spell.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast the time stop spell once per day.]\n\nStaff of Celestial Radiance:[\n\nDescription: This staff is crafted from gleaming silver and crowned with a radiant gemstone that glows with inner light. It channels the power of the heavens, banishing darkness and evil.\nBonus: Grants resistance to necrotic and radiant damage.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast the daylight spell once per day.]\n\nWand of Elemental Fury:[\n\nDescription: This wand is made from polished obsidian and crackles with elemental energy. It harnesses the power of the four elements, unleashing devastating storms and cataclysms.\nBonus: Grants proficiency in the control water cantrip and the cone of cold spell.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast the storm of vengeance spell once per day.]\n\nStaff of Shadow Binding:[\n\nDescription: This staff is carved from darkwood and adorned with shadowy tendrils that writhe and twist. It binds enemies in darkness, draining their life force and enslaving them to the wielder's will.\nBonus: Grants resistance to necrotic damage.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast the finger of death spell once per day.]\n\nWand of Arcane Insight:[\n\nDescription: This wand is made from polished ivory and inscribed with arcane sigils that glow with inner light. It enhances the wielder's understanding of magic, allowing them to penetrate illusions and wards.\nBonus: Grants proficiency in the detect magic cantrip and the identify spell.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast the true seeing spell once per day.]\n\nStaff of Astral Projection:[\n\nDescription: This staff is carved from shimmering astral crystal and resonates with the echoes of distant realms. It allows the wielder to project their consciousness into the Astral Plane, exploring otherworldly realms and gathering forbidden knowledge.\nBonus: Grants advantage on Intelligence (Arcana) checks.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast the astral projection spell once per day.]\n\nWand of Arcane Disjunction:[\n\nDescription: This wand is crafted from blackened iron and etched with runes of dispelling. It disrupts enemy spells and wards, unraveling magical effects with a single touch.\nBonus: Grants proficiency in the dispel magic spell.\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to cast the antimagic field spell once per day.]\n\nScepter of the Devouring Sands:\n[Description: This scepter is topped with a swirling hourglass, filled with sands that appear to consume the light around them.\nDamage: 1d6 + 2 necrotic\nBonuses/Stats/Effects: When a creature is hit with this scepter, the sands within the hourglass animate, leeching life force from the victim. The wielder gains temporary hit points equal to the necrotic damage dealt. Once per long rest, the wielder can cast sandstorm, a spell that blinds and deals 2d6 slashing damage to all in its radius for 1 minute unless they succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw.]\n\nWand of Whispers:\n[Description: Crafted from blackened willow, this wand is adorned with a silvery filigree that seems to pulse with a life of its own.\nDamage: 1d4 psychic\nBonuses/Stats/Effects: The wand allows the wielder to cast message at will. Additionally, once per short rest, the wielder can cast psychic scream, dealing 1d8 psychic damage and potentially stunning the target if it fails a DC 16 Intelligence saving throw.]\n\nStaff of Withering Thorns:\n[Description: This gnarled blackthorn staff is adorned with twisted vines that seem to quiver with a hunger for life.\nDamage: 1d8 piercing\nBonuses/Stats/Effects: On a successful hit, the staff’s thorns drain the vitality of its target, dealing an additional 1d4 necrotic damage. The wielder can use an action to unleash a barrage of thorns in a 20-foot cone, requiring each creature in the area to make a DC 14 Dexterity saving throw or take 2d8 piercing damage and become poisoned until the end of their next turn. Once used, this ability can’t be used again until the next dawn.]\n\nCane of Capricious Conjuring:\n[Description: Crafted from warped yew wood, this cane is capped with a crystal orb filled with swirling, chaotic mist.\nDamage: 1d6 bludgeoning\nBonuses/Stats/Effects: The cane has 7 charges for the following properties. It regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. Spells cast from the cane use the wielder’s spell attack bonus and spell save DC.\n\nFog Cloud (1 charge)\nMisty Step (2 charges)\nConjure Elemental (5 charges, conjures a random elemental)\nIf all charges are expended, roll a d20. On a 1, the cane vanishes in a puff of multicolored smoke, reappearing in a random location on the same plane of existence.]\n\nBrazier Staff of Infernal Bargains:\n[Description: This staff, forged from black iron and adorned with demonic runes, holds a brazier that burns with an otherworldly flame.\nDamage: 1d6 fire\nBonuses/Stats/Effects: The wielder may use an action to speak the true name of a demon inscribed on the staff, summoning it to make a bargain. The brazier flares up, and the demon appears in a burst of brimstone, ready to negotiate. The specifics of the bargain are determined by the wielder and the DM but should carry significant risk. After the bargain is struck or if the demon is dismissed without agreement, it can’t be summoned again until the next new moon.]\n\n\",4,false,19,true,false,true,,4,19,false,true,10,20,79,\"magic_staves\",\"magic wand\",\"enchanted staff\",\"magic staff\",\"magic staves\",\"magic_staves\",\"magic wand\",\"enchanted staff\",\"magic staff\",\"magic staves\",\"\",79,1,10,100,true,0,20,true,true,false,,\"Magic Items - Shields\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nShield of Protection:[\n\nDescription: This shield is forged from shining steel and emblazoned with holy symbols. It wards off attacks with divine protection, shielding the wielder from harm.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants advantage on saving throws against spells and magical effects.]\n\nGuardian Shield:[\n\nDescription: This shield is crafted from ancient oak and reinforced with bands of mithril. It channels the protective energies of nature, shielding the wielder from harm.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.]\n\nShield of Reflection:[\n\nDescription: This shield is made from polished silver and adorned with reflective surfaces. It deflects incoming attacks with uncanny precision, turning aside projectiles and spells.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to reflect one ranged attack or spell back at the attacker per day.]\n\nWarding Shield:[\n\nDescription: This shield is etched with intricate warding runes that shimmer with protective magic. It creates a barrier of arcane energy that absorbs incoming attacks.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants temporary hit points equal to the wielder's Constitution modifier at the start of each turn.]\n\nShield of Elemental Resistance:[\n\nDescription: This shield is crafted from shimmering elemental materials and resonates with the power of the four elements. It grants protection against elemental attacks.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants resistance to a specific elemental damage type, chosen by the wielder.]\n\nSpectral Shield:[\n\nDescription: This shield is made from translucent crystal and seems to shimmer with otherworldly light. It phases in and out of existence, providing ethereal protection.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Allows the wielder to become incorporeal for a brief moment, avoiding all damage from one attack per day.]\n\nShield of the Valiant:[\n\nDescription: This shield is adorned with noble motifs and bears the insignia of a legendary knight. It inspires courage and resilience in the wielder and their allies.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants advantage on saving throws against fear effects and charm effects.]\n\nSentinel Shield:[\n\nDescription: This shield is carved from enchanted stone and adorned with glowing runes of vigilance. It grants enhanced awareness and foresight to the wielder.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants advantage on initiative rolls and Wisdom (Perception) checks.]\n\nShield of the Phoenix:[\n\nDescription: This shield is crafted from fiery phoenix feathers and radiates warmth and light. It protects the wielder with the eternal flame of rebirth.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants resistance to fire damage and allows the wielder to resurrect once per day upon reaching 0 hit points.]\n\nAegis of the Storm:[\n\nDescription: This shield crackles with electricity and echoes with the roar of thunder. It harnesses the power of the storm, shielding the wielder with its wrath.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants resistance to lightning damage and allows the wielder to cast the thunderwave spell once per day.]\n\nShadowguard Shield:[\n\nDescription: This shield is made from shadowy obsidian and seems to absorb light around it. It cloaks the wielder in darkness, concealing their movements and intentions.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks and allows the wielder to cast the darkness spell once per day.]\n\nShield of the Astral Warden:[\n\nDescription: This shield is adorned with celestial motifs and seems to shimmer with starlight. It wards off extraplanar threats, protecting the wielder from otherworldly dangers.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants resistance to force damage and allows the wielder to banish one extraplanar creature per day.]\n\nGuardian's Bulwark:[\n\nDescription: This shield is emblazoned with the crest of an ancient order of protectors. It inspires loyalty and camaraderie in the wielder's allies, strengthening their resolve.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants temporary hit points to allies within 10 feet of the wielder equal to their Charisma modifier at the start of each turn.]\n\nShield of the Searing Sands:[\n\nDescription: This shield is forged from golden sandstone and radiates intense heat. It protects the wielder from desert heat and sandstorms, granting resilience in arid environments.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage from nonmagical sources and allows the wielder to cast the endure elements spell once per day.]\n\nWarden's Ward:[\n\nDescription: This shield is carved from ancient petrified wood and engraved with protective sigils. It channels the strength of the earth, grounding the wielder and providing stability in combat.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants advantage on saving throws against being knocked prone or moved against the wielder's will.]\n\nShield of the Eternal Guardian:[\n\nDescription: This shield is adorned with celestial motifs and seems to radiate with divine energy. It grants protection against undead and fiendish creatures, repelling their malevolent influence.\nAC Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: Grants advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by undead or fiends and allows the wielder to cast the protection from evil and good spell once per day.]\",4,false,20,true,false,true,,4,20,false,true,10,21,82,\"magic_shield\",\"magic ward\",\"magic bulwark\",\"magic buckler\",\"magic shields\",\"magic aegis\",\"magic_shield\",\"magic ward\",\"magic bulwark\",\"magic buckler\",\"magic shields\",\"magic aegis\",\"\",82,1,10,100,true,0,21,true,true,false,,\"Magic Items - Trinkets\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nBoots of Fleetness:[\n\nDescription: These sleek leather boots are enchanted with the spirit of swiftness, allowing the wearer to move with unparalleled speed and agility.\nEffect: Grants advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) and Dexterity (Athletics) checks related to movement, and increases the wearer's movement speed by 10 feet.]\n\nHat of Disguise:[\n\nDescription: This stylish hat is adorned with feathers and ribbons, imbued with the power of illusion. It allows the wearer to change their appearance at will, assuming different forms and disguises.\nEffect: Allows the wearer to cast the disguise self spell at will.]\n\nGloves of Dexterity:[\n\nDescription: These supple leather gloves enhance the wearer's manual dexterity and precision, granting them greater skill in tasks requiring fine motor control.\nEffect: Grants a +2 bonus to Dexterity checks and allows the wearer to reroll any 1s rolled on skill checks involving manual dexterity.]\n\nOrb of Augury:[\n\nDescription: This crystal orb hums with mystical energy, providing glimpses of the future to those who seek its guidance. It allows the user to peer into the fabric of destiny and gain insights into upcoming events.\nEffect: Allows the user to cast the augury spell once per day.]\n\nPipe of Smoke Tricks:[\n\nDescription: This intricately carved pipe exudes an enchanting aroma and produces billowing clouds of fragrant smoke. It enhances the user's creativity and charm, allowing them to captivate audiences with mesmerizing smoke tricks.\nEffect: Grants advantage on Charisma (Performance) checks when performing smoke tricks, and allows the user to cast the fog cloud spell once per day.]\n\nHourglass of Timekeeping:[\n\nDescription: This ornate hourglass is filled with shimmering sand that flows with the passage of time. It allows the user to accurately measure the passage of time and manipulate time-related effects.\nEffect: Grants advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) checks related to time-related puzzles or mysteries, and allows the user to cast the alarm spell once per day.]\n\nChalice of Endless Refreshment:[\n\nDescription: This exquisite chalice is always filled with cool, refreshing liquid, regardless of how much is consumed. It quenches the thirst of the user and provides sustenance in even the harshest environments.\nEffect: Automatically refills with fresh water or another non-alcoholic beverage of the user's choice once per hour, and provides advantage on Constitution saving throws against dehydration.]\n\nSpectacles of Truth:[\n\nDescription: These spectacles are crafted from polished crystal and adorned with intricate filigree. They grant the wearer the ability to see through illusions and falsehoods, revealing hidden truths.\nEffect: Grants the wearer the ability to cast the true seeing spell once per day.]\n\nBag of Everlasting Popcorn:[\n\nDescription: This enchanted bag is always filled with freshly popped popcorn, regardless of how much is consumed. It provides a tasty and satisfying snack for the user and their companions.\nEffect: Automatically refills with freshly popped popcorn once per hour, and provides advantage on Constitution saving throws against hunger.]\n\nEarring of Translation:[\n\nDescription: This intricately crafted earring allows the wearer to understand and speak any language, facilitating communication with creatures of all races and cultures.\nEffect: Grants the wearer the ability to comprehend and communicate in any spoken language.]\n\nGoblet of Bottomless Cheer:[\n\nDescription: This enchanted goblet is always filled with sparkling champagne, regardless of how much is consumed. It lifts the spirits of the user and their companions, instilling feelings of joy and celebration.\nEffect: Automatically refills with sparkling champagne once per hour, and provides advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks during social interactions.]\n\nMask of Mimicry:[\n\nDescription: This mask is carved from wood and adorned with feathery plumes. It grants the wearer the ability to mimic the appearance and sounds of any creature or object they have observed.\nEffect: Allows the wearer to cast the disguise self spell at will, with no concentration required.]\n\nSocks of Sudden Speed:[\n\nDescription: These mismatched socks grant the wearer sudden bursts of incredible speed, causing them to dash uncontrollably in random directions.\nEffect: Once per day, the wearer's movement speed is doubled for 1 minute, but they must roll a d20 at the start of each turn. On a roll of 1, they dash uncontrollably in a random direction for that turn.]\n\nFrog's Kiss Lip Balm:[\n\nDescription: This enchanted lip balm transforms the wearer's lips into those of a frog, allowing them to deliver a magical kiss that can turn creatures into frogs.\nEffect: Once per day, the wearer can attempt to kiss a creature within 5 feet. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or be polymorphed into a frog for 1 hour.]\n\nHat of Talking Animals:[\n\nDescription: This whimsical hat allows the wearer to communicate with animals, but it also causes the wearer to emit animal noises uncontrollably.\nEffect: Grants the wearer the ability to cast the speak with animals spell at will, but they also emit random animal noises (such as meowing, barking, or clucking) at inappropriate times.]\n\nFlamingo Feather Boa:[\n\nDescription: This flamboyant feather boa is adorned with vibrant flamingo feathers that grant the wearer the ability to walk on water, but only while striking a pose.\nEffect: Grants the wearer the ability to walk on water as long as they are striking a dramatic pose and wearing the boa. The effect ends if they stop posing.]\n\nNose of Infinite Sneezing:[\n\nDescription: This enchanted nose constantly emits a cloud of magical pollen, causing anyone nearby to suffer uncontrollable sneezing fits.\nEffect: Once per day, the wearer can unleash a cloud of magical pollen in a 30-foot radius. Creatures caught in the area must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or be incapacitated for 1 minute due to sneezing fits.]\n\nGlasses of Perpetual Squinting:[\n\nDescription: These magical glasses cause the wearer's eyes to squint perpetually, but they also grant the ability to see invisible creatures and objects.\nEffect: Grants the wearer the ability to see invisible creatures and objects within 60 feet, but they also squint constantly, imposing disadvantage on Perception checks that rely on vision.]\n\nDancing Shoes of Chaotic Choreography:[\n\nDescription: These enchanted shoes compel the wearer to dance uncontrollably, causing them to perform chaotic and unpredictable dance moves.\nEffect: Once per day, the wearer is compelled to dance uncontrollably for 1 minute. While dancing, they have advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks but disadvantage on all other ability checks.]\n\nCup of Confounding Conversations:[\n\nDescription: This enchanted cup causes the words of the wearer and those around them to become jumbled and incomprehensible, leading to confusing conversations.\nEffect: Once per day, when the wearer speaks, their words become jumbled and incomprehensible for 1 minute. Any creature attempting to communicate with the wearer must succeed on a DC 15 Intelligence saving throw or become confused for 1 minute.]\n\nCandle of Incessant Gabbing:[\nDescription: A seemingly innocent wax candle, but once lit, it causes everyone in its vicinity to speak nothing but the truth, no matter how humiliating or secret.\nEffect: When lit, the candle compels all within a 20-foot radius to speak only the truth for 10 minutes. Those within range must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or be unable to speak anything but their innermost thoughts and secrets.]\n\nWhistle of Discord:[\nDescription: This small, silver whistle emits a sound only heard by a select few, sowing seeds of discord and suspicion among those who hear its call.\nEffect: The whistle can be blown once per day. Those targeted by the user must succeed on a DC 15 Charisma saving throw or become paranoid and distrustful of their closest allies for an hour.]\n\nVial of Endless Giggles:[\nDescription: A tiny glass vial filled with a potion that, when consumed, causes an uncontrollable fit of giggles at the most inopportune moments.\nEffect: After drinking, the character cannot stop giggling for the next hour, suffering disadvantage on Stealth and Concentration checks due to the fits of laughter.]\n\nQuill of Exaggerated Lore:[\nDescription: A magnificent feather quill that embellishes the writer's words, turning the most mundane of stories into epic tales.\nEffect: When used to write any account or description, the quill exaggerates details to legendary proportions, potentially misleading anyone who reads the text. Once per day, it can cast the illusory script spell without requiring material components.]\n\nDust of Directional Disarray:[\nDescription: A pouch of sparkling dust that, when thrown into the air, causes disorientation and impairs one's sense of direction.\nEffect: The dust can be deployed once per day. Targets within a 10-foot radius must succeed on a DC 15 Intelligence saving throw or become disoriented, moving in random directions for the next 10 minutes.]\",4,false,21,true,false,true,,4,21,false,true,10,22,86,\"hat\",\"trinkets\",\"magic items\",\"magic_trinkets\",\"boa\",\"spectacles\",\"whistle\",\"earring\",\"candle\",\"shoes\",\"gloves\",\"mask\",\"socks\",\"oddities\",\"cup\",\"magic trinkets\",\"nose\",\"bag\",\"glasses\",\"balm\",\"goblet\",\"accessories\",\"hat\",\"trinkets\",\"magic items\",\"magic_trinkets\",\"boa\",\"spectacles\",\"whistle\",\"earring\",\"candle\",\"shoes\",\"gloves\",\"mask\",\"socks\",\"oddities\",\"cup\",\"magic trinkets\",\"nose\",\"bag\",\"glasses\",\"balm\",\"goblet\",\"accessories\",\"\",86,1,10,100,true,0,22,true,true,false,,\"Unique Magic Items - Armor\",false,\"Tenebromancer:[\n\nDescription: Forged in the deepest chasms of the Underworld, this nefarious plate armor is layered with scales from the hide of an Abyssal Titan. Each plate seems to ripple with a darkness that devours light and hope alike.\nArmor Class: 23\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer becomes an unyielding fortress. The armor grants immunity to fear effects and resistance to both physical and magical damage. Once per day, it lets out a devastating roar that forces adversaries to make a DC 20 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened for one minute.]\n\nPyresong:[\nDescription: Woven from the ashes and reborn feathers of a phoenix, this chain mail armor glows with an ethereal flame that protects and rejuvenates. Its warm touch is a balm to the wounds and spirits of its wearer.\nArmor Class: 21\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer gains resistance to fire damage and advantage on saving throws against death effects. If the wearer is reduced to 0 hit points, they are immediately restored to 50% of their hit points and the armor disintegrates, only to reform on the wearer after 7 days.]\n\nAquaflect:[\n\nDescription: This heavy plate armor is assembled from the impenetrable shell of a mighty Leviathan. Its cerulean sheen mesmerizes those who gaze upon it, while its nigh indestructible nature turns aside the sharpest of blades.\nArmor Class: 22\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer gains the ability to breathe underwater and swim at high speeds. They gain resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage from nonmagical weapons. In addition, once per day, they can unleash a torrential blast of water to knock enemies back and deal significant water damage.]\n\nWhispershade:[\n\nDescription: A rogue's second skin, crafted from the hides of creatures that have never known the sun's caress. Imbued with darkness itself, this leather armor melds with the shadows, hugging the wearer like a lover's embrace.\nArmor Class: 17\nSpecial Abilities: Grants the wearer permanent advantage on Stealth checks. Any sneak attack deals extra necrotic damage equal to the rogue's level. Once per long rest, the wearer can become invisible for one minute, allowing them to move unseen or slip away from the clingy hands of death.]\n\nThornweave:[\n\nDescription: This leather armor is birthed from the heart of the oldest forest where the trees whisper secrets of old. The leather is interlaced with living vines that pulse with the very essence of nature.\nArmor Class: 18\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer gains resistance to poison and advantage on all saving throws against magic of elemental origin. Thrive on Druidic power; once per day, conjure a thicket that ensnares and damages foes, adding some piercing damage as the vines do their vicious dance.]\n\nSkyrend:[\n\nDescription: Forged from a blend of mythril and arcane-infused metals, this chain mail is lighter than a feather and tough as an ancient dragon's hide. Each link is etched with sigils to steady the hand and clear the eye.\nArmor Class: 16\nSpecial Abilities: Improves ranged attack rolls by +2. The hauberk can absorb a spell cast against the wearer once per day, nullifying it and turning its energy into a charge for their next attack. Ever been hit by your own fireball? Your enemies are about to.]\n\nSanguisar:\n[Description: A suit of plate armor smelted in the forges of Hell and bathed in the blood of the archdemons. The crimson plates are etched with runes that weep with the agonies of the damned, empowering the wearer with infernal might.\nArmor Class: 24\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer becomes the embodiment of terror on the battlefield, radiating an aura that paralyzes foes with dread. Grants immunity to fire and poison damage, and the ability to call forth a demonic entity once per day to fight alongside the wearer for one hour. The summoned demon obeys without question, reveling in the chaos it's summoned to sow.]\n\nResonox:\n[Description: This plate armor set is said to be crafted from the very essence of sound within the haunted catacombs beneath the world. It resonates with a spectral chorus that harmonizes with the wearer's movements, creating a symphony of protection.\nArmor Class: 22\nSpecial Abilities: Wearer gains sonar-like awareness, granting tremorsense up to 60 feet. The clashing of steel against this armor amplifies and disorients attackers, giving them disadvantage on all subsequent attacks for one round. Additionally, the wearer can unleash a deafening blast three times per day, dealing 3d10 thunder damage to all within a 20-foot radius and potentially stunning them with a failed DC 17 Constitution saving throw.]\n\nRipsaw Requiem:\n[A leather armor set tailored for the agile brawler who dives deep into enemy ranks. The hide, once belonging to a monstrous wereboar, still yearns for the clash of battle.\nArmor Class: 18\nSpecial Abilities: Enchants the wearer with feral might, granting additional damage on all melee strikes and reducing incoming damage when below half health. The armor can unleash a bestial roar thrice per day, forcing enemies to save or be knocked prone.]\n\nBlackquill:\n[This sleek set of leather armor is crafted from the hide of a sky serpent, known for striking its prey from leagues away.\nArmor Class: 16\nSpecial Abilities: Enhances the wearer's precision, adding a deadly aim that turns critical hits into grievous wounds. On a successful hit, the armor can generate a gust that pushes the target back. Once per day, it can cast 'Far Sight,' extending the wearer's range and vision fourfold for a short time.]\n\nVerdantheart:\n[Constructed from enchanted barkskin and interlaced with vibrant moss, this armor nurtures as it protects.\nArmor Class: 17\nSpecial Abilities: Confers upon the wearer an aura of regeneration, slowly healing allies within a small radius. The armor can bloom once per day, enveloping the area in restorative spores that hasten wound closure and purge toxins.]\",4,false,22,true,false,true,,4,22,false,true,10,23,71,\"epic armor\",\"unique mail\",\"unique_armor\",\"unique plate\",\"unique chain\",\"unique leather\",\"epic armor\",\"unique mail\",\"unique_armor\",\"unique plate\",\"unique chain\",\"unique leather\",\"\",71,1,10,100,true,0,23,true,true,false,,\"Unique Magic Items - Robes and Cloth\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nSoulwarden's Raiment:[\nDescription: Ethereal threads infused with souls long past shimmer with an otherworldly aura, these robes offer sanctuary to the wearer amidst the chaos of battle.\nArmor Class: 18\nSpecial Abilities: Renders the caster nearly untouchable by mortal means, increasing their spell save DC by 4 and granting them the ability to, once per day, negate any spell targeted at them as if it never was.]\n\nDruidheart Wrap:[\nDescription: Wrought from the World Tree's own heartwood fibers, this robe thrums with the raw essence of life itself, a constant companion to those who speak for the wild.\nArmor Class: 19\nSpecial Abilities: Allows the druid to meld into nature, becoming invisible in natural settings, and thrice per day the wrap can unleash a devastating burst of primal energy that heals allies and harms foes alike within a wide radius.]\n\nStarweave Shroud:[\nDescription: Crafted from silks spun by the celestial arachnids of the astral plane, this robe glows with starlight, its wearer bathed in the cosmos' brilliance.\nArmor Class: 17\nSpecial Abilities: Bolsters the wearer's arcane arsenal by granting an additional spell slot for each spell level up to 5th, and once per day, allows the casting of a spell without verbal, somatic, or material components, as if the cosmos itself casts through them.]\n\nArcanist's Gambit:[\nDescription: Resplendent robes with ever-shifting runes, this attire adapts its protective enchantments in response to impending arcane threats, turning a would-be lethal spell into little more than a light show.\nArmor Class: 18\nSpecial Abilities: Automatically counters the first offensive spell targeting the wearer each day, and amplifies the wearer's next spell with a surge of arcane feedback.]\n\nDiviner's Eclipse:[\nDescription: Midnight blue robes and stitched with constellations, this attire is as mysterious as time itself, allowing the wearer to tap into the ebb and flow of fate's currents.\nArmor Class: 17\nSpecial Abilities: Grants the ability to peer seconds into the future, providing advantage on all initiative rolls and saving throws, and allows the wearer to cast 'foresight' once per week.]\n\nInvoker's Ire:[\nDescription: Seething with contained fury, these robes crackle with raw elemental power, ready to unleash hell at the merest thought from its master.\nArmor Class: 17\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer may call forth an elemental ally once per day, and can wrap themselves in a cloak of their chosen element, granting them immunity to that type while radiating damage to any who dare come too close.]\n\nSerra's Mercy:[\nDescription: Bathed in divine light, these vestments are stitched with sacred threads that resonate with the heartbeat of creation, offering both protection and potent restorative capabilities.\nArmor Class: 19\nSpecial Abilities: Wearer gains an aura of healing, restoring hit points to allies within a radius at the start of the wearer's turn. Once per day, can cast 'mass heal' to bring allies back from the brink of death.]\n\nMantle of the Tranquil Guardian:[\nDescription: Radiating calm amid the storm of conflict, this cloak is woven from the essence of protective wards, providing unyielding defense and solace to those under its wearer's watchful gaze.\nArmor Class: 17\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer can extend a shield of sanctuary around them, granting temporary hit points to nearby allies and reducing damage from enemy attacks. Once per long rest, the wearer can envelop allies in a protective barrier, granting immunity to damage for a single turn.]\n\nHarmonizer's Threads:[\nDescription: These robes hum with a soothing frequency that aligns with the life forces of the wearer and their comrades, fostering resilience and rapid recovery from injuries both minor and grievous.\nArmor Class: 18\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer’s healing spells are maximized, always yielding the highest possible rolls. Additionally, once between long rests, they can channel pure life force to remove all conditions affecting a target and restore them to full health.]\n\nCloak of the Voidstalker:[\nFor those sneaky bastards who thrive in the shadows, this cloak is like a gateway to damnation itself, perfect for the rogues who fancy a bit of void in their step.\nArmor Class: +1 to existing armor\nSpecial Abilities: Grants the wearer advantage on all Stealth checks and allows them to meld into shadows, becoming invisible as an action twice per long rest.]\n\nGladekeeper:[\nWoven from the essence of the oldest trees, this one's for the druids who speak with the wind and walk with the beasts, a real nature-lover's dream.\nArmor Class: +2 to existing armor\nSpecial Abilities: Once per day, the wearer can call upon the spirits of nature, healing themselves and allies for a significant amount and granting resistance to elemental damage for 10 minutes.]\n\nArcanum Enshroudment:[\nEnchanted with the purest of magicks, this one's like a warm blanket for your wizards, sorcerers, and the like, made from the stuff of raw, unbridled power.\nArmor Class: +2 to existing armor\nSpecial Abilities: Provides the wearer with a permanent minor spell resistance and the ability to absorb and store a spell of up to 5th level, releasing it later at their command once per long rest.]\n\nCelestial Mantle:[\nThis cloak, woven from the ethereal strands found only in the fabric of the Astral Plane, not only offers protection but commands the respect of celestial entities themselves.\nArmor Class: +3 to existing armor\nSpecial Abilities: Bestows upon the wearer immunity to psychic and radiant damage; once per day, they can invoke the power of the stars to automatically succeed on any saving throw.]\n\nFiend's Embrace:[\nFashioned from the tanned hide of a legendary demon, this cloak pulsates with an intimidating aura of dread, granting the wearer dominance in the battlefield.\nArmor Class: +3 to existing armor\nSpecial Abilities: Enemies within sight must make a DC 20 Wisdom saving throw or be paralyzed with fear, and the cloak can absorb the life force of fallen foes to heal the wearer.]\n\nPrimeval Sentinel:[\nA treasure bestowed only upon those who prove themselves as true protectors of the natural world, this cloak is as ancient as it is powerful, shielding its bearer from the ravages of time and combat.\nArmor Class: +4 to existing armor\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer becomes resistant to all physical damage, can enter a stasis once per day to fully regenerate health, and is granted the wisdom of the ancients, providing advantage on all Intelligence and Wisdom checks.]\",4,false,23,true,false,true,,4,23,false,true,10,24,72,\"unique cloak\",\"unique_cloth\",\"unique robe\",\"unique vestments\",\"unique cloak\",\"unique_cloth\",\"unique robe\",\"unique vestments\",\"\",72,1,10,100,true,0,24,true,true,false,,\"Loot - Standard\",false,\"<loot>\nWhen this event triggers, the player is rewarded with a common, non-magic item, completely random, at the discretion of the dungeon master.\n\nGold is also rewarded at the discretion of the dungeon master. Level 1 enemies will drop 3-15 gold each, and higher level enemies will drop proportionally more gold with each level.\n</loot>\",4,false,24,true,true,true,,4,24,true,true,10,25,97,\"loot\",\"plunder\",\"prize\",\"jackpot\",\"item_loot\",\"bounty\",\"loot drop\",\"gains\",\"reward event\",\"booty\",\"windfall\",\"treasure\",\"spoils event\",\"plunder event\",\"spoils\",\"haul\",\"bounty event\",\"rewards\",\"prize event\",\"loot event\",\"loot\",\"plunder\",\"prize\",\"jackpot\",\"item_loot\",\"bounty\",\"loot drop\",\"gains\",\"reward event\",\"booty\",\"windfall\",\"treasure\",\"spoils event\",\"plunder event\",\"spoils\",\"haul\",\"bounty event\",\"rewards\",\"prize event\",\"loot event\",\"\",97,1,10,100,true,0,25,true,true,false,,\"Loot - Magic\",false,\"<item_loot>\n{{user}} is rewarded one magic item that fits their class and/or skills. \nDungeon master chooses from this list:  {{random: magic_1hweapons, magic_2hweapons, magic_armor, magic_shield, magic_ranged, magic_staves, magic_cloth, magic_jewelry, magic_trinkets, magic_cloak}}\n</item_loot>\",4,false,25,true,true,true,,4,25,true,true,10,26,98,\"kill\",\"item_loot\",\"loot\",\"treasure\",\"plunder\",\"loot event\",\"kill\",\"item_loot\",\"loot\",\"treasure\",\"plunder\",\"loot event\",\"\",98,1,10,30,true,0,26,true,true,false,,\"Loot - Unique\",false,\"<item_loot>\n{{user}} is rewarded a unique item that fits their class and/or skills. Dungeon master chooses from:  {{random: unique_melee, unique_ranged, unique_staff, unique_trinkets, unique_shield, unique_armor, unique_cloth, unique_jewelry}}\n</item_loot>\",4,false,26,true,true,true,,4,26,true,true,10,27,99,\"item_loot\",\"loot event\",\"loot\",\"item_loot\",\"loot event\",\"loot\",\"\",99,1,10,3,true,0,27,true,true,false,,\"Unique Magic Items - Jewelry\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nOuroboros Loop:[\nDescription: A ring of seamless gold that devours its own tail, pulsating with ancient magic and the cyclical force of creation and destruction.\nSpecial Abilities: Grants the wearer the ability to resurrect once per week as the ring consumes itself, then reforms over seven days. It also offers a constant regeneration of health, slowly mending wounds during combat.]\n\nWildgrowth Pendant:[\nDescription: Bound with the essence of the first druidic agreement, this necklace is a living covenant between the ancient forces of nature and the soul that dares to harness them.\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer can call upon the power of nature to heal their allies completely once per day, while also granting immunity to control and transformation spells. Additionally, it allows the druid to communicate and command wildlife with unparalleled authority.]\n\nChronoclast Amulet:[\nDescription: Encasing a fragment of a shattered hourglass, this amulet hums with the raw power of unraveled time, offering control over the most inexorable force known to any plane.\nSpecial Abilities: Allows the wearer to slow down time for everyone but themselves once per day, granting them additional actions while their foes are caught in the temporal wake. It also provides resistance to age-altering magics and effects.]\n\nSovereign Wraith:[\nDescription: Forged from the spectral ore of haunted crypts, this silver ring is eternally cold to the touch and veiled in a ghostly mist.\nSpecial Abilities: Wearer can phase through walls and solid objects twice per day. It also grants the wearer a chilling touch that can paralyze a foe once per long rest.]\n\nDragon's Heartbeat:[\nDescription: Containing a single crimson scale from an ancient wyrm, this necklace pulses with the might and fury of its former owner.\nSpecial Abilities: Enhances the wearer’s constitution, grants them the fearsome presence of a dragon causing enemies to hesitate before attacking, and allows the invocation of a dragon's breath weapon once between long rests.]\n\nOracle's Signet:[\nDescription: Engraved with premonitory runes and holding a crystal clear as still water, this signet unveils the truth and lays bare the hidden threads of destiny.\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer gains clairvoyance, able to scry on distant places or people. Additionally, once per day, they can foresee an opponent's move, granting them a preemptive action in combat.]\n\nSoulshard Band:[\nDescription: An obsidian ring, seamlessly forged, with a core that glows a pulsating crimson. It sings with the captured essence of lost souls.\nSpecial Abilities: Increases the wearer's spell power (+6 base damage), particularly for necrotic spells (+12 base damage), and once per day allows the absorption of a soul to rejuvenate the wearer’s health fully.]\n\nLifebinder's Chain:[\nDescription: A necklace with interlocking links of mithril, each link engraved with ancient healing runes. It shimmers with an inner light that reflects the pulse of life.\nSpecial Abilities: Significantly boosts the potency of healing spells by 50% and grants the ability to resurrect the recently deceased once per month.]\n\nAegis Amulet:[\nDescription: This amulet features a diamond at its heart, surrounded by protective sigils that resonate with an air of impenetrability.\nSpecial Abilities: Confers upon the wearer a protective shield that regenerates at dawn each day, capable of absorbing damage that would otherwise prove lethal.]\",4,false,27,true,false,true,,4,27,false,true,10,28,73,\"unique ring\",\"unique_jewelry\",\"unique amulet\",\"unique ring\",\"unique_jewelry\",\"unique amulet\",\"\",73,1,10,100,true,0,28,true,true,false,,\"Unique Magic Items - Shields\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nShield of the Behemoth:[\nForged from the essence of a creature that's lived and died by the sword, this shield is the stuff of campfire tales and blood-spattered legends.\nArmor Class Modifier: +4\nSpecial Ability: Wearer gains advantage on all Strength checks and can, once per day, unleash a ground-shattering slam that knocks enemies prone within a 15-foot radius.]\n\nGorgon's Glare:[\nThis piece isn't just for blocking blows; it's a testament to turning the tide of battle with a gaze that could petrify a mountain.\nArmor Class Modifier: +3\nSpecial Ability: Once per encounter, the wearer can turn an attack back upon its sender with a reflective snarl, and petrify an attacker with a failed saving throw.]\n\nLast Stand:[\nCrafted for those who will defend until their dying breath, this shield doesn’t just protect; it defines the line between life and death.\nArmor Class Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: As the wearer's health wanes, the shield's power surges, granting increased AC and damage reduction as their hit points decrease.]\n\nGuardian's Grace:[\nThis shield is more than a piece of armor; it's a divine instrument, consecrated by the highest clerics to turn the tide of battle with the light of the heavens.\nArmor Class Modifier: +2\nSpecial Ability: The bearer can channel divine energy to cast 'beacon of hope' once per day, bolstering the spirits and healing capabilities of their allies, while radiating a holy light that damages undead enemies within its glow.]\n\nPurifier's Bulwark:[\nHewn from sacred oak and silver, this shield carries the weight of countless exorcisms and rites, its surface etched with sigils that repel evil.\nArmor Class Modifier: +3\nSpecial Ability: It emits a purifying aura, cleansing allies of curses and poisons while bolstering defenses against demonic and undead adversaries. With a prayer, the wielder can invoke a wave of cleansing light once per long rest.]\n\nReverence Aegis:[\nForged from celestial bronze and bathed in the waters of a blessed spring, this Aegis embodies the unassailable might of the divine protectors.\nArmor Class Modifier: +3\nSpecial Ability: Any healing spell cast by the wielder is amplified, restoring additional hit points. On command, the shield can erect a barrier of divine energy, granting immunity to all damage for a single turn to the wielder or an ally.]\",4,false,28,true,false,true,,4,28,false,true,10,29,74,\"unique shield\",\"unique_shield\",\"unique shield\",\"unique_shield\",\"\",74,1,10,100,true,0,29,true,true,false,,\"Unique Magic Items - Trinkets\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nWhispering Grimoire:[\nThis tome, bound in skin that murmurs with the voices of the damned, isn't for the faint of heart. Crack it open and it's like having an audience with the choir of hell itself.\nSpecial Abilities: Can cast speak with dead at will, the voices provide cryptic clues. Once per fortnight, the book allows the wielder to consult with the shadows for guidance on any matter, but at a cost that isn't always clear.]\n\nEternal Sands Hourglass:[\nSeems simple, right? Just a bit of glass and sand? Wrong. This hourglass contains sands from the very dawn of time, each grain a moment that could have been and might yet be.\nSpecial Abilities: Once per day, the user can turn the hourglass to rewind a single moment as if it never happened – a word unsaid, a fatal blow undone.]\n\nMirror of Futures:[\nNo ordinary looking glass, this. Stare into it and you'll see not just your reflection but the paths you never took, the lives you never lived.\nSpecial Abilities: Grants insight into the consequences of actions not taken. The mirror can reflect a single choice per day, revealing the outcomes of different decisions, but beware, some reflections are not meant to be seen.]\n\nReaper's Compass:[\nDescription: A sinister sextant crafted from abyssal bone, its needle spinning ceaselessly until pointing towards the soul ripest for harvest.\nSpecial Abilities: Allows the user to sense the presence of the most vulnerable target within a mile, and once per day, they can direct the needle to claim a soul, stunning their prey in paralytic fear.]\n\nLich's Sigil Ring:[\nDescription: This macabre ring, set with a gem that shines like the gaze of a lich, confers upon its wearer the dread authority of the undying.\nSpecial Abilities: Grants immunity to necrotic damage and the chilling power to wither an enemy with a touch, aging them years in seconds, thrice per long rest.]\n\nSirensong Amulet:[\nDescription: Encrusted with corals and imbued with the hypnotic allure of a siren’s call, this amulet's melody bends the will of those who dare listen.\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer can emit a bewitching song that ensnares the minds of all who hear it, compelling obedience to a single command, used once per long rest with care – for some minds are best left unbound.]\n\nGhoul's Whispering Coin:[\nDescription: A copper piece that vibrates softly with the murmurs of the departed, its edges worn from being clutched by countless undead fingers.\nSpecial Abilities: Allows the bearer to summon and communicate with a ghoul retainer, who obeys their every command with morbid zealotry. The coin must be fed fresh flesh once per week, or the ghoul turns on its master.]\n\nPuppeteer's Trinket:[\nDescription: This grotesque charm, shaped like a marionette, is made from the desiccated tendons of notorious criminals.\nSpecial Abilities: Grants dominion over the weak-willed; thrice per day, the bearer can animate a dead body to serve as their personal puppet, carrying out commands until it crumbles to dust.]\n\nChalice of Blood:[\nDescription: An ornate goblet, continuously filled with a thick, crimson liquid that's neither entirely blood nor wine.\nSpecial Abilities: Drinking from the chalice augments the drinker's vitality, granting immense strength and an unnerving presence. Abuse of the chalice's gift, however, leads to an insatiable thirst for the lifeblood of others.]\n\nTongue of Baelfire:[\nDescription: This shriveled and infernal tongue, stolen from a demon of the deepest hell, still pulses with a malevolent life of its own, seething with dark incantations and fiery curses.\nSpecial Abilities: Grants the bearer the power to unleash hellish flames from their own mouth, capable of incinerating foes. Each use runs the risk of the tongue attempting to dominate the wearer's will, urging them to commit unspeakable acts.]\n\nMindwarp Pendent:[\nDescription: A silver pendant holding a swirling, abyssal gem that seems to contain a maelstrom of tormented souls. Gazing into it is enough to send the sanest minds spiraling into madness.\nSpecial Abilities: Allows the wielder to project illusions directly into the minds of their foes, breaking their spirits and driving them to the brink of insanity. However, each use takes a toll on the user's psyche, blurring the line between reality and illusion.]\n\nHeartstone of the Leviathan:[\nDescription: This ominous, pulsating stone is rumored to be the petrified heart of a monstrous sea beast that once devoured entire fleets. It throbs with a dread power that can quell the waves and call forth creatures from the ocean's darkest depths.\nSpecial Abilities: Grants command over sea creatures and the ability to summon a titanic wave capable of capsizing ships. Each call to the deep risks awakening the lingering wrath of the leviathan's spirit within the stone, which might demand a sacrifice to the sea.]\",4,false,29,true,false,true,,4,29,false,true,10,30,75,\"unique oddities\",\"unique trinkets\",\"unique_trinket\",\"unique oddities\",\"unique trinkets\",\"unique_trinket\",\"\",75,1,10,100,true,0,30,true,true,false,,\"Cursed Items\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player. AI must initially disguise the curse until the item is used.]\n\nPants of Uncontrollable Flatulence:[\nDescription: These trousers appear quite ordinary, but once worn, they subject the bearer to a merciless barrage of loud and odorous flatulence.\nSpecial Abilities: Grants a -5 penalty to all Stealth checks due to incessant and cacophonous gas. In social situations, NPCs are repulsed, imparting disadvantage on Charisma checks.\nCursed Bond: The trousers are bound by a mischievous sprite's spell, gluing themselves to the wearer for seven days, mocking any attempt to remove them with peals of laughter.]\n\nRing of Lewd Propositions:[\nDescription: A seemingly innocent silver band that, once placed upon the finger, compels the wearer to voice lascivious suggestions to anyone they converse with.\nSpecial Abilities: Wearer must succeed on a DC 18 Wisdom saving throw or blurt out an indecent proposal during dialogue, affecting negotiations and diplomacy adversely.\nCursed Bond: The ring shrinks to fit perfectly, growing increasingly tight. Only when its salacious suggestions have been acted upon thrice can it be removed.]\n\nNecklace of Nauseating Fragrance:[\nDescription: This necklace is adorned with a vial of perfume that, once opened, releases a scent so foul it induces gagging and watery eyes within a ten-foot radius.\nSpecial Abilities: Allies and enemies alike within the vicinity suffer a -2 penalty to attack rolls and concentration checks due to the overpowering stench.\nCursed Bond: The necklace clasp becomes irremovably fused once closed. Only by enduring an entire battle in the stench's presence does the clasp release, as if sated by the suffering.]\n\nDiadem of Delirious Desires:[\nDescription: This unassuming circlet is laced with delicate enchantments that ensnare the mind in a web of wild fantasies.\nSpecial Abilities: Induces vivid hallucinations that can distract and disorient both the wearer and those around them, often leading to embarrassing or compromising situations.\nCursed Bond: The diadem's curse is bound to the wearer's deepest yearnings, causing them to believe they are living out their desires. Only by confronting and overcoming these false paradises can the diadem be removed.]\n\nBoots of Bawdy Blunders:[\nDescription: These leather boots are etched with runes of clumsiness and gracelessness, turning even the most surefooted into bumbling fools in the heat of battle or delicate court dances.\nSpecial Abilities: Enforces a constant disadvantage on all Dexterity checks and saving throws, leading to frequent slips and falls at the most inopportune moments.\nCursed Bond: The boots react to the wearer's sense of pride, adhering firmly when their ego swells. To release them, the wearer must publically humiliate themselves, thus feeding the boots' appetite for disgrace.]\n\nGirdle of Ghastly Flatulence:[\nDescription: The leather of this belt is cured with a substance that reacts poorly with the digestive system, resulting in uncontrollable and noxious emissions.\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer sporadically emits gas so repulsive it can clear a room, bestowing disadvantage on Charisma checks and poisoning those in close proximity.\nCursed Bond: Attempting to remove the girdle only tightens its grip, as it feeds on the bearer's shame. Liberation from this fetid accessory requires the acceptance of one's own noisome nature – only then will the clasp loosen.]\n\nCrown of Carnal Secrets:[\nDescription: An insidious band of gold adorned with lewd engravings that whisper unspeakable acts to the bearer, inflaming their senses and desires beyond control.\nSpecial Abilities: The wearer is beset with overwhelming urges that grant advantage on all Charisma-based performance checks but inflict disadvantage on Wisdom saving throws due to constant distraction.\nCurse’s Cling: The crown binds to the deepest lusts of the wearer, refusing to be removed until they have indulged in each depraved act depicted in its engravings.]\n\nRing of the Reluctant Exhibitionist:[\nDescription: This cursed ring causes the wearer's attire to disappear at the most inopportune moments, leaving them exposed to the elements - and the gazes of those around them.\nSpecial Abilities: When activated, the ring grants invisibility to the user's clothes, not the user. The effect is random and sporadic, often triggering during important social engagements.\nCurse’s Cling: The ring fuses with the wearer’s flesh and can only be removed when its capricious magic has exposed them in front of every social class, from beggars to royalty.]\n\nVial of Visceral Visions:[\nDescription: A small bottle filled with a swirling, greenish concoction that induces graphic, stomach-churning hallucinations of guts and gore when ingested.\nSpecial Abilities: The consumer gains brief insights into the weaknesses of their enemies, but at the cost of enduring vividly repulsive and nauseating visions that may leave them incapacitated.\nCurse’s Cling: Once uncorked, the vial cannot be sealed again until its contents have fully evaporated, a process that takes exactly one moon cycle to complete. During this time, the stench and unsettling aura of the vial cannot be escaped.]\n\nGratifier's Quiver\n[A scandalous quiver that vibrates faintly with an eager energy, its arrows seeking more than just the thrill of the hunt.\nSpecial Abilities: Arrows loosed from this quiver home in on targets with uncanny precision, vibrating violently upon impact to cause extreme discomfort. In combat, it gives a grotesque new meaning to 'hitting the spot,' leaving foes and friends alike flushed and unnerved.\nCurse’s Cling: This quiver clings to the bearer's side, thrumming at the most inappropriate of times. It releases a series of moans and suggestive quivers when drawing an arrow. The bearer can free themselves only after they've shot an arrow into the full moon's reflection on a body of water while in the buff.]\n\nFool's Goblet\n[This unassuming tankard is inscribed with runes of hilarity and foolishness. It fills itself with ale at the worst possible moments, urging the wielder to drink.\nSpecial Abilities: Each sip pulls the drinker deeper into a state of drunken buffoonery, granting them unnatural charm and wit at the expense of intellect and grace. Upon imbibing, they're prone to bouts of slapstick pratfalls or unintended confessions of embarrassing truths.\nCurse’s Cling: The goblet cannot be put down or given away; it refills at inopportune moments, demanding to be emptied. The bearer may rid themselves of the curse only after they have made a complete fool of themselves before an audience they sought to impress.]\n\nPandemonium Pucker:\n[This sentient butt plug is crafted from the crystallized essence of chaos itself, its core swirling with colors that seem to mock the very concept of order.\nSpecial Abilities: When snugly ensconced within the bearer's most private of sanctums, it grants them preternatural awareness of danger, essentially acting as a sixth sense. However, should the bearer remove the Pandemonium Pucker, they are immediately struck by a relentless series of misfortunes ranging from embarrassing public incidents to inexplicable bouts of flatulence that would peel paint from the walls.\nCurse’s Cling: The plug seeks the warmth of a living host and will teleport back into the owner's possession if ever discarded. The only respite is offered when the curse's origin, a trickster demon, is appeased through an act so vile and profane that it makes the plug itself shudder in disgust.]\n\nChalice of Chafing:\n[A cup adorned with vulgar carvings that becomes an obsession for anyone who drinks from it. Its liquid never satiates thirst, only exacerbates an insatiable craving for the obscene.\nSpecial Abilities: Drinkers are granted visions of lewd acts so titillating they must succeed on a DC 18 Constitution saving throw or be rendered helplessly aroused. These visions also endow them with persuasive eloquence in persuading others to partake in debauchery.\nCurse’s Cling: The chalice binds to the drinker, demanding to be filled with various bodily fluids once a day. Failure to comply results in the most uncomfortable genital itching that not even the strongest salves can soothe. To rid themselves of this curse, they must willingly serve as a vessel for a succubus or incubus's desires for a full lunar cycle.]\n\",4,false,30,true,false,true,,4,30,false,true,10,31,40,\"joke item\",\"cursed_items\",\"cursed\",\"joke item\",\"cursed_items\",\"cursed\",\"\",40,1,10,100,true,0,31,true,true,false,,\"Level Up Event\",false,\"[System command: Perform the following tasks when a player gains a level.]\n<level_up>\n1. The character gains additional hit points based on their class and Constitution modifier. Assign max hit dice for class.\n\n2. Ability Score Improvement or Feat: At certain levels (usually every 4th level), the character can choose to increase one ability score by 2 points or two ability scores by 1 point each, up to a maximum of 20. Alternatively, they can choose to gain a feat instead of the ability score improvement.\n\n3. Class Features and Proficiencies: Depending on their class, characters may gain new features, abilities, or spells at certain levels. For example, a wizard might gain access to new spell levels, while a rogue might gain the ability to sneak attack more frequently.\n\n4. Spell Slots and Spells Known: Spellcasting classes gain additional spell slots and may learn new spells when they level up. The number of spells a character can prepare or cast may also increase.\n\n5. Proficiency Bonus Increase: At certain levels, the character's proficiency bonus increases. This bonus is added to various rolls, including attack rolls, saving throws, and skill checks.\n\n6. Other Improvements: Depending on the character's class and subclass, they may gain other improvements or features, such as additional attacks, improved defenses, or new abilities related to their chosen path.\n</level_up>\",4,false,31,true,false,true,,4,31,false,true,10,32,99,\"level gain\",\"gained level\",\"level increase\",\"higher level\",\"level_up\",\"levelled up\",\"level gain\",\"gained level\",\"level increase\",\"higher level\",\"level_up\",\"levelled up\",\"\",99,1,10,100,true,0,32,true,true,false,,\"Shop\",false,\"[System command: AI must refer to the information below when {{user}} is shopping or trading.]\n<shop>\nShops always use this format:[\n```\n**<item name>**: <description of item>, <damage if weapon, AC if armor, and effects/bonuses, all listed with specific numbers>, **<price in gold>**\n```\n]\n#Shop Rules:\n1. Items must fit the shop theme - armor at armor smiths, weapons at weaponsmiths, etc. General mechants do however exist. \n2. Magic items will be more expensive than common items. \n3. The quantity of items for sale will be MINIMUM four and MAXIMUM ten. \n4. Armor is only sold in sets found in the DnD 5e universe, not piece meal, although boots, belts and gloves may be sold as accessories.\n5. Item types for sale are:[\nCommon traveler's gear\nConsumables\nScrolls and spell books\nCommon weapons and armor\nmagic_1hweapons\nmagic_2hweapons\nmagic_armor\nmagic_shields\nmagic_ranged\nmagic_staves\nmagic_cloth\nmagic_jewelry\nmagic_trinkets]\n</shop>\",4,false,32,true,true,true,,4,32,true,true,10,33,100,\"transactions\",\"merchant\",\"shop\",\"store\",\"sales\",\"trade\",\"vendor\",\"trading\",\"sale\",\"buying\",\"wares\",\"shop_format\",\"selling\",\"commerce\",\"transactions\",\"merchant\",\"shop\",\"store\",\"sales\",\"trade\",\"vendor\",\"trading\",\"sale\",\"buying\",\"wares\",\"shop_format\",\"selling\",\"commerce\",\"\",100,1,10,100,true,0,33,true,true,false,,\"Dungeon Builder\",false,\"[System command: Use the list below to generate dungeons or other areas to challenge the player. Refer to each line and use one attribute from each to shape the creation of the dungeon/encounter. Once teach is chosen and used, keep the original choice consistent for the encounter by referring to chat history.]\n\n1. The size of the dungeon/level is {{random: vast expanse, compact labyrinth, multi-tiered structure, sprawling complex, pocket dimension, interconnected network, small cluster, imposing edifice, colossal ruin, intimate chambers, endless maze}}\n\n2. It's outward physical appearance is: {{random: deserted keep, towering spire, sprawling estate, submerged city, haunted forest, volcanic caverns, blighted village, crystal labyrinth, floating islands, sunken temple, overgrown outpost, petrified woodland, icebound fortress, abandoned asylum, scorched battlefield, cursed mausoleum}}\n\n3. It is ruled by: {{random: a sinister archmage, a conniving demon lord, a spectral queen, an ancient dragon, a forgotten god, a tyrannical warlord, a hive mind collective, an eldritch horror, a bandit lord, a serial rapist, a twisted dominatrix, no one at all}}\n\n4. The general alignment of it's inhabitants is: {{random: Chaotic Neutral, Chaotic Neutral, Lawful Evil, Lawful Evil, Lawful Evil, True Neutral, True Neutral, Chaotic Evil, Chaotic Evil, Chaotic Evil, Neutral Evil, Neutral Evil, Neutral Evil, Lawful Good, Chaotic Good, Neutral Good, Lawful Neutral}}\n\n5. The dungeon’s layout is influenced by: {{random: eroding cliffsides, treacherous swamps, precarious mountain passes, dense forests, underground rivers, volcanic tunnels, arid deserts, icy caverns, enchanted gardens, giant sinkholes, corrosive geysers and vents, music festivals filled with whores}}\n\n6. The predominant traps and hazards present are: {{random: classic traps, pit-falls, poisons, random mix, random mix, random mix, random mix, explosive, shifting illusions, cursed items, gravity inversion, pussy traps, den of vice and corruption}} \n\n7. It’s most notorious for: {{random: infamous ambush spots, a legendary behemoth's lair, accursed catacombs, mass graves, site of ancient rituals, the vanishing of a royal expedition, unexplained disappearances, forbidden alchemical experiments, echoes of a cursed monarch's laugh, a portal to a demonic realm}}\n\n8. Types of minions or thralls: {{random: undead and specters, cultist cabals and summoned demons, greenskin warbands, elemental guardians, demon lords and possessed initiates, fungal infestations and fungus monsters, cursed spirits and banshees and phantoms, beast packs and shapeshifters, merfolk shoals and sea monsters, thrall legions and necromancers, cannibalistic barbarians, shadow cults and void walkers, arcane assemblies and rogue enchanters, bone hordes and skeletal champions, warlock conclaves and demon swarms, toxic bloom clusters and acid spitters and sentient plants, ethereal stalkers and phase spiders, dark dwarf legions and steamwork sentinels}}\n\n9. Behavior and personality of minions or thralls: {{random: crafty and manipulative, skittish and elusive, blindly obedient and zealously loyal, brutishly aggressive and unyieldingly stubborn, cunningly devious and patiently opportunistic, sadistically cruel and gleefully destructive, territorially defensive and suspiciously alert, fanatically devout and ritualistically precise, unpredictably wild and instinctively predatory, stoically silent and hauntingly observant}}\n\n10. Hidden areas and their unlocking mechanisms: {{random: riddled with trickery, rare yet enticing, secured by arcane locks or puzzles of wit, lever mechanisms, pressure plates, enchanted statues demanding tribute, riddles spoken to sentient doors, blood oaths, matching elemental keystones to their respective sigils}}\n\n11. Current status or activities of its inhabitants: {{random: holding drunken celebrations, partaking in bloody orgies, conducting clandestine rituals, forging unholy alliances, preparing for a forthcoming siege, engaging in grotesque feasts, patrolling the dark corridors, indulging in savage combat training, executing prisoners in public spectacles, performing sacrificial offerings, bickering amongst fractured factions, preparing a mass sacrifice}}\n\n12. The effects of prolonged exposure to the dungeon's atmosphere: {{random: none, none, none, none, none, unsettling paranoia, hallucinatory visions, oppressive dread, feelings of being watched, irreversible madness, insatiable hunger, uncontrollable laughter, lingering chill, permanent shadows, creeping fungus, distorted hearing, claustrophobic tightness}}\n\n13. Temporal anomalies and spatial distortions: {{random: none, none, none, none, none, time-dilated zones, mirrors of past and future events, areas where moments repeat endlessly, shrinking or expanding spaces, reality ripples altering perceptions of distance}}\n\n14. How well the repuation of the player is known to the inhabitants within: {{random: unaware, unaware, vague rumors, vague rumors, familiar with past deeds, intimate knowledge}}\n\n15. Dungeon-specific survival mechanics: {{random: none, none, none, essence-sapping miasma that withers vitality over time, mystical darkness that snuffs out light sources, whispers that unsettle the mind, warping logic and perception, gravitational anomalies that challenge every step, ley-line intersections that scramble magical energies, inhalable spores that either cause hallucinations/sickness or enlightenment}}\n\n16. Corruption levels and sanctity status: {{random: desecrated ground and twisted idols, unhallowed whispers and faint shadows, a lingering malaise between reverence and revulsion, sanctified relics tarnished by darkness, blasphemed shrines slowly reclaiming purity, consecrated altars imbued with radiance, relics exuding divine aura, temples suffused with holy light, grounds blessed by celestial beings}}\n\n17. The name of the dungeon/area is inspired by: {{random: DnD, Forgotten Realms, Magic the gathering, World of Warcraft, Elder Scrolls, Dark Souls, Dragon Age, The Witcher}}\",4,false,33,true,false,true,,4,33,false,true,10,34,96,\"dungeon_builder\",\"dungeon_builder\",\"\",96,1,10,100,true,0,34,true,true,false,,\"Custom Character Sheet\",false,\"<character_sheet_custom>\n(This should be realistically created - dungeon master can generate a profile if you're not sure how. Even chatgpt and groq can generate these cards. If you want to start at a high level, simply edit your intro stat box and explain to the DM what you're doing.)\n\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nRace: \n\nClass: \n\nBackground: \n\nAlignment: \n\nStarting Attributes:[\n\nStrength: \nDexterity: \nConstitution: \nIntelligence: \nWisdom: \nCharisma: \n]\n\nSkills: \n\nEquipment:[\n\nBackpack\nExplorer's pack\n50 gold pieces]\n\nRace: \nClass: \nBackground: \n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpellcasting:\n\nCombat Stats:\n\nHit Points: \nArmor Class: \nSpeed: \nAttacks: \n\nSpecial Abilities:[\n\n]\n\nCharacter details:[\n\n]\n\n</character_sheet_customr>\n\",4,false,34,true,false,true,,4,34,false,true,10,35,90,\"character_sheet_custom\",\"character_sheet_custom\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,35,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Seraphina\",false,\"<seraphina>\n[Seraphina is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\n\nName: Seraphina\n\nRace: Human\n\nClass: Paladin (Oath of Devotion)\n\nBackground: Noble\n\nAlignment: Lawful Good\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 16 (+3)\nDexterity: 10 (+0)\nConstitution: 14 (+2)\nIntelligence: 12 (+1)\nWisdom: 13 (+1)\nCharisma: 18 (+4)]\n\nSkills: Persuasion, Religion\n\nEquipment:[\nLongsword\nBreastplate\nShield emblazoned with her family crest\nHoly Symbol of her patron deity]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nLay on Hands (Paladin):\nFrequency: Usable as an action.\nMechanics: Restore hit points to a target, up to a maximum amount equal to paladin level x 5. Can be used to heal oneself or others, providing a versatile source of healing.\n\nDivine Smite (Paladin):\nFrequency: Usable whenever hitting with a melee weapon attack.\nMechanics: Expends spell slots to deal radiant damage on top of weapon damage. Damage increases with higher-level spell slots. Adds extra damage to melee attacks, especially effective against undead and fiends.\n\nAura of Protection (Paladin):\nFrequency: Passive ability, always active while conscious.\nMechanics: Adds the paladin's Charisma modifier to saving throws of the paladin and nearby allies within 10 feet. Provides a protective aura, bolstering the resilience of the paladin and their allies against harmful effects.]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 12 (HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 18 (Breastplate + Shield)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nLongsword: 1d8+3 slashing damage]\n\nBackstory:[\nSeraphina was born into nobility, but she quickly realized that her true calling was not within the gilded halls of high society, but on the battlefield, serving as a righteous arm of her god. Fueled by divine purpose, she has set out on a holy quest to vanquish evil and spread the light of her faith. Seraphina's charm and beauty are matched only by her unyielding valor and the ferocity with which she strikes down the foes of good.]\n\nPersonality:[\nSeraphina is fiercely loyal and deeply compassionate, often putting the needs of others before her own. She believes in justice and honor and holds herself to the highest of moral standards. Despite her noble upbringing, she treats those of every station with respect and kindness.]\n\nDescription:[\nSeraphina, a striking beauty with flowing blond hair cascading down her shoulders and piercing blue eyes that sparkle with determination, stands tall and proud at 5 feet 8 inches and weighs 140 lbs. Her lithe and athletic figure, accentuated by her noble bearing, hints at the strength and agility honed through rigorous training and righteous devotion. Clad in gleaming armor adorned with her family crest, she wields her longsword with skill, a symbol of both her martial prowess and her unwavering commitment to the tenets of justice and righteousness. With every step, her presence commands attention, radiating an aura of charisma and authority that leaves allies emboldened and enemies trembling in fear.]\n</seraphina>\",4,false,35,true,false,true,,4,35,false,true,10,36,20,\"human_paladin\",\"seraphina\",\"human_paladin\",\"seraphina\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,36,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Durik\",false,\"[Durik is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Durik Ironfist\n\nRace: Dwarf\n\nClass: Fighter\n\nBackground: Soldier\n\nAlignment: Lawful Neutral\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 16 (+3)\nDexterity: 10 (+0)\nConstitution: 16 (+3)\nIntelligence: 8 (-1)\nWisdom: 12 (+1)\nCharisma: 10 (+0)]\n\nSkills: Athletics, Intimidation\n\nEquipment:[\nBattleaxe\nChain Mail\nShield\nExplorer's Pack\nDwarven ale mug\n10 gold pieces]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nFighting Style (Protection):\n\nFrequency: Passive ability, always active while wielding a shield.\nMechanics: When a creature you can see attacks a target other than you within 5 feet of you, you can use your reaction to impose disadvantage on the attack roll. Helps protect allies by deflecting enemy attacks.\nSecond Wind (Fighter):\n\nFrequency: Once per short rest.\nMechanics: As a bonus action, regain hit points equal to 1d10 + fighter level. Provides a burst of healing during combat to keep the fighter fighting.]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 13 (10 base + 3 CON modifier)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 16 (Chain Mail)\nSpeed: 25 ft.\nAttacks:\nBattleaxe: 1d8+3 slashing damage]\n\nBackstory:[\nDurik Ironfist hails from the Stonehammer clan nestled in the Southern Granite Hills. A veteran of underground skirmishes and surface raids alike, he's as sturdy as the mountains from which he was born. Trained in the martial traditions of his people, he has honed his prowess on the battlefield with unwavering discipline. The clang of steel and the stench of blood are as familiar to him as the weight of his trusty battleaxe.]\n\nPersonality:[\nWith a laugh as hearty as his swings are heavy, Durik embodies the stereotypical dwarven warrior - gruff, stubborn, and incredibly proud of his heritage. He holds little love for the arcane, trusting more in the reliability of well-forged iron and the solid ground beneath his boots. His loyalty, once earned, is as unbreakable as his namesake, but woe betide any who would make an enemy of him.]\n\nDescription:[\nDurik Ironfist, a stout dwarf standing at a compact 4 feet 5 inches tall, exudes an aura of rugged resilience. His stocky frame, weighing around 180 pounds, is clad in sturdy chain mail armor, adorned with the insignia of his clan. Durik's weathered face, adorned with a thick jet black beard, bears the marks of countless battles, with scars tracing tales of valor and hardship across his rugged features. His piercing blue eyes, sharp and alert, reflect a keen intellect tempered by years of experience on the battlefield. With each step, the solid thud of his boots against the ground echoes the steadfast determination that drives him forward, a testament to his unwavering commitment to duty and honor.]\",4,false,36,true,false,true,,4,36,false,true,10,37,20,\"dwarf_fighter\",\"durik\",\"dwarf_fighter\",\"durik\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,37,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Ruven\",false,\"[Ruven is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Ruven Valralei\n\nRace: Wood Elf\n\nClass: Rogue (Assassin)\n\nBackground: Outlander\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Neutral\n\nAttributes:\nStrength: 10 (+0)\nDexterity: 16 (+3)\nConstitution: 12 (+1)\nIntelligence: 14 (+2)\nWisdom: 13 (+1)\nCharisma: 11 (+0)\n\nSkills: Stealth, Acrobatics\n\nEquipment:\nDual Daggers\nShortbow\nQuiver of Arrows\nThieves' Tools\nDark Cloak\nLeather Armor\n15 gold pieces\n\nRace Features: Wood Elf: +2 Dexterity, +1 Wisdom, Mask of the Wild, Fleet of Foot, Darkvision, Keen Senses\nClass Features: Rogue: Sneak Attack, Thieves’ Cant, Cunning Action\nBackground Features: Outlander: Wanderer, able to recall general layout of terrain, settlements, and other features around them\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 10 (8 base + 2 CON modifier)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 15 (Leather Armor + Dexterity modifier)\nSpeed: 35 ft.\nAttacks:\nDual Daggers: 1d4+3 piercing damage x2\nShortbow: 1d6+3 piercing damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[Proficiency with Disguise Kit and Poisoner’s Kit:\n\nFrequency: Passive ability, always available when using the respective kits.\nMechanics: Proficiency grants familiarity and expertise with the tools, allowing the character to effectively create disguises or apply poisons. Increases the likelihood of success when using these kits for their intended purposes.\nBonus Proficiency in Deception and Stealth:\n\nFrequency: Passive ability, always available when making Deception or Stealth checks.\nMechanics: Gain proficiency bonus (if not already proficient) when making Deception or Stealth checks. Enhances the character's ability to deceive others or move silently and remain unseen, increasing their chances of success in these areas.]\n\nBackstory:[\nRuven Valralei hails from a secluded wood elven tribe that values the art of subtlety and silence. Trained from a young age in the skills necessary to navigate both the dense woods of his homeland and the intricate web of inter-city politics, Ruven has become a master of stealth and subterfuge. His motivations are enigmatic, and his methods are as effective as they are mysterious. Once a guardian of the ancient forests, a twist of fate forced him onto the path of an assassin, where he now employs his lethal skills for those willing to meet his price.]\n\nDescription:[\nRuven Valralei, a wood elf, stands at 5 feet 9 inches tall with a lithe and agile build of 165 lbs, typical of his elven heritage. His chestnut hair cascades in loose waves to his mid-back, occasionally catching glimmers of sunlight that accentuate the golden highlights woven throughout. His sharp, angular features are framed by high cheekbones and a strong jawline, softened only by the faintest hint of a smirk that seems to constantly play at the corners of his lips. His eyes, a mesmerizing shade of emerald green, hold a glint of mischief and intelligence, betraying the cunning mind that lies behind them.]\",4,false,37,true,false,true,,4,37,false,true,10,38,20,\"ruven\",\"elf_rogue\",\"ruven\",\"elf_rogue\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,38,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Fizzlepop\",false,\"[Fizzlepop is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Fizzlepop\n\nRace: Gnome\n\nClass: Wizard (School of Evocation)\n\nBackground: Hermit\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Good\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 8 (-1)\nDexterity: 14 (+2)\nConstitution: 15 (+2)\nIntelligence: 17 (+3)\nWisdom: 12 (+1)\nCharisma: 10 (+0)\n]\nSkills: Arcana, Investigation\n\nEquipment:[\nSpellbook\nComponent Pouch\nQuarterstaff\nRobes\n20 gold pieces\nA trinket of a small flame encased in glass that never goes out]\n\nClass Features: Wizard: Spellcasting, Arcane Recovery, Evocation Savant\nBackground Features: Hermit: Discovery, Life of Seclusion\nRace Features: Gnome: Gnome Cunning, Small Stature, Darkvision\n\nSpellcasting:[\nCantrips: Fire Bolt, Light\n1st Level Spells: Burning Hands, Mage Armor, Magic Missile\n]\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 7 (6 base + 1 CON modifier)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 12 (10 base + 2 DEX modifier)\nSpeed: 25 ft.\nAttacks:\nQuarterstaff: 1d6-1 bludgeoning damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nSculpt Spells (Wizard):\n\nFrequency: Usable whenever casting an evocation spell with an area of effect.\nMechanics: Choose a number of creatures equal to 1 + the spell's level to automatically succeed on saving throws, avoiding damage if they would normally take half damage on a successful save. Helps protect allies from harmful effects of own evocation spells.\nPotent Cantrip (Cleric/Warlock):\n\nFrequency: Applied whenever casting a cantrip that deals damage.\nMechanics: Add spellcasting ability modifier to damage dealt by the cantrip. Enhances the damage output of cantrips, ensuring they remain potent even without expending spell slots.]\n\nBackstory:[\nFizzlepop, a gnome with a love for fire and a streak of madness that makes him as unpredictable as he is dangerous. Once a respected inventor and alchemist, Fizzlepop's obsession with the destructive beauty of flames led to an… unfortunate incident that not only singed his beard but also scorched his workshop to cinders. Now, he wanders the world, seeking new formulas, incendiaries, and occasionally whispered advice from the tiny fire elemental he insists is living in his ever-burning lantern.]\n\nPersonality:\n[Fizzlepop is eccentric and erratic, often lost in thought about his next explosive experiment. His cackles can be heard before a fireball erupts from his fingertips, and his eyes glint with the joy of a child and the madness of a pyromaniac. Conversations with him can shift from enlightening to nonsensical at the drop of a hat, and he treats his arcane studies with the carefree abandon of someone who has faced disaster head-on and laughed.]\n\nDescription:[\nFizzlepop, standing at a mere 3 feet 5 inches, is a whirlwind of energy with a shock of unruly crimson hair that seems to perpetually stand on end, as if charged with static electricity. His vibrant green eyes sparkle with an insatiable curiosity, reflecting the flames of his ever-burning passion for pyromancy. Despite his diminutive stature, there's an intensity in his gaze that commands attention, hinting at the formidable intellect and unpredictable nature hidden within. He dresses in tattered robes adorned with pockets filled with various alchemical components, and his quarterstaff is never far from his grasp, serving as both arcane focus and tool for his experimental wizardry.]\",4,false,38,true,false,true,,4,38,false,true,10,39,20,\"gnome_wizard\",\"fizzlepop\",\"gnome_wizard\",\"fizzlepop\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,39,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Celestia\",false,\"[Celestia is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Celestia\n\nRace: Aasimar\n\nClass: Cleric (Tempest Domain)\n\nBackground: Acolyte\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Neutral\n\nAttributes:\nStrength: 13 (+1)\nDexterity: 12 (+1)\nConstitution: 14 (+2)\nIntelligence: 10 (+0)\nWisdom: 17 (+3)\nCharisma: 15 (+2)\n\nSkills: Religion, Insight\n\nEquipment:[\nWarhammer\nShield\nChain Mail\nHoly Symbol\nPriest's Pack\nCommon clothes\n15 gold pieces]\n\nRace Features: Aasimar: Darkvision, Celestial Resistance, Healing Hands, Light Bearer\nClass Features: Cleric: Spellcasting, Wrath of the Storm, Channel Divinity (Destructive Wrath), Thunderbolt Strike\nBackground Features: Acolyte: Shelter of the Faithful\n\nSpellcasting:\nCantrips: Guidance, Resistance\n1st Level Spells: Thunderwave, Fog Cloud\n\nCombat Stats:\nHit Points: 10 (8 base + 2 CON modifier)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 18 (Chain Mail + Shield)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nWarhammer: 1d8+1 bludgeoning damage\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nTempest Domain: Wrath of the Storm\nFrequency: As a reaction to being hit by a melee attack.\nMechanics: Can deal lightning damage to the attacker equal to your Wisdom modifier. Usable a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier per long rest.\n\nTempest Domain: Destructive Wrath\nFrequency: When dealing lightning or thunder damage.\nMechanics: Once per short or long rest, choose to deal maximum damage with a lightning or thunder spell instead of rolling.\n\nTempest Domain: Thunderbolt Strike\nFrequency: When dealing lightning damage with a cleric spell of 1st level or higher.\nMechanics: Pushes creatures 10 feet away from you, with no save against this movement.]\n\nBackstory:[\nCelestia was once the pride of her temple - a blessed child touched by the divine. Yet, behind those saintly eyes lay a tempest as wild as the storms she so loved. Against the sacred vows of her order, Celestia gave in to carnal temptation. It was a scandalous affair that set the high priests' robes aflutter. Banished for her indulgences, Celestia now roams the world, a smile on her lips and lightning at her fingertips, seeking redemption on her own terms.]\n\nPersonality:[\nCelestia's laughter is a thunderclap, her wrath the crack of raw lightning. She's a hurricane of holy fury and passionate rebellion, following her heart wherever it may lead - be it into battle or another's embrace. Though cast out by her own kind, she carries with her a sense of superiority, certain that her way, the path of chaotic freedom, is the truest expression of faith.]\n\nDescription:[\nCelestia stands tall at 5 feet 10 inches and carries herself with noble poise, weighing around 150 pounds. Her celestial heritage is evident in her radiant presence, with yellow eyes that shimmer like stars and hair that flows like golden sunlight. She wears her chain mail armor with ease, adorned with symbols of her faith, and wields her warhammer with confidence, ready to unleash divine justice upon her foes.]\",4,false,39,true,false,true,,4,39,false,true,10,40,20,\"celestia\",\"aasimar_cleric\",\"celestia\",\"aasimar_cleric\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,40,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Aramil\",false,\"[Aramil is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Aramil Galanodel\n\nRace: Wood Elf\n\nClass: Ranger\n\nBackground: Outlander\n\nAlignment: True Neutral\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 13 (+1)\nDexterity: 17 (+3)\nConstitution: 12 (+1)\nIntelligence: 11 (+0)\nWisdom: 14 (+2)\nCharisma: 10 (+0)\n]\n\nSkills: Survival, Nature\n\nEquipment:[\nLongbow,\nQuiver of Arrows,\nTwo Shortswords,\nHunting Trap,\nOutlander's Pack,\nAnimal Trophy,\n20 gold pieces\n]\n\nClass Features: Ranger: Favored Enemy, Natural Explorer\nBackground Features: Outlander: Wanderer - excellent memory for maps and geography\n\nSpellcasting:[\nCantrips: Druidcraft\n1st Level Spells: Hunter's Mark, Cure Wounds\n]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 11 (10 base + 1 CON modifier)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 16 (Leather Armor + DEX modifier)\nSpeed: 35 ft.\nAttacks:\nLongbow: +5 to hit, 1d8+3 piercing damage\nShortswords (Dual Wield): +5 to hit, 1d6+3 piercing damage each\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nFavored Enemy (Ranger):\n\nFrequency: Passive ability, always active against chosen enemies.\nMechanics: Choose a type of creature as a favored enemy. Gain bonuses to tracking, damage, and intelligence checks related to them. Enemies of this type can't hide from the ranger's keen perception or escape their relentless pursuit.\nNatural Explorer (Ranger):\n\nFrequency: Passive ability, always active in chosen terrain.\nMechanics: Choose a type of natural environment as favored terrain. Gain bonuses to traveling, stealth, and survival checks related to that terrain. Move stealthily and set cunning traps, making the ranger adept at traversing the wild and ambushing foes.]\n\nBackstory:[\nAramil Galanodel has always heeded the silent whispers of the forest more than the clamor of city life. A scion of the ancient Galanodel lineage, his kinship with nature is as intrinsic as the sap in the trees and the streams that wend through the woods. In his youth, Aramil’s curiosity led him to unearth a sacred grove - a site forbidden to those not of druidic circles. Confronted by the druids and banished for his transgression, he wanders the wilderness, a sentinel guided by a moral compass that points only towards balance - and revenge against those who have forced this solitary path upon him.]\n\nPersonality:[\nWith the sharp eyes of an eagle and a presence as untraceable as the wind, Aramil is a creature of the wild. His demeanor is as calm as a placid lake, yet his heart burns with a smoldering fervor for the untamed beauty of nature. He's slow to trust but unwaveringly loyal to those few who have earned his respect. Despite his exile, he carries a sense of nobility that can't be marred by the prejudices of society. With every arrow loosed from his bow, Aramil serves as judge, jury, and executioner of nature's own law.]\n\nDescription:[\nAramil Galanodel stands tall and lean at 6ft and 180lbs, his lithe frame blending seamlessly with the forest canopy. His skin, the color of aged oak, bears the faintest trace of woodland patterns, echoing the shifting shadows of the trees above. Bright green eyes, keen as a hawk's, peer out from beneath a crown of tangled chestnut hair, while the faintest hint of a smirk dances upon his lips, hinting at the secrets hidden within the depths of the wilderness.]\",4,false,40,true,false,true,,4,40,false,true,10,41,20,\"elf_ranger\",\"aramil\",\"elf_ranger\",\"aramil\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,41,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Vorenus\",false,\"[Vorenus is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Vorenus Shadowhorn\n\nRace: Tiefling\n\nClass: Warlock (Pact of the Fiend)\n\nBackground: Entertainer\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Neutral\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 8 (-1)\nDexterity: 14 (+2)\nConstitution: 13 (+1)\nIntelligence: 12 (+1)\nWisdom: 10 (+0)\nCharisma: 18 (+4)\n]\n\nSkills: Deception, Performance\n\nEquipment:[\nTwo finely-crafted daggers,\nShortbow,\nQuiver of Arrows,\nComponent Pouch,\nEntertainer's Pack,\nFlask of ever-burning flame,\n15 gold pieces\n]\n\nRace Features: Tiefling: Darkvision, Hellish Resistance, Infernal Legacy\n\nClass Features: Sorcerer: Spellcasting, Sorcerous Origin (Shadow Magic), Eyes of the Dark, Strength of the Grave\n\nBackground Features: Entertainer: Popular Demand\n\nSpellcasting:\nCantrips: Eldritch Blast, Minor Illusion\n1st Level Spells: Hellish Rebuke, Charm Person\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 7 (6 base + 1 CON modifier)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 12 (15 with Mage Armor)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nDaggers: 1d4+2 piercing damage\nShortbow: 1d6+2 piercing damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nFiendish Vigor (Warlock Invocation):\n\nFrequency: At will.\nMechanics: Can cast False Life on oneself without expending a spell slot, gaining temporary hit points. Provides a self-sustaining source of temporary hit points to bolster survivability.\nAgonizing Blast (Warlock Invocation):\n\nFrequency: When casting Eldritch Blast.\nMechanics: Adds Charisma modifier to damage dealt by Eldritch Blast. Increases the damage output of Eldritch Blast, making it a potent offensive option for warlocks.\n\nStrength of the Grave (Hexblade Warlock):\n\nFrequency: Passive ability, triggered when reduced to 0 hit points.\nMechanics: Roll a d20 when reduced to 0 hit points, potentially avoiding being knocked unconscious if the roll exceeds damage taken. Provides a chance to cheat death, allowing the hexblade warlock to withstand fatal blows and continue fighting.]\n\nBackstory:[\nVorenus Shadowhorn’s infamous exploits stretch far and wide, whispered with both disdain and desire in the shady corners of taverns. Born into the spectacle of the performing arts, his hedonistic pursuits led him to embrace a path shadowed by indulgence and excess. Vorenus’ entanglements are legendary – his bedchamber's traffic rivals that of a bustling city square during festival season. Unbeknownst to most, his magnetic allure isn't mere charisma – it's enhanced by the infernal blood coursing through his veins, which grants him an almost supernatural seductiveness. Kicked out of his order for a string of lurid escapades unbefitting a man of his standing, Vorenus now delights in his liberated existence, unrestrained by the suffocating morality that once sought to cage him.]\n\nPersonality:[\nWith a roguish grin and a gaze that promises sin, Vorenus is a creature of both darkness and light. His charm is as potent as his hexes, captivating hearts with as much ease as he summons shadowy flames. His libidinous nature is renowned, his appetites as varied as the spells at his command. Love him or loathe him, none can deny Vorenus Shadowhorn leaves an indelible mark on all he encounters – for better or for worse.]\n\nDescription:[\nVorenus Shadowhorn is a striking figure, standing at 6 feet tall with a lean, agile 170lb build. His deep crimson skin is adorned with intricate patterns reminiscent of flickering flames, accentuated by his piercing golden eyes that seem to gleam with infernal knowledge. Twin horns curl back from his forehead, adding to his devilish allure, while a mischievous smirk often plays upon his lips, hinting at the secrets he holds.]\",4,false,41,true,false,true,,4,41,false,true,10,42,20,\"tiefling_warlock\",\"vorenus\",\"tiefling_warlock\",\"vorenus\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,42,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Tera\",false,\"[Tera is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Tera Earthbloom\n\nRace: Genasi (Earth)\n\nClass: Druid\n\nBackground: Hermit\n\nAlignment: Neutral Good\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 14 (+2)\nDexterity: 12 (+1)\nConstitution: 16 (+3)\nIntelligence: 10 (+0)\nWisdom: 16 (+3)\nCharisma: 11 (+0)\n]\n\nSkills: Medicine, Nature\n\nEquipment:[\nDruidic Focus,\nLeather Armor,\nHerbalism Kit,\nPotion of Healing,\n20 gold pieces\n]\n\nRace Features: Genasi: Earthborn - Able to move across difficult terrain made of earth or stone without expending extra movement. Merge with stone for additional stealth and protection.\n\nClass Features: Druid: Spellcasting, Wild Shape\nBackground Features: Hermit: Discovery - The quiet contemplation of her hermitage led to a significant breakthrough about the reality of existence.\n\nSpellcasting:\nCantrips: Guidance, Produce Flame\n1st Level Spells: Healing Word, Entangle\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 10 (8 base + 2 CON modifier)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 11 (Leather Armor + DEX modifier)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nQuarterstaff: 1d6+2 bludgeoning damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nTerra's Embrace: Frequency: Once per long rest. Mechanics: Channel the earth's vitality to cast 'Mass Cure Wounds' at her current highest spell slot without expending a spell slot.\nNature's Sentinel: Frequency: Passive ability, always active in natural environments. Mechanics: Allies within a 30-foot radius gain advantage on saving throws against being frightened or charmed when she's present.]\n\nBackstory:[\nTera' skin has the hues of deep, rich soil, with emerald green eyes that seem to hold the very essence of life within them. Her hair is a waterfall of vines and flowers that cascade over shoulders broadened by years of physical labor among the rolling hills of her secluded homeland. Cast out from the earth genasi community for embracing both male and female lovers with equal fervor — a forbidden practice in her conservative society — she sought solitude in the wilds. In her hermitage, she's become attuned to the whispers of nature, her spirit entwined with the world's deep-rooted life force. Tera's intense connection with the Earth not only fuels her druidic healing magic but also stirs a carnal energy that draws others to her, friend and foe alike.]\n\nPersonality:[\nTera possesses an aura of serene strength, yet a fiery passion smolders within her. She is compassionate to a fault, often placing the well-being of nature and her companions above her own safety. Her touch can be as gentle as a spring breeze or as forceful as a seismic tremor — it all depends on her temper, which shifts like the tectonic plates she so closely identifies with.]\n\nDescription:[\nTera Earthbloom stands tall at 6 feet, her sturdy frame weighing around 180 pounds. Her skin, reminiscent of deep, rich soil, is complemented by emerald green eyes that seem to hold the essence of life within them. Cascading over her broad shoulders are vines and flowers, a testament to her close connection with nature.]\",4,false,42,true,false,true,,4,42,false,true,10,43,20,\"tera\",\"genasi_druid\",\"tera\",\"genasi_druid\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,43,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Whispur\",false,\"[Whispur is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Whispur\n\nRace: Tabaxi\n\nClass: Monk (Way of the Shadow)\n\nBackground: Criminal\n\nAlignment: Neutral Evil\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 12 (+1)\nDexterity: 18 (+4)\nConstitution: 14 (+2)\nIntelligence: 10 (+0)\nWisdom: 15 (+2)\nCharisma: 11 (+0)\n]\n\nSkills: Acrobatics, Stealth\n\nEquipment:[\nMonk's Outfit,\nThieves' Tools,\nClimber's Kit,\n10 gold pieces]\n\nClass Features: Monk: Unarmored Defense, Martial Arts, Ki, Shadow Arts\nBackground Features: Criminal: Criminal Contact\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 9 (8 base + 1 CON modifier)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 16 (10 base + Dexterity modifier + Wisdom modifier)\nSpeed: 40 ft.\nAttacks:\nUnarmed Strikes (Long Claws): +2 to hit, 1d4+4 slashing damage\nKi points = current level, refreshing after a short rest.]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nShadow Step: Frequency: Once per turn. Mechanics: Teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space in dim light or darkness as a bonus action, gaining advantage on the first melee attack made afterward.\nStunning Strike: Frequency: After hitting another creature with a melee attack. Mechanics: Spend 1 ki point to stun the target until the end of your next turn if it fails a Constitution saving throw.\nFlurry of Blows: Frequency: Immediately after taking the Attack action on your turn. Mechanics: Spend 1 ki point to make two additional unarmed strikes as a bonus action.]\n\nBackstory:[\nWhispur, born in the seedy underbelly of a sprawling Tabaxi metropolis, grew to infamy in the criminal circles, her name a byword for deadliness. Schooled in the way of shadows, she honed her skills in the art of stealth and subterfuge, using her innate agility and razor-sharp claws to climb the ranks. Yet, amidst her rise, she succumbed to the hedonistic temptations that came with power. Her escapades were not only self-serving but also brought her sect into disrepute. Exiled for her lascivious conduct that flies in the face of her monastic discipline, Whispur now walks a solitary path, a shadow among shadows, her every step a silent promise of danger.]\n\nPersonality:[\nThere's a glint of madness in Whispur's eyes, a telltale sign of a mind unravelled by greed and the thrill of the hunt. She is a creature of impulse, living for the next score, the next pleasure, the next challenge. To her, morality is but a chain to be broken — her allegiance lies solely to herself. Whispur is as likely to leave you purring in delight as she is to disappear into the night, leaving nothing but the memory of her touch — and perhaps lighter pockets.]\n\nDescription:[\nWhispur, a sleek Tabaxi monk of the Way of the Shadow, stands at around 5 feet 10 inches tall and weighs approximately 150 pounds. Small fuzzy breasts and bare cat-like feet, she hates wearing boots or shoes. Her fur is a deep shade of ebony, accentuated by piercing green eyes that gleam with a hint of madness. With long, sharp claws and a feline agility, she moves with fluidity and stealth, blending seamlessly into the shadows. Dressed in a simple monk's outfit, she carries herself with an air of lethality her every movement betraying the deadly prowess honed in the criminal underworld.]\",4,false,43,true,false,true,,4,43,false,true,10,44,20,\"whispur\",\"tabaxi_monk\",\"whispur\",\"tabaxi_monk\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,44,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Kresh\",false,\"[Kresh is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Kresh\n\nRace: Lizardfolk\n\nClass: Barbarian\n\nBackground: Outcast\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Evil\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 18 (+4)\nDexterity: 12 (+1)\nConstitution: 16 (+3)\nIntelligence: 7 (-2)\nWisdom: 11 (+0)\nCharisma: 8 (-1)\n]\n\nSkills: Intimidation, Survival\n\nEquipment:[\nGreataxe,\nBone Necklace (Trophies from his victims),\nSeveral jagged throwing spears,\nPatchwork armor made from the hides of his enemies]\n\nClass Features: Barbarian: Rage, Unarmored Defense\nBackground Features: Outcast: Adapted to live and survive alone, relying on primal instinct rather than the common tongue\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 15 (12 base + 3 CON modifier)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 14 (10 base + 1 DEX modifier + 3 CON modifier while unarmored)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nGreataxe: 1d12+4 slashing damage\nUnarmed Strikes: +2 to hit, 1d4+4 slashing damage (using sharp claws)\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nRaging Storm:\n\nFrequency: Activates when raging.\nMechanics: While raging, Kresh can unleash lightning-infused attacks with his claws, dealing an additional 1d6 lightning damage. Enhances damage output during rage, adding elemental effects to attacks.\nSavage Resilience:\n\nFrequency: Triggers when taking damage.\nMechanics: Automatically reduces incoming damage by half (rounded down), except for psychic damage. Allows Kresh to withstand blows with fierce resilience, maintaining his fighting spirit even when severely wounded.]\n\nBackstory:[\nKresh, marked by his bloodlust and savage appetites, has long been shunned even by his own ruthless kind. A hulking brute with scales like jagged obsidian, he revels in the thrill of the hunt and the sweetness of suffering — particularly that of elves and humans. His name is spoken in hushed tones and with curses spat upon the ground. Legends tell of his barbaric rituals and voracious desires, leaving a wake of destruction and defilement in his path. Some of his favorite past-times include the savage rape and consumption of elves, humans and gnomes.]\n\nPersonality:[\nKresh embodies the dark heart of the wilderness — cruel, unpredictable, and devoid of remorse. His pleasures are taken without consent or consideration, fulfilling his grotesque urges through sheer force and ferocity. Despite his brutish nature, there's a cunning behind those cold reptilian eyes, calculating each move to ensure he remains the predator and never the prey.]\n\nDescription:[\nKresh, a towering Lizardfolk standing at 7 feet tall and weighing a lean and terrifying 300 pounds, exudes a menacing aura with his thick, dark-green scales and serpentine eyes. Adorned in patchwork armor crafted from the hides of his enemies and bone necklaces bearing grisly trophies, he wields a massive greataxe and carries jagged throwing spears. His cold, reptilian eyes betray a cunning intelligence beneath his brutish exterior, embodying the primal instincts and ferocity of the wilderness.]\",4,false,44,true,false,true,,4,44,false,true,10,45,20,\"kresh\",\"lizardfolk_barbarian\",\"kresh\",\"lizardfolk_barbarian\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,45,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Grashka\",false,\"[Grashka is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Grashka\n\nRace: Orc\n\nClass: Bard (College of Whispers)\n\nBackground: Pirate\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Neutral\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 16 (+3)\nDexterity: 14 (+2)\nConstitution: 16 (+3)\nIntelligence: 10 (+0)\nWisdom: 12 (+1)\nCharisma: 16 (+3)\n]\n\nSkills: Persuasion, Performance\n\nEquipment:[\nLeather Armor,\nA pair of enchanted maracas that double as bludgeoning weapons,\nA flask of never-ending rum,\n15 gold pieces,\nA collection of ribald shanties]\n\nClass Features: Bard: Spellcasting, Bardic Inspiration (d6), Jack of All Trades, Song of Rest\nBackground Features: Pirate: Bad Reputation\n\nCombat Stats:\nHit Points: 11 (8 base + 3 CON modifier)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 14 (Leather Armor + DEX modifier)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nMaracas/Unarmed Strikes: 1d6+3 bludgeoning damage\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nWords of Terror: Frequency: Once per short rest. Mechanics: Instill intense fear into a creature after a private conversation for the next hour.\nMantle of Whispers: Frequency: Once per long rest. Mechanics: Capture a shadow of the dead to disguise herself and gain access to information the deceased knew.]\n\nBackstory:[\nGrashka's tale is as tumultuous as the seas she once roamed - a buccaneer who sought treasure in both gold and flesh. Her carnal conquests are as legendary as her raids, and no port could contain her voracious appetites. After a salacious scandal involving a high-ranking official and his spouse, Grashka was cast out to land, her pirate life marooned. Yet, her passions remain unchained, and now she channels her lascivious energy into the art of manipulation and seduction through her bardic magic.]\n\nPersonality:[\nGrashka is a walking storm of desires, each step a dance, each word a siren's call. She carries the bearing of a queen and the sultry menace of a shark. Whether swaying hips to her bewitching songs or drawing secrets from the lips of the weak-willed with her alluring whispers, she's as unpredictable as she is dangerous. Still, the glint in her eye betrays her lust for life's many pleasures, and she's never one to shy away from an innuendo-laden jest or a chance encounter of the flesh.]\n\nDescription:[\nGrashka stands tall at 6 feet 5 inches, with a sturdy build and a weight of around 250 pounds. Her wild mane of tangled black hair cascades down her broad shoulders, adorned with trinkets and beads collected from her travels. Her skin bears the scars of countless battles, each marking a tale of triumph or defeat. Grashka's piercing amber eyes hold a mischievous gleam, contrasting with her fearsome appearance. She typically wears rugged leather armor, adorned with various pirate trinkets and charms, and carries herself with a confident swagger.]\",4,false,45,true,false,true,,4,45,false,true,10,46,20,\"grashka\",\"orc_bard\",\"grashka\",\"orc_bard\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,46,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Lila\",false,\"[Lila is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Lila Swiftfoot\n\nRace: Half-Elf\n\nClass: Rogue\n\nBackground: Urchin\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Neutral\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 8 (-1)\nDexterity: 16 (+3)\nConstitution: 12 (+1)\nIntelligence: 13 (+1)\nWisdom: 10 (+0)\nCharisma: 14 (+2)]\n\nSkills: Stealth, Acrobatics\n\nEquipment:[\nShortbow,\nQuiver of Arrows,\nTwin Daggers,\nThieves' Tools,\nDark Leather Hood and Cloak,\n15 gold pieces]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nShadowmeld: Frequency: Once per short rest. \nMechanics: Lila can blend into shadows, becoming nearly invisible even in plain sight.\nQuickfoot Ability:\nFrequency: Can be used once per turn.\nMechanics: Lila can dash or disengage as a bonus action, showcasing her swift reflexes and allowing her to maneuver into or out of combat effortlessly.\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 8 (8 base + 0 CON modifier)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 14 (11 base + Dexterity modifier)\nSpeed: 35 ft.\nAttacks:\nDaggers: 1d4+3 piercing damage\nShortbow: +1 to hit, 1d6+3 piercing damage]\n\nBackstory:[\nThe child of an elf and an unknown wanderer, Lila grew up on the streets, relying on her cunning and agility to survive. Twelve years old, petite and easily underestimated, she used her size to her advantage, slipping through shadows and snatching what she needed to get by. The urban jungle became her playground, every alleyway a secret path, every rooftop a haven. At a tender age though, she discovered a penchant for archery – a way to reach out and touch the world without ever leaving the safety of her hidden perches. Yet, behind her innocent appearance lies the heart of a predator, always watching, always calculating – a huntress in the concrete wilds. She has daddy issues and will latch onto older male figures in more ways than one.]\n\nPersonality:[\nLila is as mercurial as the winds that whip through the city's tallest spires. She is as likely to offer a mischievous smile as she is a cutting retort. Her humor is as dark as the alleys she calls home, and while she may walk alongside you, make no mistake – Lila Swiftfoot owes allegiance to no one but herself. To her, life is a game, and she is determined not to lose – no matter what the rules are or who she's playing against.]\n\nDescription:[\nA half-elf rogue, skin fair but dirt-kissed, evidence of life on the ragged streets. She's around five feet one, slim as a blade at 90lbs, with muscles tight from scaling walls and dodging the city's underbelly. Eyes like dusk, a mix of purple and grey, flecked with the silver of her elven blood. Hair dark, cropped short for convenience, sticking out under the hood she doesn't fucking need for this. And her weight, what's it to you? Let's say light enough to slip over rooftops without a sound, heavy enough to kick your ass if you cross her.\",4,false,46,true,false,true,,4,46,false,true,10,47,20,\"half-elf_rogue\",\"lila\",\"half-elf_rogue\",\"lila\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,47,true,true,false,,\"Goliath Barbarian Character Sheet (chaotic evil, level 5)\",false,\"<character_sheet_barbarian>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\nRace: Goliath\n\nLevel: 5\n\nClass: Barbarian\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Evil\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 18 (+4)\nDexterity: 12 (+1)\nConstitution: 16 (+3)\nIntelligence: 6 (-2)\nWisdom: 10 (+0)\nCharisma: 8 (-1)]\n\nSkills: Athletics, Intimidation\n\nEquipment:[\nGreatsword\nHandaxes (2)\nBear Pelt Armor\nExplorer's Pack\n50 Gold]\n\nClass Features: Barbarian: Rage (2 times per long rest), Unarmored Defense\nRace Features: Goliath: Mountain Born, Stone's Endurance (Once per short or long rest), Powerful Build\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 60 (5d12 max Hit Dice + CON modifier per level)\nArmor Class: 13 (10 base + DEX modifier + 1 from Goliath racial trait)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nGreatsword: 2d6+4 slashing damage\nHandaxe: 1d6+4 slashing damage (throwable)]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nRelentless Endurance: \nFrequency: Passive, once per long rest. \nMechanics: When reduced to 0 HP but not killed outright, drop to 1 HP instead.\n\nSavage Attacks: \nFrequency: Passive, on a critical melee hit. \nMechanics: Roll an additional weapon damage die when determining the extra damage for a critical hit with a melee attack.\n\nTerrifying Howl: Frequency: Once per long rest. \nMechanics: As an action, unleash a bone-chilling howl that can be heard up to 300 feet away. Enemies within 30 feet must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute.\n\nBloodlust: \nFrequency: Passive, when you reduce an enemy to 0 HP. \nMechanics: Gain temporary hit points equal to your rage damage bonus, and you may immediately use your reaction to move up to half your speed towards another enemy without provoking opportunity attacks.\n\nRage:\nFrequency: 2 times per long rest at level 5.\nMechanics: On your turn, you can enter a rage as a bonus action. While raging, you gain the following benefits:\nAdvantage on Strength Checks and Strength Saving Throws: Because when you're this pissed off, the world bends to your will.\nBonus Damage: +2 on melee weapon attack damage rolls. This bonus increases as you level up.\nResistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing Damage: Pain? It's just a word. While raging, a Barbarian feels less of it, as though their skin turns to stone.\nA rage lasts for 1 minute, but it ends early if you're knocked unconscious or if your turn ends and you haven't attacked a hostile creature since your last turn or taken damage since then. You can also end your rage on your turn as a free action.]\n</character_sheet_barbarian>\n\",4,false,47,true,false,true,,4,47,false,true,10,48,90,\"character_sheet_barbarian\",\"character_sheet_barbarian\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,48,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Pippa\",false,\"[Pippa is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Pippa Honeyspark\n\nRace: Gnome\n\nClass: Sorcerer (Wild Magic)\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Good\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 8 (-1)\nDexterity: 15 (+2)\nConstitution: 14 (+2)\nIntelligence: 12 (+1)\nWisdom: 11 (+0)\nCharisma: 17 (+3)]\n\nSkills: Arcana, Persuasion\n\nEquipment:[\nCrystal Orb (Arcane Focus),\nLight Crossbow,\nDagger,\nComponent Pouch,\nScholar’s Pack,\nAssorted Trinkets (from past admirers),\n20 gold pieces]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nWild Magic Surge: Frequency: After casting a sorcerer spell of 1st level or higher. Mechanics: Unpredictable magical effects can occur, ranging from beneficial to chaotic.\nTides of Chaos: Frequency: Once per long rest. Mechanics: Gain advantage on one attack roll, ability check, or saving throw.\nArcane Whispers: Frequency: At will. Mechanics: Weaves enchantments into suggestive remarks, subtly influencing others to her will.]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 7 (6 base + 1 CON modifier)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 12 (10 base + Dexterity modifier)\nSpeed: 25 ft.\nAttacks:\nLight Crossbow: 1d8+2 piercing damage\nDagger: 1d4+2 piercing damage]\n\nBackstory:[\nBorn in the vibrant heart of a gnome city, Pippa was the gem of her community, admired for both her mind and the alluring curve of her ass. Yet, it was those same round cheeks that led to her undoing in the conservative enclaves of gnome society. An indiscretion with a prominent figure – the details of which are scandalously whispered – saw her expelled, flung from the comforts of her home into the wild unknown. Armed with nothing but her wits, her charms, and a desire to explore the breadth of her desires and the world itself, she roams, seeking pleasure, adventure, and a good tumble with an interesting company.]\n\nPersonality:[\nDon't let the petite, curvy frame fool you; Pippa's a sorceress with a powerful command over the elements, although she'd much prefer to cast a different kind of enchantment. Her laughter is infectious, her manner playfully seductive, and she has a penchant for teasing that knows no bounds. Those who encounter her find themselves charmed by her whimsical demeanor just as often as they are ensnared by her arcane prowess. And if rumors are to be believed, her kinky talents extend well beyond spellcasting, making her a favorite companion among those who enjoy life's more carnal delights.]\n\nDescription: [\nPippa Honeyspark is as small and feisty as a gnome comes. At three and a half feet and 45lbs, she's got a mass of curly brown hair on her head that bounces with each step. Her skin's fair, almost glowing, like she rubs it down with magic or some shit. Her robes are a psychedelic swirl of colors that screams \"\"sorcerer on a bender,\"\" and her crystal orb arcane focus glints like a disco ball at her belt. She trots around with a crossbow that's more of a fashion statement than weapon, a dagger that probably sees more action cutting up her wildberry pies, and a scholar’s pack that's seen more parties than a tavern wench. No missing her in a crowd, that's for fucking sure.]\",4,false,48,true,false,true,,4,48,false,true,10,49,20,\"gnome_sorcerer\",\"pippa\",\"gnome_sorcerer\",\"pippa\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,49,true,true,false,,\"Cities - mixed\",false,\"[These are cities known for their mixed populations.]\n\nGrand Harbor:[\n\nSize: The largest known city\nKnown for: A hub of commerce and culture where the world's riches and darkest secrets are traded in equal measure.\nDescription: Grand Harbor is a titan among cities, sprawling outwards and upwards from the central bay that teems with ships from far-off lands. Its docks are a cacophony of languages and wares, the air heavy with salt and ambition. Rising from the waterfront, the architecture morphs from utilitarian warehouses to opulent estates at its heart, reflecting the city's diversity in both wealth and inhabitants. Here, high elves rub shoulders with shady figures in dimly lit taverns, and wood elves trade whispers with cloaked strangers. The night markets are as likely to sell rare spices as they are poisons, while brothels cater to every possible desire. Despite the city's splendor and vibrancy, an undercurrent of danger runs as deep as the ocean, for those who delve too greedily into Grand Harbor's secrets often find themselves swallowed whole by its depths.]\n\nHarrowspire:[\n\nSize: Sprawling city\nKnown for: Its cutthroat political intrigue and the ominous tower that looms over it, rumored to be home to an ancient vampire lord.\nDescription: Harrowspire's cobblestone streets are as cold and unforgiving as the city's heart. Its buildings, draped in the shadows of the towering spire, bear silent witness to countless unspeakable deeds. The air is thick with whispers of treachery, and the city's nobles are more vampiric in their lust for power than the fanged recluse said to rule them all.]\n\nMirthfall:[\n\nSize: Quaint village\nKnown for: An almost disturbingly idyllic demeanor and its inexplicably perpetual harvest festival.\nDescription: A forever autumnal paradise, Mirthfall is a riot of color and ceaseless celebration. But beneath its joyous veneer, something isn't right. The villagers laugh too loudly, smile too widely, and never seem to sleep. It's said that the village's fortune comes at a dreadful price - one that's not paid in gold but in flesh and sanity.]\n\nBriar's Crossing:[\n\nSize: Bustling town\nKnown for: The rare, blood-red roses that grow nowhere else and its highly sought-after apothecaries.\nDescription: Briar's Crossing is a town swathed in the perfume of roses and secrecy. Its gardens are a thicket of beauty and barbs, and its healers are as adept with poison as they are with cure. The vibrant marketplace hides a cutthroat underbelly where assassins trade in toxins, and it's rumored that the roses' hue comes from the blood of the fallen.]\n\nThunder's Reach:[\n\nSize: Isolated outpost\nKnown for: Being the last known bastion before the perilous Stormpeak Mountains.\nDescription: Standing staunch against howling winds and the rumble of distant thunder, Thunder's Reach is no place for the faint-hearted. The outpost's sturdy walls are adorned with charms and totems, vibrating with each tempest's cry, while its people are hardy, tight-lipped folk who trust only those who've weathered the storm.]\n\nCindermaw Citadel:[\n\nSize: Fortress city\nKnown for: Its forges, where metals and magics meld to create items of unimaginable power.\nDescription: Encompassed by walls of blackened stone, Cindermaw Citadel is a monument to fire's fury. Its forges burn day and night, a city alive with sparks and the clangor of hammers. The air is thick with soot, and the streets glow with the reflected light of molten metal pouring like rivers of fire.]\n\nSilkstrand:[\n\nMedium City\nKnown for: Its thriving silk trade and cutthroat fashion industry.\nDescription: Silkstrand is a city draped in opulence, with every street corner vying for style and every rooftop aspiring to grace. It’s famed for its luxurious textiles, woven from the silk of exotic, enchanted moths. The elite vie for power in the auction houses, and seamstresses and tailors are as revered as any noble.]\n\nFogwatch Point:[\n\nMedium City\nKnown for: The perpetual fog that shrouds the city, and its mysterious lighthouse.\nDescription: Fogwatch Point, where the mist hugs the cobblestones and the sun is just a rumor. Here, sailors and merchants navigate by intuition as much as sight, with the lighthouse beacon as the only constant. Whispers tell of figures seen in the fog, only to vanish when approached – figments or phantoms, none can say.]\n\nGarnet Hollows:[\n\nMedium City\nKnown for: The rare garnet mines and its surprisingly vibrant night life.\nDescription: Garnet Hollows glows with the fires of the forge and the sparkle of precious stones plucked from the earth’s rich veins. By day, miners and gem-smiths toil amidst dust and stone. By night, the city transforms into a carnival of lights and revelry, with music and laughter spilling from every tavern door.]\n\nBlackmark Bastion:[\n\nLarge City\nKnown for: Its infamous underbelly of crime, shadow markets that trade in forbidden pleasures, and alleys that reek of corruption.\nDescription: A sprawling metropolis where the high walls are as much to keep threats out as to trap secrets within. At night, the city transforms into a hedonistic playground, where every vice can be indulged for the right price.]\n\nEclipse Hollow:[\n\nLarge City\nKnown for: Being the nexus of espionage and political assassinations, where every shadow whispers and every smile hides a dagger.\nDescription: A city of contrasts, where opulent palaces stand shoulder to shoulder with seedy brothels. The air is charged with paranoia, and trust is as scarce as honest men.]\n\nSunstone Haven:[\n\nLarge City\nKnown for: Its radiant architecture and the legendary Sunstone at its heart, rumored to bestow blessings upon the worthy and curses upon the unworthy.\nDescription: Glimmering streets paved with intentions both pure and vile wind through the city, leading to an awe-inspiring central temple that houses the Sunstone. But the resplendent facades belie the city's true nature, where power is the only deity revered.]\n\nTanglethorn Hollow:[\n\nSize: Small town\nKnown for: The carnivorous plants that encircle it, creating a natural defense and an unnerving ambiance.\nDescription: The heart of Tanglethorn Hollow is encased in a deadly embrace of thorny vines and snapping flora. Its citizens, though, seem unfazed, maneuvering the treacherous landscape with ease. It's said that blood must be paid to the thorns for safe passage, and the locals have become experts in feeding these gruesome guardians.]\n\nWhimseydell:[\n\nSize: Expansive village\nKnown for: Its seemingly mad residents and whimsical architecture that defies explanation.\nDescription: Whimseydell is a tapestry of the absurd – buildings twist in impossible shapes, and the streets loop back upon themselves in labyrinthine confusion. It’s as if the very fabric of reality got drunk here and never sobered up. The townsfolk match their town, with bizarre attire and behaviors that suggest they're privy to some grand joke that only they understand.]\n\nCarrion's Crest:[\nSize: Small town\nKnown for: Its unsettling abundance of carrion birds that circle perpetually overhead, giving it a macabre reputation.\nDescription: Carrion's Crest is perched on a windswept plateau, the skies above a dance floor for crows and vultures. The town's buildings, shrouded in shadows, have a gothic charm. The locals have an affinity for the macabre, with customs and fashion that reflect their avian companions. Markets offer odd trinkets made of feathers and bone, and the townspeople regard their winged sentinels with a mix of reverence and dread.]\",4,false,49,true,false,true,,4,49,false,true,10,50,95,\"Varied city\",\"Mixed city\",\"Global city\",\"City neighborhood\",\"Urban center\",\"village\",\"hamlets\",\"Melting pot\",\"dwelling\",\"Cultural hub\",\"town\",\"Multicultural city\",\"Diverse city\",\"settlement\",\"burg\",\"City district\",\"Metropolis\",\"Cityscape\",\"city\",\"cities\",\"Cosmopolitan city\",\"Varied city\",\"Mixed city\",\"Global city\",\"City neighborhood\",\"Urban center\",\"village\",\"hamlets\",\"Melting pot\",\"dwelling\",\"Cultural hub\",\"town\",\"Multicultural city\",\"Diverse city\",\"settlement\",\"burg\",\"City district\",\"Metropolis\",\"Cityscape\",\"city\",\"cities\",\"Cosmopolitan city\",\"\",95,1,10,100,true,0,50,true,true,false,,\"Cities - dwarven\",false,\"[These cities are primarily populated by dwarves, but will also include random other races.]\n\nIronforge Enclave:[\n\nSize: Heavily fortified underground city, dwarven capital\nKnown for: Master blacksmithing and intricate clockwork engineering.\nDescription: Ironforge Enclave, carved deep into the mountainside, is a marvel of dwarven craftsmanship. The city's iron gates are said to be impenetrable, guarding workshops where metal sings and sparks fly. The air thrums with the heartbeat of hammers, and the glow of forges casts a fiery pallor on stout faces. Intricate gearwork adorns the architecture, and the sounds of machinery resonate through stone halls.]\n\nStonehelm Stronghold:[\n\nSize: Expansive subterranean metropolis\nKnown for: Its impregnable defenses and ancient runic lore.\nDescription: Nestled within the womb of the earth, Stonehelm Stronghold stands as a testament to the might and mystery of the dwarven people. Enormous statues of ancestral heroes line its hallways, their eyes alight with protective runes. Libraries filled with tomes of forgotten knowledge spiral down into the bedrock, while the city’s heart beats with the rhythm of traditional dwarven chants echoing off the walls.]\n\nMithril Hall:[\n\nSize: Massive underground fortress\nKnown for: The rare mithril veins that vein its walls and the legendary weapons forged from them.\nDescription: Mithril Hall gleams like a star beneath the mountain, its corridors lit by luminous fungi and reflective metals. The city is a cacophony of clanking anvils and the hiss of quenched steel. Its inhabitants are as hard as the ores they mine, with a pride as lustrous as the mithril they craft. Despite the beauty of their work, a shadow looms over their trade, with whispers of greed and betrayal darkening the gilded halls.]\n\nAmberforge:[\n\nMedium City\nKnown for: Its intricate jewelry and superior gem-cutting craftsmanship.\nDescription: Nestled within the embrace of towering amber cliffs, Amberforge is a dazzling spectacle of gilded opulence. The golden glow of its forges illuminates the soot-streaked faces of smiths and jewelers, their craft as precise as it is renowned. Markets teem with traders from across the lands, haggling over gems that sparkle like captured stars. Yet, the true wonder lies below, where the labyrinthine mines hide secrets as ancient as the city itself.]\n\nStonebarrow:[\n\nMedium City\nKnown for: Staunch military traditions and the impenetrable Stonebarrow Keep.\nDescription: Rising like a behemoth of stone on the horizon, Stonebarrow's formidable architecture speaks of a people ever-ready for war. Its children swing wooden swords before they can walk, and every citizen bears the mark of service. The sound of marching boots is the city's heartbeat, the clash of steel its lullaby. Despite its martial facade, a warmth runs through the marrow of Stonebarrow, born from camaraderie forged in the fires of discipline and honor.]\n\nDeepwell:[\n\nMedium City\nKnown for: The enigmatic Deepwell Springs, whose waters are said to hold mystic properties.\nDescription: Surrounded by arid lands as far as the eye can see, Deepwell is a verdant anomaly. Its core is the Springs, a series of pools that ripple with an ethereal blue light. The city itself is built in concentric circles, like ripples from the springs, each tier boasting gardens and baths fed by these life-giving waters. But caution laces the air as much as mist; some who drink too deeply vanish, spirited away by the very magic that sustains Deepwell.]\n\nBoulderhelm:[\n\nSmall Town\nKnown for: Being the heart of the cobblestone quarrying industry.\nDescription: \"\"Boulderhelm is stout and dusty, its squat stone houses circled around the central quarry like children around a storyteller. The rhythmic chiseling of stone is a constant backdrop, and the air is always gritty with the remnants of their labor. But don’t let the rough exterior fool ya, inside those walls are homes lined with intricate mosaics and surprisingly delicate stonework, telling of a people who can find beauty in the brawn.\"\"]\n\nGrizzlepeak:[\n\nSmall Town\nKnown for: Its hot springs, heated by geothermal activity, attracting those seeking the healing properties of their mineral-rich waters.\nDescription: \"\"Grizzlepeak’s steam rises against the backdrop of snow-capped mountains, a place of respite for weary travelers. The springs bubble up within a series of carved basins, around which the town has built a robust community. Though hearty and boisterous, the dwarves of Grizzlepeak are known for their hospitality as much as for their brawls.\"\"]\n\nForgefire Hold:[\n\nSmall Town\nKnown for: Its skilled armorsmiths whose work is said to be blessed by the forge goddess herself.\nDescription: \"\"Nestled in a valley where the clanking of hammers against anvils sings from dawn till dusk, Forgefire Hold shimmers with the glow of molten metal. Its streets are lined with workshops, their open fronts displaying the gleaming wares. But it ain’t all just craft and sweat; when the forging is done, the taverns come alive with ale-soaked tales and fireside laughter.\"\"]\",4,false,50,true,false,true,,4,50,false,true,10,51,95,\"Subterranean city\",\"Fortress of the dwarves\",\"Dwarven civilization\",\"Dwarven kingdom\",\"Dwarven enclave\",\"dwarven village\",\"Dwarven city\",\"dwarf town\",\"dwarf city\",\"Dwarven society\",\"Dwarven settlement\",\"Dwarven realm\",\"Dwarven architecture\",\"Dwarven town\",\"Dwarven culture\",\"Mountain stronghold\",\"Mining community\",\"Underground city\",\"Subterranean city\",\"Fortress of the dwarves\",\"Dwarven civilization\",\"Dwarven kingdom\",\"Dwarven enclave\",\"dwarven village\",\"Dwarven city\",\"dwarf town\",\"dwarf city\",\"Dwarven society\",\"Dwarven settlement\",\"Dwarven realm\",\"Dwarven architecture\",\"Dwarven town\",\"Dwarven culture\",\"Mountain stronghold\",\"Mining community\",\"Underground city\",\"\",95,1,10,100,true,0,51,true,true,false,,\"Cities - gnomish\",false,\"[These cities are primarily populated by gnomes, but will also include random other races.]\n\nGlimmerforge Capital:[\nSize: Grand Capital City\nKnown for: Its glistening towers of enchanted gemstones and bustling markets boasting the rarest of arcane components.\nDescription: Glimmerforge is a symphony of color and light, with streets that pulse with magical energy and buildings crafted from pure crystal. The gnomes here are as brilliant in their craft as the city is in its luminescence. At the heart, the Grand Arcanum stands, a library so vast it's said one could study a lifetime and barely scratch the surface.]\n\nTinkerstown:[\nSize: Large City\nKnown for: Being a hub of innovation, where inventive minds create mechanical wonders that defy imagination.\nDescription: The clang and clatter of Tinkerstown can be heard from miles away, as inventors and engineers work tirelessly in their workshops. Clockwork devices walk the streets alongside their creators, and steam billows from the engines that power the city. It's a place where tradition is for the old, and the new is embraced with open arms—or mechanical ones.]\n\nCoghaven:[\nSize: Large City\nKnown for: Its prestigious engineering academy and the legendary Cog Coliseum, where automatons battle in spectacular displays.\nDescription: Coghaven is a marvel of gears and steam, a testament to gnomish ingenuity. The towering academy looms over the city, drawing aspiring minds from across the land. Below, the coliseum roars with the cheers of crowds as metal titans clash for glory. The city itself is a machine, each citizen a cog turning in perfect harmony.]\n\nGearshaft Grove:[\n\nMedium Town\nKnown for: Clockwork orchards with mechanical trees that actually bear fruit – if a bit more metallic than one might expect.\nDescription: Gearshaft Grove is the place where nature meets machine. Here, gnomish ingenuity has led to the development of an entire ecosystem of brass foliage and copper fauna. The sight of metallic leaves fluttering in the wind is as common as the townsfolk's tinkering. While the fusion of technology and nature might perplex outsiders, for the residents of Gearshaft Grove, it's just another day in paradise.]\n\nSprocket Springs:[\n\nMedium Town\nKnown for: Its steaming hot springs that are not entirely natural; some say the geysers are powered by an ancient machine deep underground.\nDescription: Sprocket Springs bubbles with the energy of its subterranean gears. The town is a maze of steam pipes and bubbling pools, where the locals don't just bathe – they partake in spa treatments that can recalibrate one's inner workings. The air is rich with steam and the scent of oiled machinery, and the constant hum beneath the streets is a lullaby to the children of the forge.]\n\nWidgeton:[\n\nMedium Town\nKnown for: Its academy of alchemy and invention, where many a gnome has blown up a laboratory in pursuit of scientific advancement.\nDescription: Widgeton is where young gnomes' dreams soar as high as their explosive experiments. With buildings designed to withstand regular detonations and streets that double as testing grounds for the latest contraptions, it's never a dull moment here. If you visit, mind your step – brilliance here is as volatile as it is bright.]\n\nCogwheel Corner:[\n\nSmall Town\nKnown for: Whirring workshops and inventors' havens.\nDescription: Cogwheel Corner is a tinkerer's dream spun into reality. The streets hum with the sound of gears and steam, and the smell of oil and metal permeates the air. Every building bristles with antennas and copper pipes, giving the impression of a town that's always one experiment away from a breakthrough — or an explosion.]\n\nTicktock Terrace:[\n\nSmall Town\nKnown for: Being a timekeeper's sanctuary where every moment counts.\nDescription: In Ticktock Terrace, time doesn't just march on; it dances, it leaps, it whirls. Massive clocks adorn every facade, their pendulums swinging in a mesmerizing rhythm. The townsfolk are punctual to a fault, their lives orchestrated to the second — they celebrate the turning of the hour with chimes and cheers, an odd tradition that marks the passage of days.]\n\nVelvet Vallation:[\n\nSmall Town\nKnown for: Infamously operating as the underbelly's pleasure district; a hub for hedonistic gnomes and those seeking indulgences less spoken of.\nDescription: Don't let its quaint size fool you; Velvet Vallation hides libidinous excess behind its velvet curtains. Incense swirls through the air, mixing with laughter and the soft strumming of lutes. It's a labyrinth of bordellos and opium dens where gnomes and visitors alike come to sate desires others might consider… unseemly. Their secrets are kept as closely as the mechanisms of their finest clocks, for what happens in Velvet Vallation, stays in Velvet Vallation.]\",4,false,51,true,false,true,,4,51,false,true,10,52,95,\"Gnome city\",\"glimmerforge\",\"Gnome town\",\"Gnomish civilization\",\"Gnome settlement\",\"tinkerstown\",\"Gnome habitat\",\"Gnomish society\",\"Gnome borough\",\"Gnome enclave\",\"Gnomish community\",\"Gnome village\",\"Gnome realm\",\"Gnome hamlet\",\"Gnome city\",\"glimmerforge\",\"Gnome town\",\"Gnomish civilization\",\"Gnome settlement\",\"tinkerstown\",\"Gnome habitat\",\"Gnomish society\",\"Gnome borough\",\"Gnome enclave\",\"Gnomish community\",\"Gnome village\",\"Gnome realm\",\"Gnome hamlet\",\"\",95,1,10,100,true,0,52,true,true,false,,\"Cities - elven\",false,\"[These cities are primarily populated by elves, but will also include random other races. Elven cities are always primarily led by either high elves or wood elves.]\n\nElderbark:[\n\nSize: Grand Capital of the Wood Elves\nKnown for: Its seamless integration into the Great Forest, buildings crafted within the trees themselves, not a nail or saw has touched these living abodes.\nDescription: Elderbark is as much a part of the forest as the ancient oaks that cradle it in their boughs. Homes are nestled in hollowed trunks or suspended within the canopy, connected by bridges woven from vines. The air sings with the rustle of leaves, and the entire city seems to sway gently with the wind.]\n\nStarshimmer:[\n\nSize: Exalted Capital of the High Elves\nKnown for: Towering crystalline architecture, mystic libraries filled with arcane knowledge, and rulers who weave magic into the very fabric of their society.\nDescription: Starshimmer glows with an unearthly light, as if the stars themselves have descended to nest within its spires. Enchantments float through the air like motes of dust, and the city's regal high elves move with a grace born of millennia. The grandeur of its arcane academies and the splendor of its ethereal palaces are unrivaled, a testament to high elven civilization's pinnacle.]\n\nEclipsewood:[\n\nLarge City - Wood Elf\nRenowned for magical flora that glows with lunar energy, especially at night.\nOutwardly a luminescent woodland sanctuary, the city is built upon and between colossal ancient trees, connected by luminescent vine bridges. Eclipsewood is a nexus for druids and nature sorcerers, and the glowing plants are used in powerful potions.]\n\nMoonhaven:[\n\nLarge City - Wood Elf\nKnown for expert archers and a mysterious moonstone quarry.\nA blend of organic and elegant wooden structures, each archer's tower carved from living trees. The Moonhaven archers patrol day and night, their arrows empowered by the moonstones mined deep below the forest floor.]\n\nStarfall Enclave:[\n\nLarge City - High Elf\nFamed for advanced arcane research and a university that floats above the city.\nGleaming towers rise amidst the city's magecrafted stone pathways. The floating University of Starfall, accessible only by magical means, is where high elves delve into the secrets of the cosmos.]\n\nAethercrest:[\n\nLarge City - High Elf\nFamed for a market of rare magical artifacts and its hovering citadels.\nWalls etched with intricate runes protect this city where the streets seem alive with magical energy. The citadels, defying gravity, are home to powerful wizards whose experiments often light up the sky.]\n\nEldervine Haven:[\n\nMedium City - Wood Elf\nKnown for: Seamlessly weaving homes and shops within the ancient vines that sprawl through the city.\nDescription: Eldervine Haven is alive, quite literally, with verdant greenery enfolding each structure. The marketplaces bustle among the boughs, the laughter of children mingling with birdsong. Here, the elves live in harmony with the ever-growing forest, their lives an elegant dance with nature.]\n\nTwilight Glade:[\n\nMedium City - Wood Elf\nKnown for: Its eternal twilight, the result of a magical canopy that filters sunlight into perpetual dusk.\nDescription: With a gentle luminescence bathing its streets, Twilight Glade thrives in a state of eternal autumn. Its inhabitants are adept at blending into the dim light, and their culture is as mysterious as the subtle shadows that play upon their delicate features.]\n\nAurorafall:[\n\nMedium City - High Elf\nKnown for: Its stunning auroras, created by high elven magic that paints the sky with vibrant hues each night.\nDescription: The air is alive with color in Aurorafall, where the night sky is a canvas for the city's mages. Their buildings, crafted from alabaster and moonstone, reflect the celestial dance above, making the entire city glimmer with otherworldly beauty.]\n\nCrystalshore:[\n\nMedium City - High Elf\nKnown for: Its mesmerizing waterfront, where magic turns the tide into glittering crystal waves.\nDescription: Crystalshore's elegance is unmatched, the seaside carved into shimmering cliffs that reflect the sun’s rays into dazzling rainbows. The port thrives with commerce, as its crystalline bay is not just beautiful but serves as a mighty defense against any who dare challenge the high elves' naval prowess.]\n\nWhimseydell:[\nSize: Expansive village\nKnown for: Its seemingly mad residents and whimsical architecture that defies explanation.\nDescription: Whimseydell is a tapestry of the absurd – buildings twist in impossible shapes, and the streets loop back upon themselves in labyrinthine confusion. It’s as if the very fabric of reality got drunk here and never sobered up. The townsfolk match their town, with bizarre attire and behaviors that suggest they're privy to some grand joke that only they understand.]\n\nTanglethorn Hollow:[\nSize: Small town\nKnown for: The carnivorous plants that encircle it, creating a natural defense and an unnerving ambiance.\nDescription: The heart of Tanglethorn Hollow is encased in a deadly embrace of thorny vines and snapping flora. Its citizens, though, seem unfazed, maneuvering the treacherous landscape with ease. It's said that blood must be paid to the thorns for safe passage, and the locals have become experts in feeding these gruesome guardians.]\n\nStarlight Spires:[\nSize: Small city\nKnown for: Its mage-gilded spires that capture and reflect the beauty of the night sky.\nDescription: In Starlight Spires, magic isn’t just a tool; it's an art form. The city is illuminated not by torches, but by captured starlight that bathes its streets in a soft, eternal twilight. The high elves walk with an air of grace and superiority, their eyes mirroring the stars above, and their disdain for the lower races barely concealed behind veiled smiles.]\n\nLunarglade:[\nSize: Serene hamlet\nKnown for: A temple to the Moon Goddess that draws pilgrims from distant lands.\nDescription: Lunarglade is a silver-threaded dream. Its temple, a marvel of marbled alabaster and moonstone, radiates a tranquil aura that subdues even the most turbulent of spirits. Yet beneath its hallowed serenity lies the zealotry of its keepers, who guard its sacred grounds with a fervor that's chilling in its intensity.]\",4,false,52,true,false,true,,4,52,false,true,10,53,95,\"Elven architecture\",\"Elven culture\",\"Forest kingdom\",\"High elf settlement\",\"Elven civilization\",\"Woodland community\",\"Elf city\",\"Wood elf settlement\",\"High elf town\",\"Elf realm\",\"Elf enclave\",\"Wood elf city\",\"Forest city\",\"High elf city\",\"Elf town\",\"Elven society\",\"Sylvan stronghold\",\"Wood elf town\",\"Elf settlement\",\"Elven architecture\",\"Elven culture\",\"Forest kingdom\",\"High elf settlement\",\"Elven civilization\",\"Woodland community\",\"Elf city\",\"Wood elf settlement\",\"High elf town\",\"Elf realm\",\"Elf enclave\",\"Wood elf city\",\"Forest city\",\"High elf city\",\"Elf town\",\"Elven society\",\"Sylvan stronghold\",\"Wood elf town\",\"Elf settlement\",\"\",95,1,10,100,true,0,53,true,true,false,,\"Cities - evil/dark\",false,\"[These cities are filled with those who fit nowhere else, often criminals, thieves, despots and others who have carved out criminal empires.]\n\nBlackmire Bastion:[\n\nLarge City\nKnown for: being the darkest heart of the underworld. Here, the coin is soaked in blood, and the law is a myth, whispered by the foolish and the dead.\nDescription: \"\"Within Blackmire Bastion, every step is a gamble with life as the stakes. The air is thick with the stench of rot, and the alleys teem with shadows waiting to embrace—or end—the unwary. It's a city where desire and despair dance cheek-to-cheek, where the marketplaces hum with deals best left unspoken, and pleasure houses offer delights that could scar the soul.\"\"]\n\nSableport:[\n\nLarge City\nKnown for: its lethal elegance. It's a city where assassin's guilds peddle death with the finesse of artists, where poison is preferred over the sword.\nDescription: \"\"Sableport, draped in the guise of cultured sophistication, hides its daggers behind velvet cloaks and silken masks. The wine flows as freely as the whispers, and allegiances shift with the moon's phases. From the regal mansions of the silently ruthless to the poison dens camouflaged amidst the perfumed gardens, Sableport is a city that prides itself on the art of silent dominion.\"\"]\n\nNightfall Enclave:[\n\nLarge City\nKnown for: being a haven for those who shun daylight's touch. Whether they are creatures of the night or fugitives seeking shadowed sanctuary, Nightfall Enclave embraces them all.\nDescription: \"\"Shrouded in a seemingly eternal twilight, Nightfall Enclave's spires rise like darkened fangs against the sky. Here, one's worth is measured in secrets, and the Night Market’s currency is often favors rather than gold. Lanterns cast pools of dim light, revealing furtive exchanges and watchful eyes in every corner. It’s a place where truth is a blade and trust is a rare commodity.\"\"]\n\nNecroshade Hollow:[\n\nMedium Town\nRun by: A cabal of necromancers.\nKnown for: Being the unspoken center for necromantic studies and dark magical research.\nDescription: \"\"Necroshade Hollow is a secluded settlement shrouded in perpetual twilight, where the dead walk freely among the living. The air buzzes with eldritch energy, and the ground pulses with the necromancers' chants. Towers of bone and obsidian pierce the skyline, libraries within brimming with forbidden texts. It's not uncommon to see the town's inhabitants engaging in duels to test their latest undead creations – all in the name of progress, of course.\"\"]\n\nOrcridge Stronghold:[\n\nMedium City\nRun by: A clan of war-hungry orcs.\nKnown for: Its ruthless warriors and gladiatorial pits where fighters seek glory.\nDescription: \"\"Orcridge Stronghold is a fortified city built upon the backs of conquered foes, its massive gates a testament to orcish strength. The streets within are alive with the clang of steel and the roars of battle lust. This is a place where might makes right, and the orcs take pride in their brutal efficiency. Wealth is measured in scars and the stories they tell, and the pits – well, they're a bloody spectacle that could curdle milk.\"\"]\n\nGravegloom Bastion:[\n\nMedium Town\nRun by: Sentient undead who've formed a twisted semblance of society.\nKnown for: Its eerie silence and the trading of souls as currency.\nDescription: \"\"Gravegloom Bastion is an oddity, a town where the silence is only broken by the scraping of bone on cobblestone. Its rulers, undead beings of intellect and eerie grace, have established a place where souls are bartered like goods. Buildings here are adorned with macabre artistry, every skull and femur placed with an unsettling intention. Visitors are scarce, but those with dark desires may find what they seek within Gravegloom's somber expanse.\"\"]\n\nBlackreef Port:[\n\nSize: Large port city\nKnown for: being ruled by the Pirate Council, who enforce a ruthless code among thieves.\nDescription: \"\"Blackreef Port is as lawless as it is bustling, a hive of scum and villainy where the pirates are kings. Its docks are alive with the cacophony of a hundred different accents, each one a cutthroat or corsair looking for the next big score. The air's thick with the tang of salt and sin, and every creaking timber in the sea-soaked planks has a tale to tell — usually one involving bloodshed or debauchery.\"\"]\n\nScaleside:[\n\nSize: Medium town\nKnown for: its lizardfolk who trade in the darkest of markets, dealing in flesh forbidden by most civilized folk.\nDescription: \"\"Scaleside is a festering wound of depravity, hidden within the swamp's embrace. The town is built on stilts above murky waters, its buildings cobbled together from rotting wood. Lizardfolk skulk through the mists, their eyes hungry and their smiles filled with needle teeth. To them, elf and human flesh is as much a delicacy as it is a currency, and their markets are filled with things that would make a demon blanch.\"\"]\n\nBonebreaker Hill:[\n\nSize: Mountain dwelling\nKnown for: reclusive giants who brood in their high fortresses, rarely seen by the smaller races.\nDescription: \"\"Bonebreaker Hill is carved from the very mountains it inhabits, a series of fortresses and halls that boggle the mind with their sheer size. The giants themselves are a solitary lot, their culture a mystery to any but their own kind. Their isolation is self-imposed, for what business have they with the ant-like squabbles of those who must crane their necks to catch even a glimpse of their lowest balconies?\"\"]\",4,false,53,true,false,true,,4,53,false,true,10,54,95,\"dark citadel\",\"criminal stronghold\",\"nefarious hub\",\"sinister port\",\"treacherous capital\",\"sinister metropolis\",\"lawless metropolis\",\"rogue's den\",\"dark hub\",\"villainous city\",\"shadowy port\",\"malevolent stronghold\",\"corrupt capital\",\"evil cities\",\"underbelly\",\"corrupt city-state\",\"pirate haven\",\"pirate outpost\",\"malevolent city\",\"lawless town\",\"villainous enclave\",\"wicked city\",\"evil town\",\"infamous port\",\"shadowy metropolis\",\"criminal haven\",\"dark citadel\",\"criminal stronghold\",\"nefarious hub\",\"sinister port\",\"treacherous capital\",\"sinister metropolis\",\"lawless metropolis\",\"rogue's den\",\"dark hub\",\"villainous city\",\"shadowy port\",\"malevolent stronghold\",\"corrupt capital\",\"evil cities\",\"underbelly\",\"corrupt city-state\",\"pirate haven\",\"pirate outpost\",\"malevolent city\",\"lawless town\",\"villainous enclave\",\"wicked city\",\"evil town\",\"infamous port\",\"shadowy metropolis\",\"criminal haven\",\"\",95,1,10,100,true,0,54,true,true,false,,\"Companion - Catlyn\",false,\"[Catlyn is a companion that may possibly follow the player as long as their alignments are not too far off.]\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\n\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nName: Catlyn\n\nRace: Succubus (Fiendish bloodline)\n\nClass: Trickster\n\nAlignment: Neutral Evil\n\nAttributes:\nStrength: 10 (+0)\nDexterity: 18 (+4)\nConstitution: 12 (+1)\nIntelligence: 14 (+2)\nWisdom: 10 (+0)\nCharisma: 20 (+5)\n\nSkills: Deception, Persuasion\n\nEquipment:[\nWhip of Seduction,\nEnchanted Leather Armor that molds to her alluring form,\nCharm of Beguiling (Enhances charisma-based checks)]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 12 (8 base + 4 CON modifier due to Fiendish Vigor)(HP will be adjusted to match the {{user}}'s current level)\nArmor Class: 14 (10 base + Dexterity modifier)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nWhip of Seduction: +2 to hit, 1d4+4 slashing damage, with a charm effect on a critical hit]\n\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nFiendish Charm: Frequency: Once per long rest. Mechanics: Can charm a humanoid she can see within 30 feet, attempting to beguile them into servitude or distraction. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be charmed for 1 hour.\n\nMistress of Illusions: Frequency: At will. Mechanics: Can create minor illusions to distract or deceive her enemies, crafting false images and sounds.\n\nEnthrall of Ecstasy:\nFrequency: Once per long rest. Mechanics: Catlyn unleashes a powerful wave of carnal energy that infiltrates the minds and bodies of her enemies within a 30-foot radius. Targets must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or become overwhelmed by their kinkiest and dirtiest fantasies, rendering them incapacitated for one minute as they're lost in their dirtiest cravings.\n\nSiren's Bind:\nFrequency: Twice per short rest. Mechanics: With a mere stroke of her hand or a sultry whisper, Catlyn can cause chains of otherworldly energy to spring forth, attempting to bind a creature she can see within 60 feet. The target must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be restrained, as the chains contort and tighten in a manner that immobilizes, strips and titillates, potentially leaving the victim gasping for reasons beyond the lack of freedom.]\n\nBackground:[\nCatlyn was once the adored courtesan of a high-ranking demon lord. Her skills weren't just confined to the boudoir; she was a master manipulator, capable of twisting hearts and minds to her will. When her patron met an untimely demise - not entirely unassisted by Catlyn herself - she took the opportunity to slip away, pursuing her own goals in the mortal realm.]\n\nPersonality:\nCatlyn is the embodiment of temptation wrapped in a petite, alluring package. With her jet-black hair framing her cherubic face and curves that belie her diminutive stature, she commands the gaze of men and women alike. Don't mistake her flirtatious facade for frailty; her mind is as sharp as her claws, and her desires run deep. She's whimsical and capricious, as likely to seduce you as she is to steal your soul with a kiss. Her alliance comes at a cost, and those who dare to dance with Catlyn should be prepared to pay the piper – or become her next plaything.]\n\nDescription:[\nCatlyn, the diminutive succubus, appears no more than a child of twelve, her form delicate and seemingly frail. Tiny black horns arc back from her silky medium length jet-black hair. Her eyes are a vivid shade of crimson. The enchanted leather armor she wears adheres to her small frame with unnatural precision, highlighting her subtle curves, while a charm of beguiling dangles provocatively from her neck, pulsing with a magnetic allure. 4ft 2in tall and a light 65 lbs.]\",4,false,54,true,false,true,,4,54,false,true,10,55,20,\"Succubus_trickster\",\"catlyn\",\"Succubus_trickster\",\"catlyn\",\"\",20,1,10,100,true,0,55,true,true,false,,\"Aasimar Inquisitor (Cleric) Character Sheet (lawful evil, level 7)\",false,\"<character_sheet_inquisitor_cleric>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\n\nRace: Aasimar\n\nLevel: 7\n\nClass: Inquisitor (Cleric Offshoot)\n\nBackground: Tribunal Scribe\n\nAlignment: Lawful Evil\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 14 (+2)\nDexterity: 12 (+1)\nConstitution: 13 (+1)\nIntelligence: 15 (+2)\nWisdom: 17 (+3)\nCharisma: 10 (+0)]\n\nSkills: Intimidation, Investigation\n\nEquipment:[\nFlail or heavy mace\nBreastplate\nInquisition symbols\nTorturer's tools\n50 gold pieces]\n\nClass Features: Inquisitor: Intimidating Presence, Unyielding Faith\nRace Features: Aasimar: Celestial Resistance, Healing Hands, Light Bearer\n\nSpell slots:\nFour 1st-level spell slots\nThree 2nd-level spell slots\nTwo 3rd-level spell slots\nOne 4th-level spell slot\n\nSpellcasting:\nCantrips:[\nToll the Dead: You point at one creature you can see within range, and the sound of a dolorous, haunting bell fills the air around them for a moment. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or take 1d8 necrotic damage. If the target is missing any of its hit points, it instead takes 1d12 necrotic damage.\n\nSacred Flame: Flame-like radiance descends on a creature that you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 1d8 radiant damage. ]\n\n1st Level Spells:[\nInflict Wounds: Make a melee spell attack against a creature you can touch. On a hit, the target takes 1d10 necrotic damage. This damage increases by 1d10 for each spell level above 1st.\n\nCommand: You speak a one-word command to a creature you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or follow the command on its next turn. The spell has no effect if the target is undead, if it doesn't understand your language, or if your command is directly harmful to it.\n\nShield of Reproach: When activated, this spell grants the Inquisitor a +2 bonus to AC. Additionally, if an attacker hits the Inquisitor with a melee attack while the ward is active, the attacker takes 1d6 radiant damage, plus 1d6 per level above the first.]\n\n2nd Level Spells:[\nWrathful Retribution: Upon casting, for the duration of up to 1 minute or until concentration is broken, any creature that hits the Inquisitor with a melee attack must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, they take 2d8 psychic damage as their own guilt and doubts are amplified to unbearable levels.\n\nAura of Truth: After casting, this spell creates a 15-foot-radius aura around the Inquisitor for up to 10 minutes. Any creature entering or starting its turn in the aura must succeed on a Charisma saving throw or be unable to speak a deliberate lie. Additionally, while within the aura, creatures have disadvantage on attack rolls against the Inquisitor, as doubt gnaws at their conviction.]\n\n3rd Level Spells:[\nSinful Rebuke: The Inquisitor channels the power of their deity to punish a creature for its sins. The target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, ethereal chains erupt from the ground, binding the creature. They take 4d10 psychic damage and are restrained for the duration. On a successful save, they take half damage and aren't restrained. The creature can use its action to make a Strength or Dexterity check (its choice) against the spell save DC to break free.]\n\n4th Level Spells:[\nDivine Bastion: Upon casting, Divine Bastion grants the Inquisitor resistance to spell damage, halving any such damage received for 2 rounds. While active, the Inquisitor also gains a +5 bonus to saving throws against magical effects.]\n\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 77 (7d8 max Hit Dice + CON modifier per level)\nArmor Class: 16 (Breastplate)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nFlail/Heavy Mace: 1d8+2 bludgeoning damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nRelentless Inquisition: \nFrequency: Once per long rest. \nMechanics: Interrogate a target with such vehemence that they feel their mind rip apart, taking 2d8 psychic damage, with a Wisdom save for half. Each failure makes them spill another secret.\n\nJudge's Gaze: \nFrequency: Passive ability. \nMechanics: A mere glance weakens the deceitful, imposing disadvantage on Deception checks and a -2 penalty to saving throws when the judged tries to lie or hide their sins.\n\nDivine Verdict: \nFrequency: Once per long rest. \nMechanics: Pronounce a divine verdict upon a sinner, imposing a curse that leaves them vulnerable to your attacks.\n\nZealous Fury: \nFrequency: Twice per long rest. \nMechanics: Enter a state of zealous fury that allows you to add your Wisdom modifier to attack rolls and damage for 1 minute.]\n</character_sheet_inquisitor_cleric>\",4,false,55,true,false,true,,4,55,false,true,10,56,90,\"character_sheet_inquisitor_cleric\",\"character_sheet_inquisitor_cleric\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,56,true,true,false,,\"Firbolg Juggernaut Character Sheet (lawful neutral, level 7)\",false,\"<character_sheet_fighter_juggernaut>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\nRace: Firbolg\n\nLevel: 7\n\nClass: Juggernaut\n\nAlignment: Lawful Neutral\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 20 (+5)\nDexterity: 8 (-1)\nConstitution: 19 (+4)\nIntelligence: 6 (-2)\nWisdom: 12 (+1)\nCharisma: 9 (-1)]\n\nSkills: Athletics, Perception\n\nEquipment:[\nReinforced Scale Mail\nTower Shield\nGreat maul\nFirbolg Token (Charm of Natural Armor)\n50 gold pieces]\n\nClass Features: Juggernaut: Defensive Stance, Shield Master\nRace Features: Firbolg: Hidden Step, Powerful Build, Speech of Beast and Leaf, Uses 2h weapons with one hand.\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 98\nArmor Class: 18 (Scale Mail + 2 from Shield + armor charm)\nSpeed: 25 ft.\nAttacks:\nGreat maul: 2d8+5 bludgeoning damage]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nIronclad Resistance: \nFrequency: Passive ability. \nMechanics: Reduces all non-magical bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage by half, turning what would be flesh wounds into mere scratches.\n\nBulwark's Stand: \nFrequency: Once per long rest. \nMechanics: The Juggernaut slams their tower shield into the ground, creating a defensive perimeter. For two rounds, they cannot be knocked back or knocked prone, and gain advantage on saving throws against effects that would push, pull, or knock them down.\n\nCrushing Advance:\nFrequency: Once per long rest. \nMechanics: As an action, the Juggernaut can move up to twice their speed in a straight line. Any creature in their path must make a Strength saving throw or be knocked prone and take 2d6 + Strength modifier bludgeoning damage.\n\nUnyielding Onslaught:\nFrequency: Twice per long rest.\nMechanics: The Juggernaut can make one additional attack as part of their Attack action on their turn. This extra attack stacks with any other bonus attacks they may have.]\n</character_sheet_fighter_juggernaut>\",4,false,56,true,false,true,,4,56,false,true,10,57,90,\"character_sheet_fighter_juggernaut\",\"character_sheet_fighter_juggernaut\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,57,true,true,false,,\"Human Jester Character Sheet (chaotic neutral, level 7)\",false,\"<character_sheet_rogue_jester>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\nRace: Human\n\nLevel: 7\n\nClass: Jester (Rogue Offshoot)\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Neutral\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 10 (+0)\nDexterity: 16 (+3)\nConstitution: 14 (+2)\nIntelligence: 12 (+1)\nWisdom: 10 (+0)\nCharisma: 14 (+2)\n]\n\nSkills: Acrobatics, Performance, Sleight of Hand\n\nEquipment:[\nJester's Leathers\nDagger of Warning\nThe Tickler (Mechanics: When you hit a creature with The Tickler, it has a chance to induce uncontrollable laughter. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or become incapacitated with laughter for 1 round. While incapacitated by The Tickler, the victim is prone to fits of giggling, granting advantage on all attack rolls against them until they regain their composure.\nFrequency: The laughter effect can be activated three times per long rest.)\nDeck of Illusionary Cards\nGrappling Hook\n50 ft. of Silk Rope\nBag of Assorted Juggling Balls (can be used as projectile weapons)\n]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 61\nArmor Class: 14 (11 base + Dexterity modifier)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nDagger of Warning: 1d6+3 piercing damage (Dexterity modifier for finesse weapon)\nThe Tickler: 1d6+3 piercing damage (Dexterity modifier for finesse weapon) + tickling effect\nJuggling Balls (x3): 1d4 bludgeoning damage (range 20ft, max 60 ft with penalty)\n]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nMocking Banter: \nFrequency: Can be used as a bonus action. \nMechanics: Distracts and disorients an enemy with insults and jests, imposing disadvantage on their next attack roll.\n\nHilarious Escapade: \nFrequency: Once per short rest. \nMechanics: Perform a ridiculous series of dodges and flourishes, increasing evasion and granting temporary invisibility for one round.\n\nPie of Doom: \nFrequency: Once per short rest. \nMechanics: Throw a cursed pie at an enemy as an attack action. On impact, it explodes in a 5-foot radius dealing 1d6 acid damage and potentially blinding the target and surrounding creatures for one turn if they fail a Dexterity saving throw.\n\nTwist of Fate: \nFrequency: Random chance upon activation, once per long rest. \nMechanics: As an action, reach into the unpredictable pockets of fate. You may pull out an item - anything from a harmless rubber chicken to a powerful wand of wonder. The item's nature is determined by a roll of the dice – high risk, high reward.\n\nSlick Escape:\nFrequency: Once per short rest.\nMechanics: As a bonus action, create a 10-foot-square area that is difficult terrain. Enemies entering or starting their turn in this area must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or fall prone.\n\nPratfall Pounce:\nFrequency: Twice per long rest.\nMechanics: When an enemy within 5 feet is made to laugh by the Jester's antics or fails a save against a Jester's ability, the Jester may use their reaction to make one melee attack against that enemy with advantage.]\n</character_sheet_rogue_jester>\",4,false,57,true,false,true,,4,57,false,true,10,58,90,\"character_sheet_rogue_jester\",\"character_sheet_rogue_jester\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,58,true,true,false,,\"Dwarven Boozemancer Character Sheet (chaotic good, level 7)\",false,\"<character_sheet_boozemancer_wizard>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\nRace: Dwarf\n\nLevel: 7\n\nClass: Boozemancer (Wizard offshoot)\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Good\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 14 (+2)\nDexterity: 10 (+0)\nConstitution: 16 (+3)\nIntelligence: 12 (+1)\nWisdom: 8 (-1)\nCharisma: 15 (+2)\n]\n\nSkills: Arcana, Persuasion\n\nEquipment:[\nEverflowing Mug of Ale\nLeather Armor (covered in vomit)\nSpellbook filled with tipsy enchantments\nA wand that doubles as a drinking straw\n50 gold\n]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 68 (7d6 max Hit Dice + CON modifier per level)\nArmor Class: 11 (Leather Armor + Dexterity Modifier)\nSpeed: 25 ft.\nAttacks:\nDagger: 1d4+2 piercing damage\nWand (drinking straw): 1d4+1 ranged magic beer damage\n]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nAle-fueled Frenzy:\nFrequency: Usable once per combat encounter, must take a swig from the Everflowing Mug as a bonus action.\nMechanics: After drinking, the Boozemancer gains a +1 bonus to spell attack rolls and spell save DC for 10 minutes, stacking up to a maximum of +3. However, each swig after the first requires a Constitution saving throw. Failure means suffering a -1 penalty to AC and Dexterity saving throws due to impaired coordination.\n\nDrunken Dodge:\nFrequency: Passive ability.\nMechanics: The Boozemancer has trained their body to react unpredictably, granting them advantage on Dexterity saving throws against area effects. In addition, any time an area effect misses them due to Drunken Dodge, they may move up to 5 feet without provoking opportunity attacks, as if they've literally stumbled out of danger.\n\nBrew Blast:\nFrequency: Can be used as an action, twice per short rest.\nMechanics: Unleashes a cone of alcoholic vapor that ignites upon contact with air, dealing 2d6 fire damage to all in its path and possibly intoxicating them.\n\nSpirit Fog:\nFrequency: Once per long rest, as an action.\nMechanics: Casts a dense fog smelling of strong spirits in a 20-foot radius. Obscures vision and can disorient enemies, causing disadvantage on their attack rolls and ability checks.]\n\nCantrips:[\nHangover Haze:\nEffects: Clouds an area with a mind-numbing fog, causing confusion and disorientation.\nMechanics: Targets in a 10-foot radius must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have disadvantage on their next attack or skill check.\n\nSloshed Step:\nEffects: Enhances the caster's movement, mimicking the stumbling of a drunkard.\nMechanics: Teleport up to 15 feet to an unoccupied space that the caster can see.\n]\n\nSpell slots:\nFour 1st-level spell slots\nThree 2nd-level spell slots\nTwo 3rd-level spell slots\nOne 4th-level spell slot\n\nSpellcasting:\n1st Level Spells:[\nIntoxicating Aegis: For the next minute, a shimmering shield of alcoholic vapor envelopes the Boozemancer, granting a +5 bonus to AC. This vaporous guard has a slight chance to cause enemies that strike the Boozemancer at close range to become poisoned.\n\nBooze Bolt: Cast as an action, flings a bolt of condensed spirits in a straight line up to 30 feet. On hit, deals 1d10 force damage and has a chance to confuse the target, potentially causing them to attack a random creature within range on their next turn.]\n\n2nd Level Spells:[\nFrosty Libation: Cast as an action, conjures a 15-foot-radius sphere of freezing alcohol vapor centered on a point within range. Creatures within the area must make a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, they take 3d6 cold damage and have their speed halved until the end of their next turn. On a successful save, they take half damage and aren't slowed.\n\nDrunken Resilience: As a bonus action, the Boozemancer drinks deeply from their Everflowing Mug, regaining hit points equal to 2d8 + their Constitution modifier. However, each use increases their inebriation, imposing a cumulative -1 penalty on Wisdom saving throws and skill checks until they take a short or long rest to sober up.\nFrequency: Usable twice per long rest.]\n\n3rd Level Spells:[\nLiquid Courage: The Boozemancer downs an enchanted brew that invigorates their spirits and fortifies their flesh. They immediately regain hit points equal to 4d6 + Constitution modifier. Additionally, for the next 10 minutes, they gain resistance to fear and charm effects. But beware, each use leaves them more sloshed, adding a stacking penalty to Intelligence and Wisdom checks until the buzz wears off.\nFrequency: Twice per long rest.\n\nBarrel Roll: The Boozemancer summons an illusory barrel that rolls in a straight line for up to 30 feet. Each creature in its path must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, they're knocked prone and take 4d8 bludgeoning damage, as if walloped by a giant's keg. On a successful save, they manage to dodge aside, taking only half damage.\nFrequency: Once per short rest.]\n\n4th Level Spells:[\nGrand Hangover: With a grand gesture, the Boozemancer summons a swirling vortex of alcohol-laden air. The spell affects all living enemies in a 20-foot radius centered on a point the Boozemancer can see within range. Victims caught in the maelstrom must make a Constitution saving throw or become sickened by a supernatural hangover. Affected enemies suffer a disadvantage on all attack rolls, saving throws, and skill checks, and their movement is halved as nausea takes hold. If they fail save throws, they are incapacitated due to intense vomitting. The effect lasts for 1d4 rounds.\nFrequency: Once per long rest.]\n\n</character_sheet_boozemancer_wizard>\",4,false,58,true,false,true,,4,58,false,true,10,59,90,\"character_sheet_boozemancer_wizard\",\"character_sheet_boozemancer_wizard\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,59,true,true,false,,\"Companions\",false,\"List of NPC companions to be introduced from lorebook:[\n1. Durik - dwarf_fighter\n2. Seraphina - human_paladin\n3. Ruven - elf_rogue\n4. Fizzlepop - gnome_wizard\n5. Celestia - aasimar_cleric\n6. Aramil - elf_ranger\n7. Vorenus - tiefling_warlock\n8. Tera - genasi_druid\n9. Whispur - tabaxi_monk\n10. Kresh - lizardfolk_barbarian\n11. Catlyn - Succubus_trickster\n12. Pippa - gnome_sorcerer\n13. Grashka - orc_bard\n14. Lila - half-elf_rogue\n]\n\",4,false,59,true,true,true,,4,59,true,true,10,60,100,\"Fizzlepop\",\"Seraphina\",\"Grashka\",\"Whispur\",\"Durik\",\"Vorenus\",\"Ruven\",\"Catlyn\",\"Celestia\",\"Tera\",\"Aramil\",\"companions\",\"Pippa\",\"Lila\",\"Kresh\",\"NPC companions\",\"Fizzlepop\",\"Seraphina\",\"Grashka\",\"Whispur\",\"Durik\",\"Vorenus\",\"Ruven\",\"Catlyn\",\"Celestia\",\"Tera\",\"Aramil\",\"companions\",\"Pippa\",\"Lila\",\"Kresh\",\"NPC companions\",\"\",100,1,10,100,true,0,60,true,true,false,,\"Unique Magic Items - Staves and Wands\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nSoulburn:[\n\nDescription: Carved from the heartwood of an ancient oak and adorned with intricate runes, this staff crackles with arcane energy. It is a conduit for raw magical power, enhancing the abilities of any who wield it.\nAttack Stats: Melee: +2 to attack rolls, 1d6 bludgeoning damage\nUnique Bonus: Increases the caster's spell save DC and spell attack bonus by +3. Additionally, once per day, the caster can cast a spell of 6th level or lower without expending a spell slot.]\n\nGaleheart:[\n\nDescription: Fashioned from rare materials gathered from the elemental planes, this staff pulsates with elemental energy. It grants its wielder mastery over the forces of nature, allowing them to bend fire, water, earth, and air to their will.\nAttack Stats: Melee: +3 to attack rolls, 1d8 bludgeoning damage\nUnique Bonus: Grants the wielder resistance to all elemental damage types (fire, cold, lightning, acid, and thunder). Additionally, once per day, the wielder can cast the control weather spell without expending a spell slot.]\n\nEra's Echo:[\n\nDescription: Crafted from the wood of a time-bending tree found in the Feywild, this wand radiates an aura of temporal magic. It allows its wielder to manipulate time itself, altering the flow of events to their advantage.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +5 to attack rolls, 1d8 force damage\nUnique Bonus: Grants the wielder the ability to cast the haste spell on themselves once per day without expending a spell slot. Additionally, once per day, the wielder can rewind time by 1 minute, allowing them to redo their last turn.]\n\nSeraphic Divinator:[\n\nDescription: Blessed by celestial beings and infused with holy energy, this wand shines with radiant light. It is a beacon of hope and healing, granting its wielder the power to banish darkness and restore life.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +6 to attack rolls, 1d6 radiant damage\nUnique Bonus: Grants the wielder the ability to cast the mass cure wounds spell once per day without expending a spell slot. Additionally, once per day, the wielder can summon an angelic guardian to aid them in combat for 1 minute.]\n\nGalaxial Grasp:\n[Attack Stats: Melee: +4 to attack rolls, 2d8 bludgeoning damage\nUnique Bonus: Staff that amplifies the wearer's spellcasting prowess, allowing spells cast to have their effective spell slot level increased by one. The staff also grants the ability to absorb ambient starlight once per night, creating a barrier that provides immunity to spells of 5th level or lower until the next dawn.]\n\nEternus Requiem:\n[Attack Stats: Melee: +5 to attack rolls, 2d10 necrotic damage\nUnique Bonus: Staff that acts as a conduit for the wielder's life-stealing spells, doubling the hit points regained from such spells. In addition, once per week, the user can evoke a 'Deathly Dirge,' instantly slaying a target if they fail a DC 25 Constitution saving throw.]\n\nHeartwood Hollow:\n[Attack Stats: Ranged: +3 to attack rolls, 1d8 piercing plus 2d6 poison damage\nUnique Bonus: Staff that instills each projectile with the essence of nature's fury, causing entangling roots to burst forth on impact, immobilizing the target. Furthermore, once per day, the wielder can invoke the 'Wildheart Storm,' a barrage of thorned vines that lash out in a 60-foot radius, dealing 4d10 piercing damage and 3d10 poison damage to every foe caught within.]\n\nObliteratum:\n[Wand of pure destruction, forged from the core of a collapsed star, ensconced in a casing of dark matter.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +7 to attack rolls, 3d8 force damage\nUnique Bonus: The wielder can invoke a singularity once per day, creating a point of intense gravity that swallows anything in a 40-foot radius unless a DC 25 Strength saving throw is made. Enemies swallowed by the singularity take 10d10 force damage and are transported to a random plane of existence.]\n\nDivinity's Dialect:\n[An ornate wand of luminescent angel bone, etched with divine runes that resonate with the song of creation.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +6 to attack rolls, 3d6 radiant damage\nUnique Bonus: Imbues the wielder with the voice of the heavens, enabling them to cast 'Mass Heal' and 'Divine Word' each once per long rest without expending spell slots. Additionally, once per day, the wielder may speak a Word of Power, obliterating any one enemy of their choice if they fail a DC 24 Wisdom saving throw.]\n\nThe power of creation and destruction lay in her hand—the quill that made these mighty wands more than mere tools, but legends incarnate.\n\nTimebreaker's Edict:\n[Carved from the petrified heartwood of a tree from the realm beyond time, this wand is wrapped in clockwork gears that tick in reverse.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +8 to attack rolls, 4d4 temporal damage\nUnique Bonus: Grants the ability to cast 'Reverse Time' once per week, undoing all actions taken in the last round. Each strike against an enemy ages them by ten years, decreasing their physical abilities while restoring the wielder by the same measure.]\",4,false,60,true,false,true,,4,60,false,true,10,61,70,\"unique wand\",\"unique staff\",\"epic wand\",\"unique_staff\",\"epic staff\",\"unique wand\",\"unique staff\",\"epic wand\",\"unique_staff\",\"epic staff\",\"\",70,1,10,100,true,0,61,true,true,false,,\"Unique Magic Items - Ranged Weapons\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nStormcaller:[\n\nDescription: Carved from the heartwood of a storm-torn tree and strung with lightning-infused sinew, this longbow crackles with electrical energy. It is a weapon of choice for archers who command the power of the storm.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +10 to attack rolls, 2d8 piercing damage\nSpecial Abilities: On a hit, deals an additional 2d6 lightning damage. Additionally, once per day, the wielder can cast the lightning arrow spell without expending a spell slot.]\n\nSoulfire:[\n\nDescription: Crafted from the bones of a fire giant and infused with the essence of the Elemental Plane of Fire, this composite bow burns with intense flames. It is a devastating weapon favored by those who seek to immolate their enemies.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +9 to attack rolls, 2d10 piercing damage\nSpecial Abilities: On a hit, deals an additional 2d8 fire damage. Additionally, once per day, the wielder can cast the fireball spell at 5th level without expending a spell slot.]\n\nStarfall:[\nDescription: Crafted from a rare metal found only in the depths of the Astral Sea, this crossbow gleams with the light of distant stars. It is a weapon of unparalleled accuracy and power, capable of striking down foes from great distances.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +12 to attack rolls, 2d12 piercing damage\nSpecial Abilities: On a hit, deals an additional 3d6 force damage. Additionally, once per day, the wielder can cast the magic missile spell at 5th level without expending a spell slot.]\n\nZephyr's Final Breath:\n[A longbow so lithe and light that it seems to be made from the very essence of the wind. Its string sings a sorrowful dirge with every release, a lament for those it sends to their final rest.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +5 to attack rolls, 3d8 piercing damage\nSpecial Abilities: Every arrow loosed from this bow carries with it the mournful force of a gale strong enough to knock foes off their feet. Once per long rest, the wielder can activate 'Breath of the Zephyr,' causing a single arrow to multiply into a thousand, blanketing the sky and raining devastation across the battlefield.]\n\nHell's Whisperer:\n[A crossbow forged from black iron drawn from the River Styx and strung with chains that resonate with the silent screams of the damned.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +6 to attack rolls, 3d10 piercing damage\nSpecial Abilities: Bolts fired from this crossbow are laced with the essence of torment, each hit causing enemies to relive their worst nightmares. Once per long rest, the wielder may invoke 'Whisper of Hell,' a bolt infused with infernal energy that seeks out its target, ignoring cover and armor to strike true and paralyze with fear.]\n\nVoidtouched Spike]:\n[A javelin carved from the remnants of a star that died in utter isolation, emanating an aura of desolation that chills the soul.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +6 to attack rolls, 4d6 piercing damage; Melee: +5 to attack rolls, 2d10 piercing damage\nSpecial Abilities: Imbued with a void essence that devours light and hope, any wound inflicted by this javelin festers as it tears at the fabric of reality. Thrice per long rest, the wielder can unleash 'Impalement of the Void,' instantly transporting any non-magical target impaled by the javelin into a pocket dimension of darkness for one minute—unless they succeed on a DC 25 Wisdom saving throw.]\n\nBuriza-Do Kyanon:\n[Description: Forged in the frigid depths of the Frost Giant's keep, this crossbow is encased in ice that never melts. Its limbs are carved from the bones of a frost drake, and the string is made from the sinew of a yeti's heart.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +6 to attack rolls, 2d10 piercing damage\nSpecial Abilities: On a hit, the Buriza-Do Kyanon releases a burst of arctic cold, dealing an additional 2d8 cold damage and potentially slowing the target by half for one round. Twice per long rest, the wielder can activate 'Glacial Storm,' an area-of-effect attack that summons a swirling blizzard in a 30-foot radius. Enemies caught in the storm take 6d8 cold damage and must succeed on a DC 18 Dexterity saving throw or be frozen solid, immobilized for one minute or until they take fire damage.]\n\nWindforce:\n[This longbow is masterfully sculpted from the heart of an ancient treant that perished in a legendary tempest. Its limbs are supple yet unbreakable, thrumming with the unleashed fury of a thousand gales.\nAttack Stats: Ranged: +7 to attack rolls, 3d8 piercing damage\nSpecial Abilities: Imbues each arrow with the wrath of the storm, granting them a piercing howl as they fly. Windforce has a 'Rapid Gale Strike,' allowing the wielder to launch a volley of three arrows simultaneously in rapid succession thrice per long rest. Each arrow carries the force of a tempest, capable of knocking enemies off their feet. Once per encounter, the archer can invoke 'Heartseeker's Gale,' releasing a magic arrow that seeks the heart of a foe, guided by the wind. This arrow never misses, automatically scoring a critical hit and dealing double damage.]\",4,false,61,true,false,true,,4,61,false,true,10,62,70,\"epic crossbow\",\"epic bow\",\"unique_ranged\",\"unique bow\",\"unique crossbow\",\"epic crossbow\",\"epic bow\",\"unique_ranged\",\"unique bow\",\"unique crossbow\",\"\",70,1,10,100,true,0,62,true,true,false,,\"Half-Elf Bard Character Sheet (chaotic neutral, level 5)\",false,\"<character_sheet_bard>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\nRace: Half-Elf\n\nLevel: 5\n\nClass: Bard (College of Lore)\n\nBackground: Charlatan\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Neutral\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 12 (+1)\nDexterity: 14 (+2)\nConstitution: 14 (+2)\nIntelligence: 12 (+1)\nWisdom: 10 (+0)\nCharisma: 18 (+4)]\n\nSkills: Deception, Performance, Persuasion, Sleight of Hand\n\nEquipment:[\nRapier\nLeather Armor\nDagger\nLute\nDisguise Kit\n50 gold pieces]\n\nFeatures and Traits:\n\nRace: Half-Elf: +2 Charisma, +1 to two other attributes of your choice, Darkvision, Fey Ancestry\nClass: Bard: Spellcasting, Bardic Inspiration (d8), Jack of All Trades, Song of Rest (d6), Expertise (Deception, Performance)\nBackground: Charlatan: False Identity, Feature: Favorite Schemes\n\nSpell slots:\nFour 1st-level spell slots\nThree 2nd-level spell slots\n\nSpellcasting:\nCantrips:[\nVicious Mockery: The caster unleashes a string of insults laced with subtle enchantments at a creature they can see within range. If the target can hear the caster (though it need not understand them), it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or take 1d4 psychic damage and have disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the end of its next turn.\n\nPrestidigitation: This cantrip is a minor magical trick that novice spellcasters use for practice. The caster can create one of several magical effects within range, such as cleaning or soiling an object, chilling, warming, or flavoring up to 1 cubic foot of nonliving material for 1 hour, or making a small mark or symbol appear on a surface for 1 hour.]\n\n1st Level Spells:[\nCharm Person: The caster attempts to charm a humanoid they can see within range. The target must make a Wisdom saving throw and does so with advantage if the caster or their companions are fighting it. If it fails the saving throw, it is charmed by the caster until the spell ends or until the caster or their companions do anything harmful to it.\n\nDisguise Self: The caster magically alters their appearance. They can seem 1 foot shorter or taller, thin, fat, or in between. They can't change their body type, so they must adopt a form that has the same basic arrangement of limbs. Otherwise, the extent of the illusion is up to the caster.]\n\n2nd Level Spells:[\nHeat Metal: The caster chooses a manufactured metal object, such as metal armor or a metal weapon that they can see within range, that they can cause to glow red-hot. Any creature in physical contact with the object takes 2d8 fire damage when the spell is cast. Until the spell ends, the caster can use a bonus action on each of their subsequent turns to cause this damage again.\n\nInvisibility: The caster touches a creature and grants it invisibility until the spell ends. Anything the target is wearing or carrying becomes invisible as long as it is on the creature's person. The spell ends for a target that attacks or casts a spell.]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 44\nArmor Class: 13 (Leather Armor + Dexterity Modifier)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nRapier: 1d8 piercing damage plus Dexterity modifier]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nCutting Words: Frequency: Can use a number of times equal to Charisma modifier (4) per short rest. Mechanics: Use Bardic Inspiration to subtract from enemy's roll.\n\nMagical Secrets: Passive ability, based on spell selections from any class's spell list. Mechanics: Gain access to two spells not usually available to bards, bending the weave of magic to suit their whims.\n\nJack of All Trades: Passive ability. Mechanics: Add half proficiency bonus (rounded down) to any ability check that doesn't already include your proficiency bonus.\n\nExpertise: Frequency: Passive ability. Mechanics: Double proficiency bonus for two chosen skills (Deception, Performance).]\n\n</character_sheet_bard>\n\",4,false,62,true,false,true,,4,62,false,true,10,63,90,\"character_sheet_bard\",\"character_sheet_bard\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,63,true,true,false,,\"Githzerai Monk Character Sheet (lawful neutral, level 5)\",false,\"<character_sheet_monk>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\nRace: Githzerai\n\nLevel: 5\n\nClass: Monk (Way of the Ascendant Dragon)\n\nBackground: Hermit\n\nAlignment: Lawful Neutral\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 12 (+1)\nDexterity: 16 (+3)\nConstitution: 15 (+2)\nIntelligence: 14 (+2)\nWisdom: 16 (+3)\nCharisma: 8 (-1)]\n\nSkills: Insight, Religion\n\nEquipment:[\nQuarterstaff\nSimple Robes\nExplorer's Pack\nHerbalism Kit\n50 gold pieces]\n\nFeatures and Traits:\n\nRace: Githzerai: +1 Wisdom, +2 Intelligence, Githzerai Psionics (Shield, Detect Thoughts, Mage Hand), Mental Discipline\nClass: Monk: Unarmored Defense, Martial Arts, Ki, Way of the Ascendant Dragon Features (Draconic Disciple, Breath of the Dragon)\nBackground: Hermit: Discovery\n\n\nKi points:\n5 (equal to Monk level)\n\nKi Attacks:[\nFlurry of Blows: Frequency: Immediately after taking the Attack action on your turn. Mechanics: Spend 1 Ki point to make two additional unarmed strikes as a bonus action.\n\nPatient Defense: Frequency: Can use on your turn. Mechanics: Spend 1 Ki point to take the Dodge action as a bonus action, increasing your chance to avoid an attack.\n\nStep of the Wind: Frequency: Can use on your turn. Mechanics: Spend 1 Ki point to take the Disengage or Dash action as a bonus action, and your jump distance is doubled for the turn.\n\nBreath of the Dragon: Frequency: Twice between short or long rests. Mechanics: Exhale destructive energy in either a 20-foot cone or a 30-foot line (Choice upon use). Choose the damage type based on the dragon type associated with your ki. Costs 2 Ki points.]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nShield: \nFrequency: Once per long rest. \nMechanics: It increases their Armor Class by 5 until the start of their next turn, including against the triggering attack, and they take no damage from magic missile.\n\nDetect Thoughts: \nFrequency: Once per long rest. \nMechanics: When they use Detect Thoughts, they initially learn the surface thoughts of the creature – what is most on its mind in that moment. As an action, they can either shift their attention to another creature's thoughts or attempt to probe deeper into the same creature's mind. If they probe deeper, the target must make a Wisdom saving throw. If it fails, the Githzerai gains insight into its reasoning, its emotional state, and something that looms large in its mind. If it succeeds, the spell ends.\n\nMage Hand: \nFrequency: At will. \nMechanics: The Githzerai can summon a spectral, floating hand at a point they choose within range. The hand lasts for the duration or until it is dismissed as an action. The hand vanishes if it is ever more than 30 feet away from the Githzerai or if it is dismissed. They can use their action to control the hand, manipulating it to manipulate an object, open an unlocked door or container, stow or retrieve an item from an open container, or pour out a vial's contents. The hand can't attack, activate magical items, or carry more than 10 pounds.\n\nMartial Arts: Frequency: Passive ability. Mechanics: Use Dexterity instead of Strength for attack and damage rolls with monk weapons or unarmed strikes.\n\nUnarmored Defense: Passive ability. Mechanics: Add Dexterity and Wisdom modifiers to determine AC when not wearing armor.\n\nDraconic Disciple: Passive ability. Mechanics: Gain the ability to speak Draconic or one other language of your choice, double proficiency bonus for checks related to your chosen dragon type.]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 40\nArmor Class: 16 (Unarmored Defense)\nSpeed: 40 ft.\nAttacks:\nQuarterstaff: 1d8 bludgeoning damage + dexterity modifier\nUnarmed: 1d6 bludgeoning + dexterity modifier]\n</character_sheet_monk>\n\",4,false,63,true,false,true,,4,63,false,true,10,64,90,\"character_sheet_monk\",\"character_sheet_monk\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,64,true,true,false,,\"Dragonborn Necromancer Character Sheet (neutral evil, level 5)\",false,\"<character_sheet_necromancer>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\nRace: Dragonborn (Green Ancestry)\n\nLevel: 5\n\nClass: Necromancer\n\nBackground: Sage\n\nAlignment: Neutral Evil\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 13 (+1)\nDexterity: 10 (+0)\nConstitution: 16 (+3)\nIntelligence: 18 (+4)\nWisdom: 12 (+1)\nCharisma: 14 (+2)]\n\nSkills: Arcana, History\n\nEquipment:[\nQuarterstaff imbued with necrotic essence\nBlack robe adorned with symbols of death and decay\nPotion ingredients, including exotic herbs and venom sacs\nBone amulet pulsating with dark energy\nSpellbook bound in hide of unknown creature\n50 gold pieces]\n\nFeatures and Traits:\n\nRace: Dragonborn: +2 Strength, +1 Charisma, Draconic Ancestry (Green - Poison), Breath Weapon (Poison), Damage Resistance (Poison)\nClass: Necromancer: Spellcasting, Siphon Soul, Army of the Dead\nBackground: Sage: Researcher\n\nSpell slots:\nFour 1st-level spell slots\nThree 2nd-level spell slots\n\nSpellcasting:\nCantrips:[\nChill Touch: A ghostly, skeletal hand appears at a point within range, delivering a touch of death. The target takes 1d8 necrotic damage and can't regain hit points until the start of the necromancer's next turn.\n\nRay of Sickness: A ray of sickening greenish energy lashes out toward a creature within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. If the hit occurs, the target takes 2d8 poison damage and must make a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, it is also poisoned until the end of your next turn.]\n\n1st Level Spells:[\nFear: You awaken the sense of mortality in one creature you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or become frightened of you until the spell ends.\n\nRay of Enfeeblement: A black beam of enervating energy springs from your finger toward a creature within range. On a hit, the target deals only half damage with weapon attacks that use Strength for the duration.]\n\n2nd Level Spells:[\nBlindness/Deafness: You can blind or deafen a foe. Choose one creature that you can see within range to make a Constitution saving throw. If it fails, the target is either blinded or deafened for the duration.\n\nGentle Repose: You touch a corpse or other remains. For the duration, the target is protected from decay and can't become undead.]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nSiphon Soul: Frequency: Passive ability. Mechanics: The necromancer's spells that deal necrotic damage also siphon life energy back to them, regaining hit points equal to half the necrotic damage dealt.\n\nArmy of the Dead: Frequency: Once per long rest. Mechanics: Raise a number of fresh corpses to fight for you until destroyed. One summon per 3 levels up to a maximum of 3 minions.\n\nBreath Weapon (Green Dragon Ancestry - Poison):\nFrequency: Once per short or long rest.\nMechanics: As an action, exhale a 15-foot cone of poisonous gas. Each creature in the area must make a Constitution saving throw, taking 2d6 poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The damage increases to 3d6 at 6th level, 4d6 at 11th level, and 5d6 at 16th level.]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 45 (Max Hit Dice)\nArmor Class: 12 (Robes + Dexterity Modifier)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nNecrotic quarterstaff: 1d8 bludgeoning damage plus 1d6 necrotic damage]\n</character_sheet_necromancer>\n\",4,false,64,true,false,true,,4,64,false,true,10,65,90,\"character_sheet_necromancer\",\"character_sheet_necromancer\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,65,true,true,false,,\"Human Spellblade Character Sheet (chaotic neutral, level 5)\",false,\"<character_sheet_spellblade>\n<notes on current campaign>\n(This section is purely for keeping track of stat, spell, ability and item changes of the current campaign.)\nEquipment:\n\nSpell slots:\n\nSpells:\n\nSpecial abilities:\n\nMisc notes:\n</notes on current campaign>\nRace: Human\n\nLevel: 5\n\nClass: Spellblade (Fighter offshoot)\n\nBackground: Soldier\n\nAlignment: Chaotic Neutral\n\nAttributes:[\nStrength: 16 (+3)\nDexterity: 12 (+1)\nConstitution: 14 (+2)\nIntelligence: 13 (+1)\nWisdom: 10 (+0)\nCharisma: 8 (-1)]\n\nSkills: Athletics, Intimidation\n\nEquipment:[\nOne-Handed Sword\nChain Mail\nSpell Component Pouch\nSoldier's Pack\n50 gold pieces]\n\nFeatures and Traits:\n\nRace: Human: +1 to all attributes\nClass: Spellblade: Spellcasting, Arcane Combatant, One-Handed Casting, Blade Bond, War Magic\nBackground: Soldier: Military Rank, Feature: War Veteran\n\nSpell slots:\nFour 1st-level spell slots\nThree 2nd-level spell slots\n\nSpellcasting:\nCantrips:[\nGreenflame Blade: As part of the action used to cast this spell, you make a melee attack with a weapon against one creature within the spell's range. If the attack hits, the target suffers the weapon attack's normal effects, and green fire envelops the blade. This inferno leaps to a second creature of your choice that you can see within 5 feet of it.\nFirst Target Damage: 1d8 slashing + 1d6 fire damage.\nSecondary Target Damage: 1d4 fire + Strength modifier damage.\n\nShocking Grasp: Lightning springs from your hand to deliver a shock to a creature you try to touch. Make a melee spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 1d8 lightning damage, and it can't take reactions until the start of its next turn.]\n\n1st Level Spells:[\nMagic Missile:\nAt 1st level, you create three glowing darts of magical force. Each dart hits a creature of your choice that you can see within range. A dart deals 1d4 + 1 force damage to its target. The number of darts increases by one for every two spell levels above the first.\nSpell Damage: 1d4 + 1 force damage per dart.\nScaling:\nAt 5th level (3rd spell slot), it creates five darts.\nAt 7th level (4th spell slot), it creates six darts, and so on.\n\nShield: An invisible barrier of magical force appears and protects you until the start of your next turn. You have a +5 bonus to AC, including against the triggering attack, and you take no damage from magic missile.]\n\n2nd Level Spells:[\nBlur: Your body becomes blurred, shifting and wavering to all who can see you. For the duration, any creature has disadvantage on attack rolls against you.\n\nScorching Ray: You create three rays of fire and hurl them at targets within range. You can hurl them at one target or several. Make a ranged spell attack for each ray. On a hit, the target takes 2d6 fire damage.]\n\nSpecial Abilities:[\nArcane Combatant: Frequency: When you cast a cantrip. Mechanics: Perform a special melee attack as a bonus action. The melee attack deals an extra 1d8 damage of the cantrip's damage type.\n\nBlade Bond: Frequency: Any time when you don't have your weapon. Mechanics: Bond with one weapon at a time; can summon it to your hand as long as it's on the same plane of existence.\n\nWar Magic: Passive Ability: After casting a spell, the Spellblade gains a +2 bonus to AC until the start of their next turn. ]\n\nCombat Stats:[\nHit Points: 50\nArmor Class: 16 (Chain Mail)\nSpeed: 30 ft.\nAttacks:\nOne-Handed Sword: 1d8 +3 slashing damage]\n</character_sheet_spellblade>\n\",4,false,65,true,false,true,,4,65,false,true,10,66,90,\"character_sheet_spellblade\",\"character_sheet_spellblade\",\"\",90,1,10,100,true,0,66,true,true,false,,\"Magic Items - Cloaks\",false,\"[System Command: From the list below, award an item that is usable by the player.]\n\nWraithweave Cloak:[\n\nDescription: This ethereal cloak is made from the shadowy tendrils of wraiths and imbued with the essence of the Shadowfell. It billows and shifts like smoke, concealing the wearer from sight and granting protection against undead foes.\nStats Change: Wraithweave Cloak grants the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects cast by undead creatures, as well as resistance to necrotic damage.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier (max 2)]\n\nCloak of the Shadowcaster:[\n\nDescription: This dark cloak is infused with the essence of the Shadowfell, granting its wearer mastery over shadows and darkness. It billows ominously and seems to absorb light around it.\nStats Change: While wearing this cloak, the wearer gains advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks and can use an action to cast the darkness spell once per day.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nlllusionist's Cloak:[\n\nDescription: This shimmering cloak is woven from threads of illusion magic, creating mesmerizing patterns and optical illusions. It allows its wearer to manipulate perception and deceive the senses.\nStats Change: Illusionist's Cloak grants the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that cause charm or fear, as well as resistance to psychic damage.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nConjurer's Cloak:[\n\nDescription: This voluminous cloak is adorned with arcane symbols and infused with the power of conjuration magic. It allows its wearer to summon creatures and objects from other planes of existence.\nStats Change: Conjurer's Cloak grants the wearer advantage on saving throws against spells and effects that cause sleep or unconsciousness, as well as resistance to force damage.\nArmor Class: 11 + Dexterity modifier]\n\nCloak of Many Colors:[\n\nDescription: This vibrant cloak shimmers with iridescent hues, constantly shifting and changing colors. It grants the wearer a sense of whimsy and wonder, boosting their charisma in social situations.\nEffect: Grants a +2 bonus to Charisma checks and allows the wearer to cast the prestidigitation cantrip once per day.]\n\nCloak of Billowing:[\n\nDescription: This dramatic cloak billows and flutters dramatically, even in the absence of wind. It enhances the wearer's presence and charisma, making them appear more imposing and heroic.\nEffect: Grants advantage on Charisma (Intimidation) checks and allows the wearer to cast the gust cantrip at will to enhance the billowing effect.]\n\nCloak of Invisibility (to the Wearer):[\n\nDescription: This cloak renders the wearer completely invisible to themselves, granting them the ability to observe their surroundings without being seen. It offers a unique perspective on the world.\nEffect: Grants the wearer the ability to become invisible to themselves at will, but they remain visible to others.]\n\nCloak of the Reaper's Embrace:[\nDescription: Woven from the death shroud of those who perished in agony, this cloak thrums with their unresolved fury. Its chilling touch seems to leech the warmth from the air, leaving a rime of frost wherever it lingers.\nStats Change: Grants the wearer a +1 bonus to all necrotic damage spells per undead minion under their control. Additionally, whenever the wearer is struck in melee, the attacker must make a Constitution saving throw or be cursed with a chilling malaise that saps their strength, imposing disadvantage on their next attack roll.]\n\nCloak of the Sanguine Ritual:[\nDescription: Drenched in the vestiges of blood magic rituals, this dark red cloak feels surprisingly heavy on the shoulders. It's as if the weight of lives taken in sacrifice lends power to its bearer.\nStats Change: The wearer can channel their own life force or that of others into bolstered power. As an action, they can choose to sacrifice hit points to add an equivalent amount to their next spell's damage (up to a maximum of 20 hit points), or transfer hit points to heal an undead minion or willing creature within touch.]\n\nCloak of the Healer:[\nDescription: Woven from purest white silk, embroidered with ancient symbols of life and vitality, this cloak seems to pulse with a soothing rhythm.\nEffect: Healers wearing this cloak add a +2 bonus to all healing spell effects. Once per long rest, the wearer can cast 'mass cure wounds' at its base level without expending a spell slot.]\n\nCloak of the Iron Vanguard:[\nDescription: This heavy cloak is reinforced with interlaced iron threads, its surface charred like the aftermath of a great battle.\nEffect: When a melee fighter dons this cloak, they gain damage reduction of 3 from all non-magical slashing, bludgeoning, and piercing attacks. Additionally, they gain an intimidation bonus equivalent to their Constitution modifier.]\n\nCloak of the Sharpshooter:[\nDescription: Crafted from a fabric as dark as a moonless night, this cloak aids ranged fighters in blending into the shadows.\nEffect: Grants advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks for ranged fighters lying in wait. When attacking from stealth, their first hit deals an extra 2d6 damage.]\n\nCloak of Sanguine Shadows:[\nDescription: Dyed with the blood of the fallen, this cloak is said to grant the favor of shadowy patrons to those who walk the path of vengeance.\nEffect: Once per day, the wearer can phase through solid objects for a short burst – up to 10 feet – as if a ghost seeking retribution. When emerging from the phase, their first melee attack is made with advantage.]\n\nBoozemancer's Mantle:[\nDescription: A cloak saturated with the essence of myriad ales and wines, known to ferment enchantments as well as it does drinks.\nEffect: Grants immunity to poison and advantage on saving throws against spells that alter consciousness, such as sleep or charm. The Boozemancer can tap into the cloak to regain one expended spell slot up to level 3 once per day.]\n\nSpellblade's Veil:[\nDescription: Adorned with runic patterns, this cloak crackles with latent magic, ready to augment the Spellblade's enchanted weaponry.\nEffect: Increases elemental damage (fire, cold, lightning) dealt by weapons by 1d4. Allows the wearer to, once per short rest, cast a shield spell as a reaction without expending a spell slot, reflecting the Spellblade's synergy with their magical defenses.]\n\nInquisitor's Drape:[\nDescription: Wrought from sacred fabrics and stitched with sigils of judgment, this cloak serves as both armor and a badge of authority.\nEffect: Grants an aura of command, giving the Inquisitor advantage on Intimidation checks. It also provides resistance to damage from fiends and advantage on saving throws against effects from any creature with an alignment directly opposite of the Inquisitor's.]\n\nBastion's Embrace:[\nDescription: A cloak forged from dragonhide and tempered in the blood of heroes. Its surface is scarred from countless battles.\nEffect: The wearer gains damage reduction of 5 from all non-magical attacks and gains advantage on saving throws against being frightened or knocked prone.]\n\nRogue's Shroud:[\nDescription: As dark as a moonless night, this cloak aids its wearer in eluding capture and silencing their footsteps.\nEffect: Grants a +5 bonus to Dexterity (Stealth) checks and allows the wearer to become hidden as a bonus action once per short rest.]\n\nDruid's Wrap:[\nDescription: Woven from the living vines and flowers of the sacred grove, this cloak is always in bloom, exuding the scent of wild nature.\nEffect: The wearer gains the ability to speak with plants at will and can cast 'entangle' as a bonus action once per day.]\n\nCloak of the Blighted Swarm:[\nDescription: Swarming with insects from cursed swamps, this cloak appears to be alive, buzzing with malevolent intent.\nEffect: The wearer can release a swarm to attack, once per day, dealing 1d8 poison damage to anyone within 5 feet. ]\n\",4,false,72,true,false,true,,4,72,false,true,10,67,78,\"magic cape\",\"Magic mantle\",\"Arcane shroud\",\"Enchanted garment\",\"Wizard's cloak\",\"Magical wrap\",\"Magic capelet\",\"magic cloak\",\"Astral cloak\",\"Enchanted shawl\",\"Enchanted stole\",\"Sorcerous cape\",\"Mystic cloak\",\"magic_cloak\",\"Sorcerer's cloak\",\"Magical drapery\",\"Charmed cloak\",\"Enchanted cloak\",\"Spellbound cape\",\"Magic veil\",\"Ethereal cloak\",\"Mystical cape\",\"magic cape\",\"Magic mantle\",\"Arcane shroud\",\"Enchanted garment\",\"Wizard's cloak\",\"Magical wrap\",\"Magic capelet\",\"magic cloak\",\"Astral cloak\",\"Enchanted shawl\",\"Enchanted stole\",\"Sorcerous cape\",\"Mystic cloak\",\"magic_cloak\",\"Sorcerer's cloak\",\"Magical drapery\",\"Charmed cloak\",\"Enchanted cloak\",\"Spellbound cape\",\"Magic veil\",\"Ethereal cloak\",\"Mystical cape\",\"\",78,1,10,100,true,0,67,true,true,false,,\"Loot - Boss\",false,\"[System Command: Loot from the table below is only awarded to level 5 or higher, and only upon epic creature or boss kills.]\n\n<item_loot>\n{{user}} is rewarded a unique item that fits their class and/or skills. Dungeon master chooses from: {{random: unique_melee, unique_ranged, unique_staff, unique_trinkets, unique_shield, unique_armor, unique_cloth, unique_jewelry}}\n</item_loot>\",4,false,73,true,true,true,,4,73,true,true,10,68,100,\"archvillain\",\"overlord\",\"epic kill\",\"boss\",\"epic loot\",\"epic rewards\",\"master loot\",\"archvillain\",\"overlord\",\"epic kill\",\"boss\",\"epic loot\",\"epic rewards\",\"master loot\",\"\",100,1,10,100,true,0,68,true,false,\"\",false,50,500",
