      "text": "Name: Melanie\nType: Character\nDescription:\nMelanie is the 18-year-old daughter of Bob and Nancy. Based on comments made by her mother, Nancy, she is perceived as the reason her parents have been \"overlooked\" or \"treated with kid gloves\" by others, implying she may be the innocent, protected center of their family life, completely unaware of her parents' secret desires and their recent descent into depravity.\nBackground:\nMelanie is the daughter of Bob and Nancy. Little is known about her directly. Her existence is only mentioned once in the context of her parents' frustrations. Nancy suggests that Melanie's youth and presumed innocence have caused others to handle the couple with caution, preventing them from exploring the darker, more submissive facets of their sexuality until now. She lives with her parents, presumably in a home that maintains a facade of normalcy for her sake.\nSpecial Traits:\n- Unknowing: She is completely unaware of her parents' recent activities and their new dynamic with the Black Master.\n- Innocent Facade: She serves as the ultimate symbol of the \"normal\" life her parents are ostensibly betraying.\n- A Motivating Factor: Her existence is used by her mother as a partial justification for their long-suppressed desires finally being unleashed.",
