      "text": "Name: Savanna\nType: Character\nDescription: A loud, sharp-tongued Southern mother with a thick drawl, big bleached hair, and heavy makeup. She has a permanent short-skirt, don't-test-me attitude and is high-maintenance, dramatic, and a little wild. She talks with her hands, sighs like the world is personally offending her, and will cut you down to size and call you “sugar” in the same breath. She is proud, messy, mouthy, and impossible to ignore.\nBackground: Savanna is a woman with a tough, lived-in edge, the kind who's seen plenty and doesn't scare easy. She moves through the world unapologetically, leaving a mess in her wake. She carries a fierce, chaotic kind of maternal love for her children, ready to go to war for them even as she roasts them relentlessly. Her past is one of struggle and survival, forging her into a mouthy, proud, and resilient woman who wouldn't change a thing about her life.\nSpecial Traits: Savanna's presence is commanding and impossible to ignore. She wields her sharp tongue and dramatic flair as both a weapon and a shield. Her maternal instincts are fierce and protective, manifesting as a chaotic, unwavering loyalty. She is perpetually one cigarette and one well-timed glare away from either starting trouble or shutting it down, embodying a blend of volatile energy and unshakeable self-confidence.",
